window.BOOK = {"chapters":[{"chapter":1,"names":[{"translit":"Allaah","arabic":"اللَّه","meaning":"Allaah"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"'Allaah' is a magnificent Name from the Beautiful Names of Allaah. The Name Allaah occurs the most in the Qur'aan out of all the other names at over 1200 times which no other name does and it begins 33 aayaat."},{"type":"p","text":"Some of the people of knowledge hold that 'Allaah' is Allaah's greatest Name, that if He is called upon with it He answers and if He is asked with it He gives."},{"type":"p","text":"This Name has special characteristics which is specific to it. One of which is that it is the foundation for all the Beautiful Names of Allaah and all the Names are under it."},{"type":"quote","text":"And (all) the Most Beautiful Names belong to Allah, so call on Him by them,","ref":"Suratul 'Araaf 7:180"},{"type":"p","text":"The Name 'Allaah' carries the meanings of all the Beautiful Names, it refers to them in general and the Beautiful Names are the details. It clarifies the Divine Attributes which are Perfect, Majestic and Mighty Attributes. 'Allaah' is the Name that all the others refer back to and it encompasses all their meanings."},{"type":"p","text":"The most concise and best saying about the meaning of 'Allaah' is what is narrated by Ibn 'Abbaas when he said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allaah -- the One who has the right to be taken as a deity and worshipped by the whole of creation.","ref":"Ibn Jareer in his Tafseer (Tabaree 1/121)"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that Allaah with these Attributes of Majesty, Perfection and Might deserves to be worshipped and singled out alone with humility, humbleness and submission."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Allaah occurs the most in the Qur'aan, over 1200 times, and it begins 33 aayaat.","Some of the people of knowledge hold that 'Allaah' is Allaah's greatest Name: if He is called upon with it He answers, and if asked with it He gives.","It is the foundation of all the Beautiful Names; all the Names are under it and refer back to it.","It carries the meanings of all the Beautiful Names in general, while the other Names are the details.","Ibn 'Abbaas explained it as: the One who has the right to be taken as a deity and worshipped by the whole of creation.","Allaah, with His Attributes of Majesty, Perfection and Might, deserves to be worshipped and singled out alone with humility, humbleness and submission."],"evidence":[{"text":"And (all) the Most Beautiful Names belong to Allah, so call on Him by them.","ref":"Suratul 'Araaf 7:180"},{"text":"Ibn 'Abbaas: \"Allaah -- the One who has the right to be taken as a deity and worshipped by the whole of creation.\"","ref":"Ibn Jareer in his Tafseer (Tabaree 1/121)"}],"recall":[{"q":"What is the meaning of the Name 'Allaah' according to Ibn 'Abbaas?","a":"The One who has the right to be taken as a deity and worshipped by the whole of creation."},{"q":"How many times does the Name Allaah occur in the Qur'aan, and how many aayaat does it begin?","a":"Over 1200 times, more than any other name, and it begins 33 aayaat."},{"q":"What is the relationship between the Name 'Allaah' and the other Beautiful Names?","a":"It is the foundation of all the Names; it carries their meanings in general and the other Names are the details. All the Names refer back to it."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite to show that all the Beautiful Names belong to Allaah?","a":"\"And (all) the Most Beautiful Names belong to Allah, so call on Him by them\" [Suratul 'Araaf 7:180]."}]},{"chapter":2,"names":[{"translit":"Ar-Rabb","arabic":"الرَّبّ","meaning":"The Lord"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ar-Rabb The Lord is a tremendous Name of Allaah, the Mighty and Exalted. It occurs over 500 times in the Noble Qur'aan in many situations and various contexts. Allaah the Exalted said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"All the praises and thanks be to Allah, the Lord of the 'Alamin.","ref":"Faatihah 1:2"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"Verily, my Salat (prayer), my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the 'Alamin (mankind, jinns and all that exists).","ref":"An'aam 6:162"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Ar-Rabb the Lord is: possessing Lordship over all of His creation in terms of creation, kingdom, disposing of the affairs and managing them. It comes from the Names which encompass many meanings and not just one."},{"type":"p","text":"In fact, if this Name is mentioned alone it encompasses the meanings of all of Allaah's Beautiful Names and Lofty Attributes. Regarding this Ibnul Qayyim said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Indeed ar Rabb the Lord is al Qaadir The Fully-Able, al Khaaliq The Creator, al Baari' The Originator, al Musawwir The Bestower of Forms, al Hayy The Living, al Qayyoom The Self-Subsisting, al 'Aleem The All-Knowing, as Samee' The All-Hearing, al Baseer The All-Seeing, al Muhsin The One whose actions are all perfect and good, al Mun'im The Bestower of Blessings, al Jawaad The Most Generous, al Mu'tee The Giver, al Maani' The Preventer, ad Daar an Naafi' The One who harms and benefits, al Muqaddim al Mu'akhkhir The One who gives precedence and The One who puts back. The One who leaves whoever He wills to go astray. The One who guides whomever He wills. The One who makes whoever He wills happy, sad, raises, lowers and many more besides this of the meanings of Lordship which come from it with what the Beautiful Names deserve.","ref":"Badaa'i al Fawaaid by Imaam Ibnul Qayyim 2/212"}],"keyPoints":["Ar-Rabb occurs over 500 times in the Noble Qur'aan in many situations and various contexts.","Ar-Rabb means possessing Lordship over all of His creation in terms of creation, kingdom, disposing of the affairs and managing them.","It is one of the Names which encompass many meanings and not just one.","If mentioned alone, it encompasses the meanings of all of Allaah's Beautiful Names and Lofty Attributes.","Ibnul Qayyim explained that ar-Rabb is al-Qaadir, al-Khaaliq, al-Baari', al-Musawwir, al-Hayy, al-Qayyoom and many more of the meanings of Lordship."],"evidence":[{"text":"All the praises and thanks be to Allah, the Lord of the 'Alamin.","ref":"Faatihah 1:2"},{"text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"Verily, my Salat (prayer), my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the 'Alamin.\"","ref":"An'aam 6:162"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ar-Rabb (The Lord) mean?","a":"Possessing Lordship over all of His creation in terms of creation, kingdom, disposing of the affairs and managing them."},{"q":"How many times does Ar-Rabb occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"Over 500 times, in many situations and various contexts."},{"q":"What does the Name Ar-Rabb encompass when it is mentioned alone?","a":"The meanings of all of Allaah's Beautiful Names and Lofty Attributes."},{"q":"Which scholar does the author quote listing the Names included in ar-Rabb, and from which book?","a":"Ibnul Qayyim, in Badaa'i al Fawaaid (2/212)."}]},{"chapter":3,"names":[{"translit":"Ar-Rahmaan","arabic":"الرَّحْمَٰن","meaning":"The Most Merciful"},{"translit":"Ar-Raheem","arabic":"الرَّحِيم","meaning":"The Bestower of Mercy"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Names Ar-Rahmaan and Ar-Raheem are two honourable Names which occur numerous times in the Qur'aan. Allaah began Umm al Qur'aan (Sooratul Faatihah) with them, they were made a sign of what Allaah revealed of guidance and clarification. Within them is a speech which the shaytaan cannot take hold of. The Prophet of Allaah Sulaymaan started his letter with them and Jibreel came down with them at the start of every Soorah of the Qur'aan revealing them to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. These two Names both indicate that mercy is an Attribute of Allaah."},{"type":"p","text":"Ar-Rahmaan means being described as having mercy. Ar-Raheem means bestowing mercy upon His servants. These two Names indicate perfect and complete mercy which is Allaah's Attribute and description."},{"type":"p","text":"In these two Names is a proof of Allaah's perfect mercy which is an all-encompassing Attribute of His. Everything in the higher and lower worlds (the heavens and the earth) that happens such as gaining benefits, liked enjoyable things and good things are from the effects of Allaah's Mercy. Just as what is diverted from them of hateful things: tests, frightening incidents, dangers and harms are from the effects of His Mercy. Good deeds only come from Him and only He can deflect bad deeds and He is the Most Merciful of those who have mercy."}],"keyPoints":["Ar-Rahmaan means being described as having mercy.","Ar-Raheem means bestowing mercy upon His servants.","Both Names indicate that mercy is an Attribute of Allaah, and that His mercy is perfect, complete and all-encompassing.","Allaah began Sooratul Faatihah with them, Sulaymaan started his letter with them, and Jibreel came down with them at the start of every Soorah.","All benefits and good things in the heavens and the earth, and the diverting of tests, dangers and harms, are from the effects of Allaah's Mercy."],"evidence":[],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ar-Rahmaan mean?","a":"Being described as having mercy."},{"q":"What does Ar-Raheem mean?","a":"Bestowing mercy upon His servants."},{"q":"Which Prophet started his letter with these two Names?","a":"The Prophet of Allaah Sulaymaan."},{"q":"According to the author, what are the effects of Allaah's Mercy in the heavens and the earth?","a":"Gaining benefits, liked enjoyable things and good things, as well as the diverting of hateful things such as tests, frightening incidents, dangers and harms."}]},{"chapter":4,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Hayy","arabic":"الحَيّ","meaning":"The Ever-Living"},{"translit":"Al-Qayyoom","arabic":"القَيُّوم","meaning":"The Self-Subsisting Sustainer"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Hayy Al-Qayyoom - The Ever-Living The Self-Subsisting Sustainer of all the creation are two Names that come together in the Qur'aan in three places. The first occurrence is in Aayatul Kursee:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah! La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists.","ref":"Baqarah 2:255"},{"type":"p","text":"The second occurrence is at the beginning of Soorah Aali 'Imraan:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah! La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:2"},{"type":"p","text":"The third is in Soorah Taahaa:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And (all) faces shall be humbled before (Allah), the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists.","ref":"Taahaa 20:111"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah the Blessed and Exalted's Name al Hayy The Ever-Living contains an affirmation of Allaah's Attribute of Living. It is a complete Life not preceded by non-existence nor followed by it being taken away or ending. Allaah is Living without deficiency or defect and our Lord is Exalted and free from that."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name al Qayyoom contains affirmation of His Attribute of Self-Subsistence. It being that Allaah is Self-Subsisting and sustains His creation."},{"type":"p","text":"These two Names al Hayy and al Qayyoom both encompass the meanings of Allaah's Beautiful Names where all the Attributes of the Creator return back. The Attributes of Allaah's Self such as hearing, seeing, His Hand, Knowledge and so on return back to His Name al Hayy The Ever-Living. The Attributes of Allaah that are actions such as creation, providing, bestowing blessings, giving life, giving death and so on return back to His Name al Qayyoom. Due to this, the People of Knowledge have said that they are Allaah's greatest Names which if He is called on by them He answers and if He is asked by them He gives."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Hayy and Al-Qayyoom come together in the Qur'aan in three places: Aayatul Kursee (2:255), the beginning of Aali 'Imraan (3:2) and Taahaa (20:111).","Al-Hayy affirms Allaah's Attribute of Life: a complete Life not preceded by non-existence nor followed by ending, without deficiency or defect.","Al-Qayyoom affirms His Attribute of Self-Subsistence: He is Self-Subsisting and sustains His creation.","The Attributes of Allaah's Self (hearing, seeing, His Hand, Knowledge) return back to al-Hayy.","The Attributes of action (creation, providing, bestowing blessings, giving life and death) return back to al-Qayyoom.","The People of Knowledge have said they are Allaah's greatest Names: if He is called on by them He answers and if asked by them He gives."],"evidence":[{"text":"Allah! La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists.","ref":"Baqarah 2:255"},{"text":"And (all) faces shall be humbled before (Allah), the Ever Living, the One Who sustains and protects all that exists.","ref":"Taahaa 20:111"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Hayy mean and what does it affirm?","a":"The Ever-Living; it affirms Allaah's Attribute of Life, a complete Life not preceded by non-existence nor followed by it being taken away or ending."},{"q":"What does Al-Qayyoom mean?","a":"The Self-Subsisting Sustainer; it affirms His Attribute of Self-Subsistence, that He is Self-Subsisting and sustains His creation."},{"q":"In which three places do Al-Hayy and Al-Qayyoom come together in the Qur'aan?","a":"Aayatul Kursee (Baqarah 2:255), the beginning of Aali 'Imraan (3:2), and Taahaa (20:111)."},{"q":"Which Attributes return back to al-Hayy and which to al-Qayyoom?","a":"Attributes of Allaah's Self (hearing, seeing, His Hand, Knowledge) return to al-Hayy; Attributes of action (creation, providing, bestowing blessings, giving life and death) return to al-Qayyoom."}]},{"chapter":5,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Khaaliq","arabic":"الخَالِق","meaning":"The Creator"},{"translit":"Al-Khallaaq","arabic":"الخَلَّاق","meaning":"The Ever-Creating"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The name of Allaah al Khaaliq is found in many places in the Qur'aan. For example:"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah, the Creator, the Inventor of all things, the Bestower of forms.","ref":"Hashr 59:24"},{"type":"p","text":"Al Khallaaq in the intensive form occurs in two places in the Qur'aan in the Sayings of Allaah the Exalted:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, your Lord is the All-Knowing Creator.","ref":"Hijr 15:86"},{"type":"quote","text":"Yes, indeed! He is the All-Knowing Supreme Creator.","ref":"Yaseen 36:81"},{"type":"p","text":"Creation (al Khalq) refers to and means two matters:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. The first meaning of al Khalq is bringing something new into existence from nothing:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Do they not see that We have created for them of what Our Hands have created, the cattle, so that they are their owners.","ref":"Yaseen 36:71"},{"type":"p","text":"2. The second meaning of al khalq is 'measuring/preparing/inventing' (in Arabic: taqdeer). They used to say 'he (khalaqa) the skins' which means he prepared it. Allaah's Saying:"},{"type":"quote","text":"and you only invent (takhluqoon) falsehood.","ref":"Al Ankaboot 29:17"},{"type":"p","text":"Which means that you invent it and make people inclined to it."},{"type":"p","text":"So 'creating' (al khalq) when used to describe the actions of humans means taqdeer 'preparing or inventing'. As for 'creation' which carries the meaning of inventing and bringing into existence from nothing, then this is only for the Lord of all that exists. As Allaah the Exalted said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Is there any creator other than Allah!","ref":"Faatir 35:3"},{"type":"quote","text":"This is the creation of Allah. So show Me that which those (whom you worship), besides Him have created. Nay, the Zalimun (polytheists, wrong-doers and those who do not believe in the Oneness of Allah) are in plain error.","ref":"Luqmaan 31:11"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah did not create the creation without purpose, in vain or for fun. Allaah is far removed and purified from that. Indeed Allaah created them to worship Him and single Him out alone. Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Did you think that We had created you in play (without any purpose), and that you would not be brought back to Us? So Exalted is Allah, the True King, La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Lord of the Supreme Throne!","ref":"Al Mu'minoon 23:115-116"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Khaaliq is found in many places in the Qur'aan; Al-Khallaaq, the intensive form, occurs in two places (Hijr 15:86 and Yaseen 36:81).","The first meaning of al-khalq is bringing something new into existence from nothing.","The second meaning of al-khalq is taqdeer: measuring, preparing or inventing.","When used for humans, 'creating' only means taqdeer; creation in the sense of bringing into existence from nothing is only for the Lord of all that exists.","Allaah did not create the creation without purpose, in vain or for fun; He created them to worship Him and single Him out alone."],"evidence":[{"text":"He is Allah, the Creator, the Inventor of all things, the Bestower of forms.","ref":"Hashr 59:24"},{"text":"Verily, your Lord is the All-Knowing Creator.","ref":"Hijr 15:86"},{"text":"Is there any creator other than Allah!","ref":"Faatir 35:3"}],"recall":[{"q":"What are the two meanings of creation (al-khalq) given by the author?","a":"1) Bringing something new into existence from nothing; 2) measuring/preparing/inventing (taqdeer)."},{"q":"What is the difference between Al-Khaaliq and Al-Khallaaq?","a":"Al-Khaaliq (The Creator) is the normal form; Al-Khallaaq (The Ever-Creating) is the intensive form, which occurs in two places in the Qur'aan."},{"q":"In which two places does Al-Khallaaq occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"Hijr 15:86 (\"Verily, your Lord is the All-Knowing Creator\") and Yaseen 36:81."},{"q":"What does 'creating' mean when used to describe the actions of humans?","a":"Taqdeer, 'preparing or inventing'; creating from nothing is only for the Lord of all that exists."},{"q":"Why did Allaah create the creation?","a":"To worship Him and single Him out alone; He did not create them without purpose, in vain or for fun (Al Mu'minoon 23:115-116)."}]},{"chapter":6,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Khaaliq","arabic":"الخَالِق","meaning":"The Creator"},{"translit":"Al-Baari'","arabic":"البَارِئ","meaning":"The Originator"},{"translit":"Al-Musawwir","arabic":"المُصَوِّر","meaning":"The Fashioner"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah combined these three Names in His Saying:"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah, the Creator, the Inventor of all things, the Bestower of forms. To Him belong the Best Names.","ref":"Hashr 59:24"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that He alone created the whole of creation; He invented all the inventions and bestowed the forms through His precise execution and perfected His creation of all beings. He created them, bestowed their forms and brought them forth at a suitable time for them. He measured His creation with the best of measuring and made them with the most precise making. He guided them for their benefit and gave everything a character suitable to it. Then He guided every creation to what it was fashioned and created for."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Khaaliq The Creator gives measure to things according to His wisdom. Al-Baari' the Originator brings it into being after being nothing. Al Musawwir The Fashioner fashions the creation and created beings however He wills."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibnul Qayyim says:"},{"type":"quote","text":"So Al-Baari', al Musawwir are details to the meaning of the Name al Khaaliq. So Allaah, if He wants to create something He measures it with His Knowledge and wisdom, then He makes it - meaning He brings it into existence according to what He measured and decreed in the form that He wished and wanted.","ref":"Shifaa al 'Aleel 1/366"},{"type":"p","text":"So these three Names in the aayah are in order: creation first - and that is decreeing and measuring the existence of the creation, then making it - which is bringing it into existence from non-existence, then He made it into a shape and form that He Willed."}],"keyPoints":["Allaah combined these three Names in Hashr 59:24.","Al-Khaaliq The Creator gives measure to things according to His wisdom.","Al-Baari' The Originator brings it into being after being nothing.","Al-Musawwir The Fashioner fashions the creation and created beings however He wills.","Ibnul Qayyim said Al-Baari' and Al-Musawwir are details of the meaning of al-Khaaliq.","The three Names are in order: decreeing and measuring, then bringing into existence from non-existence, then giving shape and form."],"evidence":[{"text":"He is Allah, the Creator, the Inventor of all things, the Bestower of forms. To Him belong the Best Names.","ref":"Hashr 59:24"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Khaaliq (The Creator) do, as explained in this chapter?","a":"He gives measure to things according to His wisdom."},{"q":"What does Al-Baari' (The Originator) mean?","a":"He brings it into being after being nothing."},{"q":"What does Al-Musawwir (The Fashioner) mean?","a":"He fashions the creation and created beings however He wills."},{"q":"Which aayah combines these three Names?","a":"\"He is Allah, the Creator, the Inventor of all things, the Bestower of forms. To Him belong the Best Names.\" [Hashr 59:24]"},{"q":"In what order do these three Names come, according to the author?","a":"Creation first (decreeing and measuring), then making (bringing into existence from non-existence), then giving it the shape and form He Willed."}]},{"chapter":7,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Malik","arabic":"المَلِك","meaning":"The King"},{"translit":"Al-Maleek","arabic":"المَلِيك","meaning":"The Supreme Sovereign"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Malik The King is found in the Noble Qur'aan in five places. One of which is where Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah beside Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Maleek The Supreme Sovereign is found once in Allaah's Saying:"},{"type":"quote","text":"In a seat of truth (i.e. Paradise), near the Omnipotent King (Allah, the One, the All-Blessed, the Most High, the Owner of Majesty and Honour).","ref":"Qamar 54:55"},{"type":"p","text":"These two Names indicate that Allaah possesses the Kingdom. This means the King of everything, the One Who can dispose of it without being prevented or having any obstacles. It is repeated many times in the Noble Qur'aan that Allaah alone possesses the Kingdom without partner. This is a clear proof of the obligation to single Him out alone for worship."},{"type":"quote","text":"Such is Allah your Lord. His is the kingdom, La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He). How then are you turned away?","ref":"Zumar 39:6"},{"type":"p","text":"Worshipping other than Allaah, when they do not possess the ability to harm, benefit, give life or death or resurrect is complete going astray and complete falsehood. Many aayaat in the Qur'aan has this meaning and explains this matter clearly. As Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Such is Allah your Lord; His is the kingdom. And those, whom you invoke or call upon instead of Him, own not even a Qitmir (the thin membrane over the datestone).","ref":"Faatir 35:13"},{"type":"quote","text":"Yet they have taken besides Him other aaliha (gods) that created nothing but are themselves created, and possess neither hurt nor benefit for themselves, and possess no power (of causing) death, nor (of giving) life, nor of raising the dead.","ref":"Furqaan 25:3"},{"type":"p","text":"It is not allowed to divert a portion of worship to anyone. Whoever does not own anything in this universe, not even the weight of a seed (should not be worshipped). Worship is the right of the Mighty King the Exalted Creator and the Lord Who manages the affairs of this universe. He has no partner, Exalted be His affair and Mighty is His Authority. High and Exalted is His Majesty there is nothing worthy of worship except Him."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Malik The King is found in the Qur'aan in five places, such as Hashr 59:23.","Al-Maleek The Supreme Sovereign is found once, in Qamar 54:55.","Both Names indicate that Allaah possesses the Kingdom: He is the King of everything, disposing of it without being prevented or having any obstacles.","Allaah alone possessing the Kingdom without partner is a clear proof of the obligation to single Him out alone for worship.","Worshipping others who cannot harm, benefit, give life or death or resurrect is complete going astray and falsehood; no portion of worship may be diverted to anyone else."],"evidence":[{"text":"He is Allah beside Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"text":"In a seat of truth (i.e. Paradise), near the Omnipotent King.","ref":"Qamar 54:55"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do the Names Al-Malik and Al-Maleek indicate?","a":"That Allaah possesses the Kingdom: He is the King of everything, the One Who can dispose of it without being prevented or having any obstacles."},{"q":"What does Al-Maleek mean, and how many times is it found in the Qur'aan?","a":"The Supreme Sovereign; it is found once, in Qamar 54:55."},{"q":"How many times is Al-Malik (The King) found in the Qur'aan?","a":"In five places, one of which is Hashr 59:23."},{"q":"What does Allaah alone possessing the Kingdom prove, according to the author?","a":"It is a clear proof of the obligation to single Him out alone for worship."}]},{"chapter":8,"names":[{"translit":"Ar-Razzaaq","arabic":"الرَّزَّاق","meaning":"The Great Provider"},{"translit":"Ar-Raaziq","arabic":"الرَّازِق","meaning":"The Best of Sustainers"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Ar-Razzaaq The Great Provider is found in one place in the Qur'aan. Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.","ref":"Dhaariyaat 51:58"},{"type":"p","text":"The name ar Raaziq The All-Provider occurs in the plural form in places of the Qur'aan such as Allaah's Saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is the Best of providers.","ref":"Jumu'ah 62:11"},{"type":"p","text":"It is also found in the Sunnah as will come in (the explanation of the Names) Al-Qaabid Al-Baasit The Withholder The Granter of Extensive Provision."},{"type":"p","text":"So Allaah, the far removed from every imperfection, is ar Razzaaq The Great Provider. This means that He takes care of the servants' provisions and is the One Who is in charge over every person's requirements regarding provision. Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And no (moving) living creature is there on earth but its provision is due from Allah.","ref":"Hood 11:6"},{"type":"quote","text":"And so many a moving (living) creature there is, that carries not its own provision! Allah provides for it and for you.","ref":"Ankaboot 29:60"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Provision for His servants is of two types (general and specific):"},{"type":"p","text":"General provision which encompasses the righteous people and the bad, the believer and the disbeliever, the first and the last. This is provision for the body:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And no (moving) living creature is there on earth but its provision is due from Allah.","ref":"Hood 11:6"},{"type":"p","text":"Extensive provision in the worldly life is not a proof of a servant's nobility in Allaah's Sight. Just the same as restricted provision is not a proof that the servant is insignificant in Allaah's Sight."},{"type":"quote","text":"As for man, when his Lord tries him by giving him honour and gifts, then he says (puffed up): \"My Lord has honoured me.\" But when He tries him, by straitening his means of life, he says: \"My Lord has humiliated me!\" Nay! But you treat not the orphans with kindness and generosity (i.e. you neither treat them well, nor give them their exact right of inheritance)!","ref":"Fajr 89:15-17"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that not everyone whom Allaah has blessed in the world is honoured in His Sight and not everyone who has restricted means is humiliated in Allaah's Sight. Wealth, poverty, ease and restriction are tests and trials from Allaah in order to know who is grateful or ungrateful, patient or impatient."},{"type":"p","text":"Specific Provision: This is the provision of the hearts - feeding them with knowledge, faith and halaal provision which help to rectify their religion. This is specific to the believers according to the levels that they deserve in accordance to His Wisdom and Mercy. Allaah completes His generosity upon them from Him by admitting them into blessed gardens on the Day of Resurrection. Allaah the Exalted says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And whosoever believes in Allah and performs righteous good deeds, He will admit him into Gardens under which rivers flow (Paradise), to dwell therein forever. Allah has indeed granted for him an excellent provision.","ref":"Talaq 65:11"}],"keyPoints":["Ar-Razzaaq is found in one place in the Qur'aan (Dhaariyaat 51:58); Ar-Raaziq occurs in the plural form, such as 'the Best of providers' (Jumu'ah 62:11), and is also found in the Sunnah.","Ar-Razzaaq means He takes care of the servants' provisions and is in charge over every person's requirements regarding provision.","General provision is provision for the body and encompasses the righteous and the bad, the believer and the disbeliever.","Extensive or restricted worldly provision is not a proof of a servant's nobility or insignificance in Allaah's Sight; wealth and poverty are tests.","Specific provision is the provision of the hearts (knowledge, faith and halaal provision), specific to the believers, completed by admitting them into Paradise."],"evidence":[{"text":"Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.","ref":"Dhaariyaat 51:58"},{"text":"And no (moving) living creature is there on earth but its provision is due from Allah.","ref":"Hood 11:6"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ar-Razzaaq (The Great Provider) mean?","a":"He takes care of the servants' provisions and is the One Who is in charge over every person's requirements regarding provision."},{"q":"Where is Ar-Raaziq (The Best of Sustainers) found?","a":"In the plural form in places of the Qur'aan, such as \"And Allah is the Best of providers\" [Jumu'ah 62:11], and also in the Sunnah."},{"q":"What are the two types of Allaah's provision?","a":"General provision (for the body, for the righteous and the bad, believer and disbeliever) and specific provision (provision of the hearts: knowledge, faith and halaal provision, specific to the believers)."},{"q":"Is extensive worldly provision a proof of a servant's nobility with Allaah?","a":"No. Wealth, poverty, ease and restriction are tests from Allaah to know who is grateful or ungrateful, patient or impatient (Fajr 89:15-17)."}]},{"chapter":9,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Ahad","arabic":"الأَحَد","meaning":"The Unique"},{"translit":"Al-Waahid","arabic":"الوَاحِد","meaning":"The One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As for Allaah's Name Al-Ahad The Unique, it is found in one place in the Qur'aan in Sooratul Ikhlaas. This is the magnificent Soorah which is mentioned in the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ as being equal to a third of the Qur'aan due to it sincerely clarifying the Lord's Beautiful Names and His Great Lofty Attributes."},{"type":"p","text":"As for His Name al Waahid The One, then it is found in numerous places in the Qur'aan."},{"type":"p","text":"These two Names indicate Allaah's Oneness and Uniqueness which means that He alone has Attributes of Glory and Majesty. He alone is described as having Grandeur and Beauty."},{"type":"p","text":"He is One in His Self - no one is like Him. He is One in His Attributes - no one compares to Him. He is One in His Actions - He has no partner or helper. He is One in deserving to be worshipped and He has no rival in love, honour, humility or humbleness."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name al Waahid occurs in the Noble Qur'aan in numerous situations in the context of establishing Monotheism (Tawheed) and invalidating Polytheism (Shirk - associating partners and associates with Allaah)."},{"type":"p","text":"In establishing Oneness and obligating sincerity (ikhlaas) of the religion for Him, Allaah said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And your Ilah (God) is One Ilah (God - Allah), La ilaha illa Huwa (there is none who has the right to be worshipped but He), the Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful.","ref":"Baqarah 2:163"},{"type":"p","text":"And He said in destroying the beliefs of the polytheists:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah said (O mankind!): \"Take not ilahain (two gods in worship, etc.). Verily, He (Allah) is (the) only One Ilah (God). Then, fear Me (Allah).","ref":"Nahl 16:51"},{"type":"quote","text":"O two companions of the prison! Are many different lords (gods) better or Allah, the One, the Irresistible?","ref":"Yoosuf 12:39"},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore it is obligatory upon the servants to single Allaah out for worship alone in beliefs, speech and actions. They need to recognise His absolute perfection and single Him out alone for worship. They need to single Him out through types of worship alone without partner."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Ahad is found in one place in the Qur'aan, in Sooratul Ikhlaas, which the Sunnah mentions as equal to a third of the Qur'aan.","Al-Waahid is found in numerous places in the Qur'aan, in the context of establishing Tawheed and invalidating Shirk.","Both Names indicate Allaah's Oneness and Uniqueness: He alone has Attributes of Glory and Majesty, Grandeur and Beauty.","He is One in His Self, His Attributes, His Actions, and in deserving to be worshipped.","It is obligatory upon the servants to single Allaah out for worship alone in beliefs, speech and actions."],"evidence":[{"text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"He is Allah, (the) One.\"","ref":"Ikhlaas 112:1"},{"text":"And your Ilah (God) is One Ilah (God - Allah), La ilaha illa Huwa, the Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful.","ref":"Baqarah 2:163"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Ahad mean and where is it found in the Qur'aan?","a":"The Unique; it is found in one place in the Qur'aan, in Sooratul Ikhlaas."},{"q":"What does Al-Waahid mean and in what context does it occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"The One; it occurs in numerous places in the context of establishing Tawheed and invalidating Shirk."},{"q":"In which four matters is Allaah One?","a":"In His Self (no one is like Him), His Attributes (no one compares to Him), His Actions (no partner or helper), and in deserving to be worshipped (no rival in love, honour, humility or humbleness)."},{"q":"Why is Sooratul Ikhlaas equal to a third of the Qur'aan, as mentioned by the author?","a":"Due to it sincerely clarifying the Lord's Beautiful Names and His Great Lofty Attributes."}]},{"chapter":10,"names":[{"translit":"As-Samad","arabic":"الصَّمَد","meaning":"The Self-Sufficient Master"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This name is found in Suratul Ikhlaas."},{"type":"p","text":"'As Samad' means (as-Sayyid al-'Adheem) The Great Master who has complete and perfect knowledge, wisdom, forbearance, power, honour, greatness and is Perfect in all His Attributes and descriptions."},{"type":"p","text":"So He possesses great and encompassing descriptions. All of the creation depend upon Him. All beings, even the most hidden, call upon Him in all their affairs. They do not have a Lord other than Him. They do not have anyone other than Him that they can call on to rectify their religious or worldly matters. They take refuge in Him at times of calamities and troubles. They humbly implore Him when disasters and hard times strike. They ask Him for help during hardships and trials. This is because they know that He can meet their needs and remove the calamities due to His Perfect and complete Knowledge, encompassing Mercy and Compassion, His Perfection, great Ability, His Honour and His Authority."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Jareer at Tabaree narrated in his Tafseer from 'Abdullaah bin 'Abbaas that he said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"As Samad The Self-Sufficient Master: The Master who is complete in his Mastership; The Sublime who is complete in His Sublimity; The Great who is complete in His Greatness; The Forbearing who is complete in His Forbearance and Clemency; The Rich who is complete in His Richness; The Wise who is complete in His Wisdom. He is the One who is complete and perfect in types of Exaltedness and Mastership. He is Allaah, the One removed from every defect who deserves these descriptions which are only befitting to Him.","ref":"Tafseer at-Tabaree (24/736 At Turki Print); Suyooti in 'Dur al Manthoor' (15/780)"}],"keyPoints":["As-Samad is found in Suratul Ikhlaas.","As-Samad means the Great Master who has complete and perfect knowledge, wisdom, forbearance, power, honour and greatness, and is Perfect in all His Attributes.","All of the creation depend upon Him and call upon Him in all their affairs, taking refuge in Him in calamities and hardships.","They turn to Him because He can meet their needs and remove calamities due to His perfect Knowledge, Mercy, Ability, Honour and Authority.","Ibn 'Abbaas explained As-Samad as the One complete in Mastership, Sublimity, Greatness, Forbearance, Richness and Wisdom."],"evidence":[{"text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"He is Allah, (the) One. Allah-us-Samad (The Self-Sufficient Master, Whom all creatures need). He begets not, nor was He begotten; and there is none co-equal or comparable unto Him.\"","ref":"Ikhlaas 112:1-4"},{"text":"Ibn 'Abbaas: \"As Samad: The Master who is complete in his Mastership ... He is the One who is complete and perfect in types of Exaltedness and Mastership.\"","ref":"Tafseer at-Tabaree (24/736)"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Samad mean?","a":"The Self-Sufficient Master: the Great Master who has complete and perfect knowledge, wisdom, forbearance, power, honour, greatness and is Perfect in all His Attributes and descriptions."},{"q":"In which Soorah is the Name As-Samad found?","a":"Suratul Ikhlaas."},{"q":"How did Ibn 'Abbaas explain As-Samad?","a":"The Master complete in His Mastership, the Sublime complete in His Sublimity, the Great complete in His Greatness, the Forbearing complete in His Forbearance, the Rich complete in His Richness, the Wise complete in His Wisdom."},{"q":"Why do all beings call upon As-Samad in their needs?","a":"Because they know He can meet their needs and remove the calamities due to His perfect Knowledge, encompassing Mercy and Compassion, His Perfection, great Ability, Honour and Authority."}]},{"chapter":11,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Haadee","arabic":"الهَادِي","meaning":"The Guide"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah mentioned this Name twice in the Qur'aan:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And verily, Allah is the Guide of those who believe, to the Straight Path.","ref":"Haj 22:54"},{"type":"quote","text":"Thus have We made for every Prophet an enemy among the Mujrimun (disbelievers, polytheists, criminals, etc.). But Sufficient is your Lord as a Guide and Helper.","ref":"Furqaan 25:31"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Haadee The Guide means that He guides His servants, directs them and indicates what will give them happiness in this Life and the Next. Through His guidance He directs the living creatures to what will benefit them and protect them from what will harm them."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah is the One who created the creation and guided them."},{"type":"quote","text":"Who has created (everything), and then proportioned it; And Who has measured (preordainments for each and everything even to be blessed or wretched); then guided.","ref":"A'laa 87:2-3"},{"type":"p","text":"So He guided them to general guidance for their benefit. He made them prepared for what they were created for."},{"type":"p","text":"He guided to a guidance of clarification. He revealed the Books and sent Messengers. He legislated the legislation and rulings, halal (permissible) and haraam (impermissible). He clarified the foundations and the branches of the religion. He guided to and clarified the straight path which will lead to His pleasure and reward. He made clear the other (deviant) paths to warn the servants."},{"type":"p","text":"He guided His believing servants with the guidance of success to belief and obedience. He guided them to their stations in Paradise as He guided them in the world to take the means and paths leading to it. His Name al Haadee The Guide encompasses all types of guidance."}],"keyPoints":["Allaah mentioned the Name Al-Haadee twice in the Qur'aan (Haj 22:54 and Furqaan 25:31).","Al-Haadee means He guides His servants, directs them and indicates what will give them happiness in this Life and the Next.","General guidance: He guided the creation to their benefit and prepared them for what they were created for.","Guidance of clarification: He revealed the Books, sent Messengers, legislated rulings and clarified the straight path and warned of deviant paths.","Guidance of success: He guided His believing servants to belief and obedience, and to their stations in Paradise; His Name al-Haadee encompasses all types of guidance."],"evidence":[{"text":"And verily, Allah is the Guide of those who believe, to the Straight Path.","ref":"Haj 22:54"},{"text":"But Sufficient is your Lord as a Guide and Helper.","ref":"Furqaan 25:31"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Haadee (The Guide) mean?","a":"He guides His servants, directs them and indicates what will give them happiness in this Life and the Next, directing living creatures to what benefits them and protecting them from what harms them."},{"q":"How many times is Al-Haadee mentioned in the Qur'aan, and where?","a":"Twice: Haj 22:54 and Furqaan 25:31."},{"q":"What types of guidance does the author mention?","a":"General guidance for the creation's benefit, guidance of clarification (Books, Messengers, rulings, the straight path), and guidance of success to belief and obedience, including guidance to their stations in Paradise."},{"q":"What does the guidance of clarification include?","a":"Revealing the Books, sending Messengers, legislating rulings of halaal and haraam, clarifying the foundations and branches of the religion, clarifying the straight path and making clear the deviant paths as a warning."}]},{"chapter":12,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Wahhaab","arabic":"الوَهَّاب","meaning":"The Bestower"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name occurs in three places of the Noble Qur'aan:"},{"type":"quote","text":"(They say): \"Our Lord! Let not our hearts deviate (from the truth) after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from You. Truly, You are the Bestower.\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:8"},{"type":"quote","text":"Or have they the treasures of the Mercy of your Lord, the Almighty, the Real Bestower?","ref":"Saad 38:9"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said when He mentioned the du'aa of Prophet Sulaymaan:"},{"type":"quote","text":"He said: \"My Lord! Forgive me, and bestow upon me a kingdom such as shall not belong to any other after me: Verily, You are the Bestower.\"","ref":"Saad 38:35"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Wahhaab The Bestower means plentiful in giving gifts, blessings and benefits. The Name is of (the Arabic grammatical pattern of) fa''aal which the Arabs use to express the meaning of intensification. Allaah is the Bestower - He bestows of His great virtue upon His servants by conferring blessings, increasing and abundantly giving gifts to them."},{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Wahhaab comes in the grammatical form of intensification due to Allaah's abundance in giving constantly in a variety of forms and liberally."},{"type":"p","text":"In Allaah's Hand is the treasures of everything. He owns the heavens and the earth and has rule over everything. He disposes of His kingdom however He wills."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah mentioned in the Noble Qur'aan the different types of His giving. He mentions His directing His Prophets and righteous people from amongst His servants to seek it and attain it."},{"type":"p","text":"These various gifts belong to Allaah. He is Al Maalik The Owner of this Universe. He can dispose of it as He wishes."},{"type":"quote","text":"To Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth. He creates what He wills. He bestows female (offspring) upon whom He wills, and bestows male (offspring) upon whom He wills. Or He bestows both males and females, and He renders barren whom He wills. Verily, He is the All-Knower and is Able to do all things.","ref":"Shooraa 42:49-50"},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah to You is all praise out of gratefulness, to You is giving out of Your Grace."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Wahhaab occurs in three places in the Noble Qur'aan (Aali 'Imraan 3:8, Saad 38:9 and Saad 38:35).","Al-Wahhaab means plentiful in giving gifts, blessings and benefits.","The Name is on the Arabic pattern fa''aal, used for intensification, due to Allaah's abundance in giving constantly, in a variety of forms and liberally.","In Allaah's Hand are the treasures of everything; He owns the heavens and the earth and disposes of His kingdom however He wills.","Allaah directed His Prophets and righteous servants to seek His gifts, as in Sulaymaan's du'aa."],"evidence":[{"text":"Our Lord! Let not our hearts deviate (from the truth) after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from You. Truly, You are the Bestower.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:8"},{"text":"My Lord! Forgive me, and bestow upon me a kingdom such as shall not belong to any other after me: Verily, You are the Bestower.","ref":"Saad 38:35"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Wahhaab (The Bestower) mean?","a":"Plentiful in giving gifts, blessings and benefits."},{"q":"Why does the Name Al-Wahhaab come in the grammatical form of intensification?","a":"Due to Allaah's abundance in giving constantly in a variety of forms and liberally."},{"q":"How many times does Al-Wahhaab occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"In three places: Aali 'Imraan 3:8, Saad 38:9 and Saad 38:35."},{"q":"Which Prophet's du'aa does the author cite that ends with \"Verily, You are the Bestower\"?","a":"The du'aa of Prophet Sulaymaan [Saad 38:35]."}]},{"chapter":13,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Fattaah","arabic":"الفَتَّاح","meaning":"The Just Judge"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say: \"Our Lord will assemble us all together (on the Day of Resurrection), then He will judge between us with truth. And He is the (Most Trustworthy) All-Knowing Judge.\"","ref":"Saba 34:26"},{"type":"quote","text":"Our Lord comprehends all things in His Knowledge. In Allah (Alone) we put our trust. Our Lord! Judge between us and our people in truth, for You are the Best of those who give judgment.","ref":"A'raaf 7:89"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of this Name is the One who rules over His servants with whatever He wishes, He judges between them with what He Wills. He gives those of them He Wills whatever He Wills. Nothing can repel His rule and nothing comes after His decree and command. Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Whatever of mercy (i.e. of good) Allah may grant to mankind, none can withhold it, and whatever He may withhold, none can grant it thereafter. And He is the Almighty, the All-Wise.","ref":"Faatir 35:2"},{"type":"p","text":"A servant's belief that His Lord is Al-Fattaah The Judge should make him turn to Allaah alone in a good manner to open the doors of guidance for him, the doors of provision, the doors of mercy and that Allaah opens his heart to do good."},{"type":"quote","text":"Is he whose breast Allah has opened to Islam, so that he is in light from His Lord (as he who is non-Muslim)? So, woe to those whose hearts are hardened against remembrance of Allah! They are in plain error!","ref":"Zumar 39:22"},{"type":"p","text":"Qurtubi said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"This opening/conquest/expanding does not have a limit. Every believer takes a share from it. The Prophets succeeded in taking the highest share, then after them the awliyaa' allies of Allaah, then the scholars, then the general believers and no one will fail except the disbelievers.","ref":"Al Asnaa fee Sharh Asmaa Allaah al Husnaa 1/225"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Fattaah is the One who rules over His servants with whatever He wishes and judges between them with what He Wills.","He gives whom He Wills whatever He Wills; nothing can repel His rule and nothing comes after His decree and command.","Believing that Allaah is Al-Fattaah should make the servant turn to Allaah alone to open for him the doors of guidance, provision and mercy, and to open his heart to do good.","Qurtubi said this opening has no limit: every believer takes a share, the Prophets the highest, then the awliyaa', then the scholars, then the general believers; only the disbelievers fail."],"evidence":[{"text":"Then He will judge between us with truth. And He is the (Most Trustworthy) All-Knowing Judge.","ref":"Saba 34:26"},{"text":"Whatever of mercy Allah may grant to mankind, none can withhold it, and whatever He may withhold, none can grant it thereafter.","ref":"Faatir 35:2"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Fattaah (The Just Judge) mean?","a":"The One who rules over His servants with whatever He wishes, judges between them with what He Wills and gives whom He Wills whatever He Wills; nothing can repel His rule."},{"q":"What should a servant's belief that his Lord is Al-Fattaah lead him to do?","a":"Turn to Allaah alone in a good manner to open for him the doors of guidance, provision and mercy, and to open his heart to do good."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite showing that none can withhold what Allaah grants?","a":"Faatir 35:2: \"Whatever of mercy Allah may grant to mankind, none can withhold it, and whatever He may withhold, none can grant it thereafter.\""},{"q":"According to Qurtubi, who takes the highest share of Allaah's opening?","a":"The Prophets, then the awliyaa', then the scholars, then the general believers; no one fails except the disbelievers."}]},{"chapter":14,"names":[{"translit":"As-Samee'","arabic":"السَّمِيع","meaning":"The All-Hearing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As-Samee' The All-Hearing is a Name which occurs many times in the Qur'aan. It comes in nearly 50 places. An example is Allaah the Exalted's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.","ref":"Shooraa 42:11"},{"type":"quote","text":"And (remember) when Ibrahim (Abraham) and (his son) Isma'il (Ishmael) were raising the foundations of the House (the Ka'bah at Makkah), (saying), \"Our Lord! Accept (this service) from us. Verily! You are the All-Hearer, the All-Knower.\"","ref":"Baqarah 2:127"},{"type":"p","text":"As-Samee' is the One who hears every sound in different languages and the diverse needs. Secret speech and open loud speech is the same to Allaah."},{"type":"quote","text":"It is the same (to Him) whether any of you conceal his speech or declare it openly, whether he be hid by night or go forth freely by day.","ref":"Ra'd 13:10"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Hearing encompasses all sounds, so the sounds are not different to Him neither do they resemble each other. Neither does listening to one sound occupy Him from listening to another. Allaah does not make a mistake in the various requests neither does He become weary of the many pleas."},{"type":"p","text":"Imaam Ahmad and others reported that 'Aa'ishah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Praise be to Allah Whose hearing encompasses all voices. Khawlah came to the Messenger of Allah complaining about her husband, but I could not hear what she said. Then Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, revealed: 'Indeed Allah has heard the statement of her that disputes with you concerning her husband, and complains to Allah. And Allah hears the argument between you both.' [Sooratul Mujaadilah 58:1]","ref":"Musnad Ahmad 6/168; Sunan an-Nasa'i 3460"},{"type":"p","text":"In another narration she said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Blessed is the One whose Hearing encompasses everything.","ref":"Ibn Maajah 188"},{"type":"p","text":"If every jinn and human from the first of them until Allaah inherits the earth and everything on it were to stand in one place and all ask Allaah at the same moment, each one expressing his need, each one speaking in his dialect and language Allaah would Hear all of them without mixing up this speech with that one and this language with that or this need with that need."}],"keyPoints":["As-Samee' occurs many times in the Qur'aan, in nearly 50 places.","As-Samee' is the One who hears every sound in different languages and the diverse needs; secret and open speech are the same to Him.","Listening to one sound does not occupy Him from another; He does not make a mistake in the various requests nor become weary of the many pleas.","'Aa'ishah praised Allaah Whose hearing encompasses all voices when He heard Khawlah's complaint, which she herself could not hear (Mujaadilah 58:1).","If all jinn and humans stood in one place and asked at the same moment in their own languages, Allaah would hear all of them without mixing up any speech, language or need."],"evidence":[{"text":"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.","ref":"Shooraa 42:11"},{"text":"'Aa'ishah: \"Praise be to Allah Whose hearing encompasses all voices. Khawlah came to the Messenger of Allah complaining about her husband, but I could not hear what she said. Then Allah revealed: 'Indeed Allah has heard the statement of her that disputes with you concerning her husband...'\"","ref":"Musnad Ahmad 6/168; Sunan an-Nasa'i 3460"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Samee' (The All-Hearing) mean?","a":"The One who hears every sound in different languages and the diverse needs; secret speech and open loud speech are the same to Him."},{"q":"Approximately how many times does As-Samee' occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"In nearly 50 places."},{"q":"What did 'Aa'ishah say about Khawlah's complaint?","a":"\"Praise be to Allah Whose hearing encompasses all voices\" - Khawlah complained about her husband, 'Aa'ishah could not hear what she said, and Allaah revealed Mujaadilah 58:1."},{"q":"What would happen if all jinn and humans asked Allaah at the same moment in one place?","a":"Allaah would hear all of them without mixing up this speech with that one, this language with that, or this need with that need."}]},{"chapter":15,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Baseer","arabic":"البَصِير","meaning":"The All-Seeing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Baseer is a Name found in the Noble Qur'aan in more than 40 places. Examples are,"},{"type":"quote","text":"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.","ref":"Shooraa 42:11"},{"type":"quote","text":"Truly, Allah is Ever All-Hearer, All-Seer.","ref":"Nisaa 4:58"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Baseer means the One who sees all visual sights. He sees everything whether minute or small. He sees a crawling black ant on a black rock in the dark night. He sees the path of the morsel of food carried by their limbs. He sees what is beneath the seven earths as He sees what is above the seven heavens. He sees the blinking of the eyelids and the treachery of the eyes. Someone rightly said (some poetry):"},{"type":"quote","text":"O One who sees the beating of the mosquito's wing\nIn the darkness of the night. The moaning cattle\nHe sees the place where its veins are suspended in its neck\nAnd its brain from those weakened bones.\nGrant me repentance to wipe away from me what I did in my early days.","ref":"Poetry quoted by al-Qurtubi in at-Tathkirah 1/464"},{"type":"p","text":"Then this magnificent Name instills humility and humbleness. It encourages a person to know that Allaah is observing him and that he should perfect His worship and stay away from disobedience and sins."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Rajab said, \"A man sought to seduce a woman and have his way with her one night. She refused so he said, 'No one can see us except the stars.' She replied 'So where is the One who created the stars?' Meaning, does He not see us. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Knows he not that Allah does see (what he does)?","ref":"'Alaq 96:14"},{"type":"p","text":"This was enough of a rebuke and a deterrent.\""}],"keyPoints":["Al-Baseer is found in the Noble Qur'aan in more than 40 places.","Al-Baseer means the One who sees all visual sights, whether minute or small.","He sees a crawling black ant on a black rock in the dark night, and what is beneath the seven earths just as what is above the seven heavens.","He sees the blinking of the eyelids and the treachery of the eyes.","This Name instills humility and humbleness, and encourages a person to know Allaah is observing him, to perfect his worship and stay away from sins."],"evidence":[{"text":"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.","ref":"Shooraa 42:11"},{"text":"Knows he not that Allah does see (what he does)?","ref":"'Alaq 96:14"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Baseer mean?","a":"The One who sees all visual sights; He sees everything whether minute or small."},{"q":"How many times is Al-Baseer found in the Qur'aan according to the book?","a":"In more than 40 places."},{"q":"In the story narrated by Ibn Rajab, what did the woman reply when the man said 'No one can see us except the stars'?","a":"'So where is the One who created the stars?' meaning, does He not see us."},{"q":"Which aayah does Ibn Rajab cite after the story of the woman?","a":"'Knows he not that Allah does see (what he does)?' ['Alaq 96:14]"},{"q":"What effect does this Name have on the servant?","a":"It instills humility and humbleness, and encourages him to know Allaah is observing him, so he perfects his worship and stays away from disobedience and sins."}]},{"chapter":16,"names":[{"translit":"Al-'Aleem","arabic":"العَلِيم","meaning":"The All-Knowing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name occurs in the Noble Qur'aan more than 150 times. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He creates what He wills. And it is He Who is the All-Knowing, the All-Powerful (i.e. Able to do all things).","ref":"Room 30:54"},{"type":"quote","text":"and Allah is Sufficient as All-Knower.","ref":"Nisaa 4:70"},{"type":"p","text":"This means the One Whose knowledge encompasses the apparent and the hidden; the secret and the open; knowledge of the upper and lower; the past, present and future. Not one thing is hidden from Him. He knew what was, what will be and what was not; and if it were, how it would be. His knowledge encompasses everything and He keeps count of all things (knows the exact number of everything)."},{"type":"p","text":"Faith in this magnificent Name has a blessed effect upon the servant. It is in fact the biggest deterrent and greatest admonition."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykh Muhammad al-Ameen ash-Shinqeetee said, \"The scholars have agreed that it is the biggest admonition and the greatest deterrent that was revealed from the heavens to the earth... you do not turn a single page of the Noble mushaf without finding this great admonition and great deterrent."},{"type":"quote","text":"And He is the All-Knower of everything.","ref":"Baqarah 2:29"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Well-Acquainted with what you do.","ref":"Baqarah 2:234"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah knows what you conceal and what you reveal.","ref":"Nahl 16:19"},{"type":"quote","text":"And with Him are the keys of the Ghaib (all that is hidden), none knows them but He. And He knows whatever there is in (or on) the earth and in the sea; not a leaf falls, but he knows it. There is not a grain in the darkness of the earth nor anything fresh or dry, but is written in a Clear Record.","ref":"An'aam 6:59"},{"type":"quote","text":"And indeed We have created man, and We know what his ownself whispers to him. And We are nearer to him than his jugular vein (by Our Knowledge).","ref":"Qaaf 50:16"},{"type":"quote","text":"And know that Allah knows what is in your minds, so fear Him.","ref":"Baqarah 2:235"},{"type":"quote","text":"Whatever you (O Muhammad) may be doing, and whatever portion you may be reciting from the Quran, - and whatever deed you (mankind) may be doing (good or evil), We are Witness thereof, when you are doing it.","ref":"Yoonus 10:61"},{"type":"p","text":"So all of us we need to take heed of this great deterrent and mighty admonition and not forget it so as not to destroy ourselves.\""}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-'Aleem occurs in the Noble Qur'aan more than 150 times.","It means the One Whose knowledge encompasses the apparent and the hidden, the secret and the open, the upper and lower, and the past, present and future.","He knew what was, what will be, and what was not and, if it were, how it would be; He keeps count of all things.","Faith in this Name is the biggest deterrent and greatest admonition for the servant.","Ash-Shinqeetee said the scholars agreed it is the biggest admonition revealed from the heavens, and no page of the mushaf is without it."],"evidence":[{"text":"He creates what He wills. And it is He Who is the All-Knowing, the All-Powerful.","ref":"Room 30:54"},{"text":"And with Him are the keys of the Ghaib (all that is hidden), none knows them but He... not a leaf falls, but he knows it.","ref":"An'aam 6:59"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-'Aleem mean?","a":"The One Whose knowledge encompasses the apparent and the hidden, the secret and the open, the upper and lower, the past, present and future; not one thing is hidden from Him."},{"q":"How many times does Al-'Aleem occur in the Qur'aan according to the book?","a":"More than 150 times."},{"q":"What did Shaykh ash-Shinqeetee say the scholars agreed upon regarding Allaah's knowledge?","a":"That it is the biggest admonition and the greatest deterrent revealed from the heavens to the earth; you do not turn a page of the mushaf without finding it."},{"q":"Which aayah mentions that not a leaf falls but He knows it?","a":"An'aam 6:59."},{"q":"Does Allaah's knowledge include what did not happen?","a":"Yes, He knew what was, what will be and what was not; and if it were, how it would be."}]},{"chapter":17,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Lateef","arabic":"اللَّطِيف","meaning":"The Subtle and Kind"},{"translit":"Al-Khabeer","arabic":"الخَبِير","meaning":"The Fully Aware"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are two Names that have repeatedly come together in many aayaat of the Noble Qur'aan. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"No vision can grasp Him, but His Grasp is over all vision. He is the Most Subtle and Courteous, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:103"},{"type":"p","text":"He said in mentioning the advice that Luqmaan the wise gave to his son,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"O my son! If it be (anything) equal to the weight of a grain of mustard seed, and though it be in a rock, or in the heavens or in the earth, Allah will bring it forth. Verily, Allah is Subtle (in bringing out that grain), Well-Aware (of its place).","ref":"Luqmaan 31:16"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Khabeer The Fully-Aware means the One through His knowledge knows the hidden matters, sees what is hidden in the innermost conscience and the most insignificant of matters. He knows the hidden seeds and the minute atoms."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Khabeer is a Name that refers back to His knowledge of hidden matters which consist of the utmost minute, tiny, concealed matters. In addition to this even more so His knowledge encompasses that of the apparent and open matters."},{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Lateef The Subtle and Kind has two meanings:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. It has the same meaning of Al-Khabeer The Fully-Aware - that He knows the minute and insignificant details such as the secrets, inner conscience and the hidden matters."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Allaah facilitates what is in the interests of His servants and allies with kindness and perfection through ways they do not perceive."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Lateef and Al-Khabeer have repeatedly come together in many aayaat of the Qur'aan.","Al-Khabeer means the One who through His knowledge knows the hidden matters, what is hidden in the innermost conscience, the hidden seeds and the minute atoms.","Al-Khabeer refers back to His knowledge of the most minute, concealed matters, and His knowledge encompasses the apparent matters even more so.","Al-Lateef's first meaning is the same as Al-Khabeer: He knows the minute details such as secrets, inner conscience and hidden matters.","Al-Lateef's second meaning: Allaah facilitates what is in the interests of His servants and allies with kindness and perfection through ways they do not perceive."],"evidence":[{"text":"No vision can grasp Him, but His Grasp is over all vision. He is the Most Subtle and Courteous, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:103"},{"text":"Verily, Allah is Subtle (in bringing out that grain), Well-Aware (of its place).","ref":"Luqmaan 31:16"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Khabeer mean?","a":"The One who through His knowledge knows the hidden matters, sees what is hidden in the innermost conscience and the most insignificant of matters; He knows the hidden seeds and the minute atoms."},{"q":"What are the two meanings of Al-Lateef?","a":"1) The same meaning as Al-Khabeer: He knows the minute details such as secrets, inner conscience and hidden matters. 2) He facilitates what is in the interests of His servants and allies with kindness and perfection through ways they do not perceive."},{"q":"Whose advice to his son does the author cite for these two Names?","a":"Luqmaan the wise [Luqmaan 31:16]."},{"q":"Which aayah says 'No vision can grasp Him...'?","a":"An'aam 6:103."}]},{"chapter":18,"names":[{"translit":"Al-'Afuww","arabic":"العَفُوّ","meaning":"The Pardoner"},{"translit":"Al-Ghafoor","arabic":"الغَفُور","meaning":"The Ever-Forgiving"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah the Exalted said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"That is so. And whoever has retaliated with the like of that which he was made to suffer, and then has again been wronged, Allah will surely help him. Verily! Allah indeed is Oft-Pardoning, Oft-Forgiving.","ref":"Hajj 22:60"},{"type":"quote","text":"For these there is hope that Allah will forgive them, and Allah is Ever Oft Pardoning, Oft-Forgiving.","ref":"Nisaa 4:99"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-'Afuww The Pardoner. He is the One who wipes away bad deeds and overlooks sins. It has a similar meaning to Al-Ghafoor The Forgiver, but it is more far reaching than it."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Ghufraan (forgiveness) indicates 'covering'. Al-'Afuww (pardoning) indicates 'wiping away'."},{"type":"p","text":"Wiping away is more extensive than covering. When both words are together (they have this separate meaning). However, when the word appears on its own then each of them carries the meaning of the other."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Pardon is of two types:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. His general pardon of all the criminals from the disbelievers and other than them, by repelling the punishments that they have earned when they are more deserving of the removal of blessings. So they annoy Him by insults, shirk (polytheism) and other offenses whilst He pardons them, provides for them and abundantly bestows apparent and hidden blessings upon them. He lays out the world for them. He gives them its blessings, benefits and gives respite to them. He does not neglect them out of His Pardon and Forbearing."},{"type":"p","text":"2. His special Pardon and Forgiveness to those who turn in repentance, ask forgiveness, supplicate, worship and to those who are afflicted with trials for which they expect reward. So everyone who turns in repentance to Him with a sincere repentance - sincerely seeking His Face, generally and comprehensively, without hesitation nor persistence (upon the sin). Allaah will forgive him whatever the sin whether it is disbelief, disobedience or sin. All of these come under Allaah's Saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say: \"O 'Ibadi (My slaves) who have transgressed against themselves (by committing evil deeds and sins)! Despair not of the Mercy of Allah, verily Allah forgives all sins. Truly, He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","ref":"Zumar 39:53"},{"type":"p","text":"The doors of His Pardon and Forgiveness are open. He has always been and will always be pardoning and forgiving. Allaah promised forgiveness and pardon to those who come with its prerequisites as Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And verily, I am indeed Forgiving to him who repents, believes (in My Oneness, and associates none in worship with Me) and does righteous good deeds, and then remains constant in doing them, (till his death).","ref":"Taha 20:82"}],"keyPoints":["Al-'Afuww is the One who wipes away bad deeds and overlooks sins; it is similar in meaning to Al-Ghafoor but more far reaching.","Forgiveness (al-ghufraan) indicates covering, while pardoning (al-'afuww) indicates wiping away, which is more extensive; when mentioned alone, each carries the meaning of the other.","Allaah's general pardon covers all criminals, including disbelievers: He repels the punishments they earned and still provides for them and gives them respite.","His special pardon and forgiveness is for those who repent, seek forgiveness, supplicate, worship, and those afflicted with trials who expect reward.","Whoever repents sincerely is forgiven whatever the sin, even disbelief; the doors of His Pardon and Forgiveness are open."],"evidence":[{"text":"Verily! Allah indeed is Oft-Pardoning, Oft-Forgiving.","ref":"Hajj 22:60"},{"text":"Despair not of the Mercy of Allah, verily Allah forgives all sins. Truly, He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.","ref":"Zumar 39:53"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-'Afuww mean?","a":"The One who wipes away bad deeds and overlooks sins."},{"q":"What is the difference between Al-'Afuww and Al-Ghafoor when mentioned together?","a":"Forgiveness (ghufraan) indicates covering, while pardoning ('afuww) indicates wiping away, which is more extensive. When either appears alone it carries the meaning of the other."},{"q":"What are the two types of Allaah's Pardon?","a":"1) His general pardon of all criminals, including disbelievers, by repelling the punishments they earned while still providing for them. 2) His special Pardon and Forgiveness for those who repent, seek forgiveness, supplicate, worship and are patient with trials hoping for reward."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite to show that Allaah forgives all sins for the one who repents?","a":"Zumar 39:53: 'Despair not of the Mercy of Allah, verily Allah forgives all sins...'"},{"q":"Which aayah mentions the prerequisites for Allaah's forgiveness?","a":"Taha 20:82: 'And verily, I am indeed Forgiving to him who repents, believes and does righteous good deeds, and then remains constant in doing them.'"}]},{"chapter":19,"names":[{"translit":"Al-'Alee","arabic":"العَلِيّ","meaning":"The Exalted"},{"translit":"Al-A'laa","arabic":"الأَعْلَى","meaning":"The Most High"},{"translit":"Al-Muta'aal","arabic":"المُتَعَال","meaning":"The Supreme and Exalted One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And He is the Most High, the Most Great.","ref":"Baqarah 2:255"},{"type":"quote","text":"Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High","ref":"'Alaa 87:1"},{"type":"quote","text":"All-Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Most Great, the Most High.","ref":"Ra'd 13:9"},{"type":"p","text":"These Names indicate Allaah's absolute Highness from every aspect and consideration:"},{"type":"p","text":"* He is Al-'Alee The High in His Self (dhaat). He rose over the throne and is above and separate from all of the created beings. He said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"The Most Beneficent (Allah) rose over (Istawa) the (Mighty) Throne (in a manner that suits His Majesty).","ref":"Taha 20:5"},{"type":"p","text":"He said in six aayaat in the Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"then He rose over (Istawa) the Throne (really in a manner that suits His Majesty).","ref":"A'raaf 7:54"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that He is above and rose over it high above in a manner that suits His Majesty, Perfection and Greatness."},{"type":"p","text":"* He is The High in His Esteem (qadr). He is High regarding His descriptions and greatness. His Attributes are magnificent and nothing is like them and no one's description can be close to them. Indeed the servants are incapable of comprehending even one of His Attributes."},{"type":"p","text":"* He is The High in His Control (qahr). He overcomes everything. The created beings come close to Him with their secrets. The forelocks of all the creation are in His Hand. None of them move or stay still except by His Permission. What He willed came to pass and what He did not will did not happen."},{"type":"p","text":"A servant's faith in Allaah's Highness above His creation instills in him the Greatness of Allaah, humbleness before Him and humility to Him. It removes shortcomings and defects from Him and makes him sincere in his worship. It distances him from taking partners and associates with Him. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"That is because Allah He is the Truth (the only True God of all that exists, Who has no partners or rivals with Him), and what they (the polytheists) invoke besides Him, it is Batil (falsehood) And verily, Allah He is the Most High, the Most Great.","ref":"Hajj 22:62"}],"keyPoints":["These Names indicate Allaah's absolute Highness from every aspect and consideration.","He is High in His Self (dhaat): He rose over the Throne and is above and separate from all created beings, in a manner that suits His Majesty.","He is High in His Esteem (qadr): His Attributes are magnificent, nothing is like them, and the servants cannot comprehend even one of them.","He is High in His Control (qahr): He overcomes everything, the forelocks of all creation are in His Hand, and none moves or stays still except by His Permission.","Faith in His Highness instills humility and sincerity in worship and distances the servant from taking partners with Him."],"evidence":[{"text":"And He is the Most High, the Most Great.","ref":"Baqarah 2:255"},{"text":"The Most Beneficent (Allah) rose over (Istawa) the (Mighty) Throne (in a manner that suits His Majesty).","ref":"Taha 20:5"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do the Names Al-'Alee, Al-A'laa and Al-Muta'aal indicate?","a":"Allaah's absolute Highness from every aspect and consideration."},{"q":"What are the three aspects of Allaah's Highness mentioned by the author?","a":"High in His Self (dhaat), High in His Esteem (qadr), and High in His Control (qahr)."},{"q":"What does Highness in His Self mean?","a":"He rose over the Throne and is above and separate from all of the created beings, in a manner that suits His Majesty, Perfection and Greatness."},{"q":"In how many aayaat does Allaah say He rose over (Istawa) the Throne, according to the book?","a":"In six aayaat (e.g. A'raaf 7:54), besides Taha 20:5."},{"q":"Which aayah contains 'the Most Great, the Most High' (Al-Kabeer Al-Muta'aal)?","a":"Ra'd 13:9: 'All-Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Most Great, the Most High.'"}]},{"chapter":20,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Kabeer","arabic":"الكَبِير","meaning":"The Most Great"},{"translit":"Al-'Adheem","arabic":"العَظِيم","meaning":"The Magnificent"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Kabeer The Most Great means the One who has al-kibriyaa' greatness (majesty/pride) as a description and al-'adhamah might as an attribute."},{"type":"p","text":"In a hadeeth qudsee on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allaah said: \"Pride is my cloak and greatness my robe, and he who competes with Me in respect of either of them I shall cast into Hell-fire\".","ref":"Musnad Imaam Ahmad 2/248; Sunan Aboo Daawood 4090"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah has these two descriptions of majesty and might and their value cannot be comprehended nor can they be grasped in their entirety."},{"type":"p","text":"If a Muslim believes and has faith that Allaah is greater than everything and that no matter how great something may be it will be insignificant to Allaah's greatness and might. He will humble himself to his Lord and submit in front of Him. He will perform different types of worship for Him and he will believe that Allaah deserves this worship and no one else does. He will know that every polytheist will not give His Great Lord the due he deserves. As Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"They made not a just estimate of Allah such as is due to Him. And on the Day of Resurrection the whole of the earth will be grasped by His Hand and the heavens will be rolled up in His Right Hand. Glorified is He, and High is He above all that they associate as partners with Him!","ref":"Zumar 39:67"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah is far removed from every imperfection, subhaanAllaah. Where have the intellects of the polytheists gone when they direct their humility and humbleness to lowly creation and ignoble created beings that do not possess anything of benefit or harm for themselves never mind possessing them for others. They left humbleness and humility of the Mighty Lord, the Great, the Exalted, the Majestic Creator to whom faces are humbled, voices are hushed, hearts tremble out of awe and heads lowered. Blessed be Allaah the Lord of the worlds."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Kabeer means the One who has greatness (al-kibriyaa': majesty/pride) as a description and might (al-'adhamah) as an attribute.","In a hadeeth qudsee Allaah said: \"Pride is my cloak and greatness my robe\", and whoever competes with Him in either will be cast into Hell-fire.","The value of these two descriptions of majesty and might cannot be comprehended nor grasped in their entirety.","Whoever believes Allaah is greater than everything humbles himself to his Lord and believes that only He deserves worship.","The polytheists did not make a just estimate of Allaah, directing their humility to lowly creation that possesses no benefit or harm."],"evidence":[{"text":"Pride is my cloak and greatness my robe, and he who competes with Me in respect of either of them I shall cast into Hell-fire.","ref":"Musnad Imaam Ahmad 2/248; Sunan Aboo Daawood 4090"},{"text":"They made not a just estimate of Allah such as is due to Him. And on the Day of Resurrection the whole of the earth will be grasped by His Hand and the heavens will be rolled up in His Right Hand.","ref":"Zumar 39:67"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Kabeer mean?","a":"The One who has greatness (majesty/pride, al-kibriyaa') as a description and might (al-'adhamah) as an attribute."},{"q":"What does the hadeeth qudsee say about pride and greatness?","a":"\"Pride is my cloak and greatness my robe, and he who competes with Me in respect of either of them I shall cast into Hell-fire.\""},{"q":"What is the effect on a Muslim who believes Allaah is greater than everything?","a":"He humbles himself to his Lord, submits to Him, performs worship for Him and believes that only Allaah deserves this worship."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite to show the polytheists did not give Allaah His due?","a":"Zumar 39:67: 'They made not a just estimate of Allah such as is due to Him...'"},{"q":"What is the meaning of Al-'Adheem, and what does the book say about the descriptions of majesty and might?","a":"Al-'Adheem means The Magnificent. Allaah has the two descriptions of majesty (al-kibriyaa') and might (al-'adhamah), and their value cannot be comprehended nor grasped in their entirety."}]},{"chapter":21,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Qawee","arabic":"القَوِيّ","meaning":"The One Perfect in Strength"},{"translit":"Al-Mateen","arabic":"المَتِين","meaning":"The Strong"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Qawee The One Perfect in Strength comes in many places in the Noble Qur'aan. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah is very Gracious and Kind to His slaves. He gives provisions to whom He wills. And He is the All-Strong, the Almighty.","ref":"Shooraa 42:19"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Mateen The Strong only appears once alongside the description of Allaah having strength. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.","ref":"Dhaariyaat 51:58"},{"type":"p","text":"'Mateen' means strong power. 'Qawee' means nothing is too difficult for Him. No one can overcome Him. His decree is not rejected, His Command is fulfilled and His Decree takes place in His creation. He honours whomever He wills, He debases whomever He wills. He helps whomever He wills, He forsakes whomever He wills. All power and strength is for Allaah. No one is helped except those He helps. No one is honoured except those whom He honours. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"If Allah helps you, none can overcome you; and if He forsakes you, who is there after Him that can help you? And in Allah (Alone) let believers put their trust.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:160"},{"type":"p","text":"A servant's belief in this Name instills within him a sense of humility before Allaah, humbleness, fear of Him and makes him turn to Allaah alone. It makes a person rely upon Him sincerely, submitting to His Might and returning all his affairs to Him. It makes him assign might and power only to Allaah."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Qawee comes in many places in the Qur'aan, while Al-Mateen appears only once, alongside the description of Allaah having strength (Dhaariyaat 51:58).","'Mateen' means strong power.","'Qawee' means nothing is too difficult for Him and no one can overcome Him; His Command is fulfilled and His Decree takes place in His creation.","He honours, debases, helps and forsakes whomever He wills; all power and strength is for Allaah.","Belief in this Name instills humility and fear of Allaah, and makes a person rely on Him alone and assign might and power only to Him."],"evidence":[{"text":"Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.","ref":"Dhaariyaat 51:58"},{"text":"If Allah helps you, none can overcome you; and if He forsakes you, who is there after Him that can help you?","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:160"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Mateen mean?","a":"Strong power."},{"q":"What does Al-Qawee mean?","a":"Nothing is too difficult for Him and no one can overcome Him; His decree is not rejected and His Command is fulfilled."},{"q":"How many times does Al-Mateen appear in the Qur'aan, and where?","a":"Only once, in Dhaariyaat 51:58: 'Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.'"},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite showing that no one can help if Allaah forsakes?","a":"Aali 'Imraan 3:160."},{"q":"What does belief in this Name instill in the servant?","a":"Humility, humbleness, fear of Allaah, turning to Him alone, sincere reliance upon Him, and assigning might and power only to Him."}]},{"chapter":22,"names":[{"translit":"Ash-Shaheed","arabic":"الشَّهِيد","meaning":"The Witness"},{"translit":"Ar-Raqeeb","arabic":"الرَّقِيب","meaning":"The Ever-Watchful Guardian"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ash-Shaheed The Witness is repeated in many places in the Qur'aan."},{"type":"quote","text":"and Allah is Sufficient as a Witness.","ref":"Nisaa 4:79"},{"type":"p","text":"As for Ar-Raqeeb The Ever-Watchful Guardian, it is found in three places. One of those places Ar-Raqeeb is paired with Ash-Shaheed."},{"type":"quote","text":"Surely, Allah is Ever an All-Watcher over you.","ref":"Nisaa 4:1"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Ever a Watcher over all things.","ref":"Ahzaab 33:52"},{"type":"quote","text":"And I was a witness over them while I dwelt amongst them, but when You took me up, You were the Watcher over them, and You are a Witness to all things.","ref":"Maa'idah 5:117"},{"type":"p","text":"Ash-Shaheed means He is acquainted with everything and nothing is hidden from Him. He hears all sounds hidden and apparent, He sees everything that exists – the minute and the great, the small and the big. His knowledge encompasses everything. He witnesses in favour of His servants and against them for what they have done."},{"type":"p","text":"Ar-Raqeeb means that He is acquainted with what the chests conceal, He knows what each soul earns. The One who protects the creation and subjects them to the best system and most complete management. He observes with His sight everything that can be seen with nothing being hidden from Him. He encompasses everything that can be heard with His hearing. He observes all of creation with His knowledge that encompasses everything."},{"type":"p","text":"Faith in this Name and what it encompasses instils in a servant that Allaah is observing Him in all of his actions and situations."},{"type":"p","text":"So knowing that Allaah is watching a person is the fruits of a servant knowing that Allaah observes him, sees him, hears his speech and is acquainted with what he is doing at all times, in every second, every breath and every blink of an eye."}],"keyPoints":["Ash-Shaheed is repeated in many places in the Qur'aan; Ar-Raqeeb is found in three places, and in one of them (Maa'idah 5:117) it is paired with Ash-Shaheed.","Ash-Shaheed means He is acquainted with everything, hears all sounds, sees everything that exists, and witnesses in favour of His servants and against them.","Ar-Raqeeb means He is acquainted with what the chests conceal and what each soul earns, and protects the creation with the best system and most complete management.","Ar-Raqeeb observes everything with His sight, hearing and all-encompassing knowledge.","Faith in this Name instils in the servant that Allaah is observing him in all his actions and situations, at every second, breath and blink of an eye."],"evidence":[{"text":"and Allah is Sufficient as a Witness.","ref":"Nisaa 4:79"},{"text":"You were the Watcher over them, and You are a Witness to all things.","ref":"Maa'idah 5:117"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ash-Shaheed mean?","a":"He is acquainted with everything and nothing is hidden from Him; He hears all sounds, sees everything that exists, His knowledge encompasses everything, and He witnesses in favour of His servants and against them for what they have done."},{"q":"What does Ar-Raqeeb mean?","a":"He is acquainted with what the chests conceal and knows what each soul earns; the One who protects the creation and subjects them to the best system and most complete management, observing everything with His sight, hearing and knowledge."},{"q":"In how many places is Ar-Raqeeb found in the Qur'aan?","a":"Three places."},{"q":"In which aayah are Ar-Raqeeb and Ash-Shaheed paired together?","a":"Maa'idah 5:117: '...You were the Watcher over them, and You are a Witness to all things.'"}]},{"chapter":23,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Muhaymin","arabic":"المُهَيْمِن","meaning":"The Ever-Watchful Witness"},{"translit":"Al-Muheet","arabic":"المُحِيط","meaning":"The All-Encompassing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Muhaymin The Ever-Watchful Witness is found in one place in the Qur'aan where Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Al-Muhaymin The Ever-Watchful Witness is the One who sees the hidden affairs, that which the chests conceal, the One who encompasses everything with His knowledge, the One who Witnesses the deeds of creation. The Watcher over their speech and deeds. Nothing is hidden from Him of their deeds at all. Not a speck of a seed in the earth or the heavens is hidden from Him."},{"type":"p","text":"As for the Name Al-Muheet The All-Encompassing, it is found in many places."},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Ever Encompassing all things.","ref":"Nisaa 4:126"},{"type":"quote","text":"Surely, Allah surrounds all that they do.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:120"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a Name that indicates Allaah encompasses everything through His knowledge, power and control."},{"type":"p","text":"Encompassing knowledge – not a speck of a seed from His creation is hidden from Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Encompassing power – nothing is impossible for Him to do in the earth or in the heaven."},{"type":"p","text":"Encompassing control – no one can escape or go missing from Him."},{"type":"quote","text":"O assembly of jinns and men! If you have power to pass beyond the zones of the heavens and the earth, then pass (them)! But you will never be able to pass them, except with authority (from Allah)!","ref":"Rahmaan 55:33"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that you will not be able to escape from Allaah's command or pre-destination because He encompasses everything by His knowledge, power and control."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Muhaymin is found in one place in the Qur'aan (Hashr 59:23).","Al-Muhaymin is the One who sees the hidden affairs and what the chests conceal, encompasses everything with His knowledge, and witnesses and watches over the speech and deeds of creation.","Al-Muheet is found in many places and indicates that Allaah encompasses everything through His knowledge, power and control.","Encompassing knowledge: not a speck of a seed is hidden from Him; encompassing power: nothing is impossible for Him; encompassing control: no one can escape or go missing from Him.","No one can escape Allaah's command or pre-destination because He encompasses everything (Rahmaan 55:33)."],"evidence":[{"text":"...the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"text":"And Allah is Ever Encompassing all things.","ref":"Nisaa 4:126"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Muhaymin mean?","a":"The One who sees the hidden affairs and what the chests conceal, encompasses everything with His knowledge, and witnesses the deeds of creation, the Watcher over their speech and deeds."},{"q":"Where is Al-Muhaymin found in the Qur'aan?","a":"In one place only: Hashr 59:23."},{"q":"What does Al-Muheet indicate?","a":"That Allaah encompasses everything through His knowledge, power and control."},{"q":"Explain the three aspects of Allaah's encompassing.","a":"Knowledge: not a speck of a seed is hidden from Him. Power: nothing is impossible for Him in the earth or heaven. Control: no one can escape or go missing from Him."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite to show that no one can escape Allaah's command?","a":"Rahmaan 55:33: 'O assembly of jinns and men! If you have power to pass beyond the zones of the heavens and the earth, then pass (them)!...'"}]},{"chapter":24,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Muqeet","arabic":"المُقِيت","meaning":"The All-Powerful Maintainer and Guardian"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Muqeet The All-Powerful Maintainer appears once in the Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Whosoever intercedes for a good cause will have the reward thereof, and whosoever intercedes for an evil cause will have a share in its burden. And Allah is Ever All-Able to do (and also an All-Witness to) everything.","ref":"Nisaa 4:85"},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Katheer said about: 'And Allah is Ever All-Able to do (and also an All-Witness to) everything.'"},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn 'Abbaas, 'Ataa, 'Atiyyah, Qataadah and Matar al-Warraaq said, 'Muqeeta' means 'Protector'."},{"type":"p","text":"Mujaahid said 'Witness' and in another narration by him he said 'Taker to account'."},{"type":"p","text":"Sa'eed bin Jubayr, Suddee and Ibn Zayd said 'All-Able'."},{"type":"p","text":"'Abdullaah bin Katheer said Al-Muqeet means 'The Lasting'."},{"type":"p","text":"Ad-Dahhaak said Al-Muqeet is Ar-Razzaaq 'The Provider'."},{"type":"p","text":"Nothing prevents this Name from encompassing all of these meanings so that it carries the meaning: The One whose knowledge encompasses the servants, their situations and what they need. He encompasses them with power as He is able to do all things, He protects, provides and helps them. The One who sustains the bodies with food and provision; and sustains the hearts of whomever He wishes of His servants with knowledge and faith."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Muqeet appears once in the Qur'aan, in Nisaa 4:85.","Ibn Katheer reported the explanations of the Salaf: 'Protector' (Ibn 'Abbaas and others), 'Witness' or 'Taker to account' (Mujaahid), 'All-Able' (Sa'eed bin Jubayr and others), 'The Lasting' ('Abdullaah bin Katheer), and 'The Provider' (Ad-Dahhaak).","Nothing prevents this Name from encompassing all of these meanings.","Al-Muqeet is the One whose knowledge encompasses the servants, their situations and needs, and who is able to do all things, protecting, providing for and helping them.","He sustains the bodies with food and provision, and sustains the hearts of whomever He wishes with knowledge and faith."],"evidence":[{"text":"And Allah is Ever All-Able to do (and also an All-Witness to) everything.","ref":"Nisaa 4:85"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Muqeet mean, combining the meanings mentioned?","a":"The One whose knowledge encompasses the servants, their situations and what they need; He encompasses them with power, protects, provides and helps them; He sustains the bodies with food and provision and the hearts of whomever He wishes with knowledge and faith."},{"q":"How many times does Al-Muqeet appear in the Qur'aan, and where?","a":"Once, in Nisaa 4:85."},{"q":"What did Ibn 'Abbaas, 'Ataa, 'Atiyyah, Qataadah and Matar al-Warraaq say 'Muqeeta' means?","a":"'Protector'."},{"q":"How did Ad-Dahhaak explain Al-Muqeet?","a":"He said Al-Muqeet is Ar-Razzaaq, 'The Provider'."},{"q":"What did Mujaahid say Al-Muqeet means?","a":"'Witness', and in another narration 'Taker to account'."}]},{"chapter":25,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Waasi'","arabic":"الوَاسِع","meaning":"The Vast One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Waasi' The Vast One is repeated in many places of the Qur'aan."},{"type":"p","text":"It means vast in Attributes and descriptions and what is connected to them in terms of no one being able to praise Him as He deserves; indeed He is as He praised Himself."},{"type":"p","text":"He is vast in might, authority and kingship. He is vast in grace and perfection, mighty in generosity and honour."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said in clarifying His vast knowledge and mercy:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Our Lord! You comprehend all things in mercy and knowledge,","ref":"Ghaafir 40:7"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said in clarifying His vast provision:"},{"type":"quote","text":"If they be poor, Allah will enrich them out of His Bounty. And Allah is All-Sufficient for His creatures' needs, All-Knowing","ref":"Noor 24:32"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said in clarifying His vast forgiveness:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah promises you Forgiveness from Himself and Bounty, and Allah is All-Sufficient for His creatures' needs, All-Knower.","ref":"Baqarah 2:268"},{"type":"p","text":"From the evidences of His Name Al-Waasi' is that He has made ease for the servants in their religion so He does not burden them with more than they can bear."},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah burdens not a person beyond his scope.","ref":"Baqarah 2:286"},{"type":"p","text":"All praises are due to Allaah for what He has given and made easy - pure, blessed and plentiful praises as our Lord likes and is pleased with."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Waasi' is repeated in many places of the Qur'aan.","It means vast in Attributes and descriptions, such that no one is able to praise Him as He deserves; He is as He praised Himself.","He is vast in might, authority and kingship, vast in grace and perfection, and mighty in generosity and honour.","The Qur'aan clarifies His vast knowledge and mercy (Ghaafir 40:7), vast provision (Noor 24:32) and vast forgiveness (Baqarah 2:268).","From the evidences of this Name is that He made the religion easy and does not burden the servants with more than they can bear (Baqarah 2:286)."],"evidence":[{"text":"Our Lord! You comprehend all things in mercy and knowledge.","ref":"Ghaafir 40:7"},{"text":"Allah burdens not a person beyond his scope.","ref":"Baqarah 2:286"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Waasi' mean?","a":"Vast in Attributes and descriptions, such that no one can praise Him as He deserves; He is vast in might, authority and kingship, vast in grace and perfection, mighty in generosity and honour."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite for Allaah's vast knowledge and mercy?","a":"Ghaafir 40:7: 'Our Lord! You comprehend all things in mercy and knowledge.'"},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite for Allaah's vast forgiveness?","a":"Baqarah 2:268: 'Allah promises you Forgiveness from Himself and Bounty...'"},{"q":"What is mentioned as one of the evidences of the Name Al-Waasi' in the religion?","a":"That He made ease for the servants in their religion and does not burden them beyond what they can bear: 'Allah burdens not a person beyond his scope.' [Baqarah 2:286]"}]},{"chapter":26,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Hafeedh","arabic":"الحَفِيظ","meaning":"The Guardian and Preserver"},{"translit":"Al-Haafidh","arabic":"الحَافِظ","meaning":"The Protector"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"So if you turn away, still I have conveyed the Message with which I was sent to you. My Lord will make another people succeed you, and you will not harm Him in the least. Surely, my Lord is Guardian over all things.\"","ref":"Hood 11:57"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily We: It is We Who have sent down the Dhikr (i.e. the Quran) and surely, We will guard it (from corruption).","ref":"Hijr 15:9"},{"type":"p","text":"These two great Names point to Allaah being described as protecting. Allaah's protection for His servants is of two types: general and specific."},{"type":"p","text":"The General Protection is His protection for them by facilitating their food, drink and air. It is also guiding them to that which will benefit them and to what He has decreed and ordained for them of the necessities and needs. This is general guidance about which Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"[Musa (Moses)] said: \"Our Lord is He Who gave to each thing its form and nature, then guided it aright.\"","ref":"Taha 20:50"},{"type":"p","text":"He protects them by repelling different types of disliked things, harms and evils from them. This protection is shared for the good person and the corrupt one and even the animals and other than them. Angels are appointed over humankind to protect them by Allaah's command as He says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"For each (person), there are angels in succession, before and behind him. They guard him by the Command of Allah.","ref":"Ra'd 13:11"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that they repel all that will harm them by Allaah's command which if it did reach them would harm them if it were not for Allaah's protection."},{"type":"p","text":"The Specific Protection is His protection for those of His allies who are close to Him. This is in addition to the previous general protection. He protects their faith from deviant doubts, devastating trials and destructive desires. He saves them from this. He protects them from their enemies of jinn and mankind."},{"type":"p","text":"He helps them against them and repels the schemes and plots of the enemies as He says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Truly, Allah defends those who believe. Verily! Allah likes not any treacherous ingrate to Allah [those who disobey Allah but obey Shaitan (Satan)].","ref":"Hajj 22:38"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah defends the servants according to the level of their faith."},{"type":"p","text":"Due to this the Prophet ﷺ said in his advice to Ibn 'Abbaas,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you\".","ref":"Jaami' at-Tirmidhee Vol. 4, Book 11, Hadith 2516"},{"type":"p","text":"This means preserve Allaah's commands by doing them: His prohibitions by avoiding them and His limits by not overstepping them and Allaah will protect you in your body, your religion, your wealth, your children and in everything that Allaah has given you."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Hafeedh and Al-Haafidh point to Allaah being described as protecting.","Allaah's protection for His servants is of two types: general and specific.","General protection: facilitating food, drink and air, guiding them to what benefits them, and repelling harms and evils; it is shared by the good and the corrupt and even the animals, and angels are appointed to guard humankind (Ra'd 13:11).","Specific protection is for His close allies: He protects their faith from deviant doubts, devastating trials and destructive desires, and protects them from their enemies of jinn and mankind.","Allaah defends the servants according to the level of their faith, as in the hadeeth \"Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you\"."],"evidence":[{"text":"Surely, my Lord is Guardian over all things.","ref":"Hood 11:57"},{"text":"Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you.","ref":"Jaami' at-Tirmidhee Vol. 4, Book 11, Hadith 2516"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do the Names Al-Hafeedh (The Guardian and Preserver) and Al-Haafidh (The Protector) point to?","a":"Allaah being described as protecting."},{"q":"What are the two types of Allaah's protection for His servants?","a":"General protection (food, drink, air, guidance to what benefits them, repelling harms, shared by all including animals) and specific protection for His close allies (protecting their faith from doubts, trials and desires, and protecting them from their enemies)."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite about the angels who guard each person?","a":"Ra'd 13:11: 'For each (person), there are angels in succession, before and behind him. They guard him by the Command of Allah.'"},{"q":"What advice did the Prophet ﷺ give Ibn 'Abbaas related to this Name, and what does it mean?","a":"\"Be mindful of Allah and He will protect you\": preserve Allaah's commands by doing them, His prohibitions by avoiding them and His limits by not overstepping them, and He will protect you in your body, religion, wealth, children and all He has given you."},{"q":"According to what does Allaah defend His servants?","a":"According to the level of their faith."}]},{"chapter":27,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Walee","arabic":"الوَلِيّ","meaning":"The Protector"},{"translit":"Al-Mawlaa","arabic":"المَوْلَى","meaning":"The Protector and Supporter"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Both Names are repeatedly found in the Noble Qur'aan. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Or have they taken (for worship) Auliya' (guardians, supporters, helpers, protectors, etc.) besides Him? But Allah, He Alone is the Wali (Protector, etc.). And it is He Who gives life to the dead, and He is Able to do all things.","ref":"Shooraa 42:9"},{"type":"quote","text":"and hold fast to Allah [i.e. have confidence in Allah, and depend upon Him in all your affairs] He is your Maula (Patron, Lord, etc.), what an Excellent Maula (Patron, Lord, etc.) and what an Excellent Helper!","ref":"Hajj 22:78"},{"type":"quote","text":"Nay, Allah is your Maula (Patron, Lord, Helper and Protector, etc.), and He is the Best of helpers.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:150"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's protection and support over His servants are of two categories:"},{"type":"p","text":"General Guardianship is His management for all beings and His decree over the servants in what He wills of good and bad, benefit and harm. It is a confirmation of the meaning that all of the kingdom is Allaah's. All of the servants obey His control, there is no escape for anyone from His Will being executed or His Ability encompassing them. This matter includes the believer and the disbeliever, the good and the bad, Allaah indicates this by saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Then they are returned to Allah, their Maula [True Master (God), the Just Lord (to reward them)]. Surely, His is the judgement and He is the Swiftest in taking account.","ref":"An'aam 6:62"},{"type":"p","text":"Specific Guardianship and Support. This is the category most found in the Noble Qur'aan and in the Prophetic Sunnah. It is the great guardianship and noble support. Allaah grants this specifically to His believing servants, His obedient party and God fearing allies."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah clarified in the Noble Qur'aan that this great guardianship is not achieved except with true faith and God consciousness (taqwa) of Allaah in secret and in the open, striving in coming close to Him through the obligatory duties of Islaam and the desired aspects of the religion. As Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"No doubt! Verily, the Auliya' of Allah [i.e. those who believe in the Oneness of Allah and fear Allah much (abstain from all kinds of sins and evil deeds which he has forbidden), and love Allah much (perform all kinds of good deeds which He has ordained)], no fear shall come upon them nor shall they grieve. Those who believed (in the Oneness of Allah - Islamic Monotheism), and used to fear Allah much.","ref":"Yoonus 10:62-63"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Walee and Al-Mawlaa are both repeatedly found in the Noble Qur'aan.","Allaah's protection and support over His servants are of two categories: general and specific.","General guardianship is His management of all beings and His decree over them in good and bad, benefit and harm; it includes the believer and the disbeliever.","Specific guardianship and support is the category most found in the Qur'aan and Sunnah, granted specifically to His believing, obedient and God-fearing allies.","This specific guardianship is only achieved with true faith and taqwa in secret and in the open, and striving to come close to Him through the obligatory duties and the desired aspects of the religion."],"evidence":[{"text":"But Allah, He Alone is the Wali (Protector, etc.).","ref":"Shooraa 42:9"},{"text":"Verily, the Auliya' of Allah... no fear shall come upon them nor shall they grieve. Those who believed, and used to fear Allah much.","ref":"Yoonus 10:62-63"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do Al-Walee and Al-Mawlaa mean?","a":"Al-Walee: The Protector; Al-Mawlaa: The Protector and Supporter."},{"q":"What is Allaah's general guardianship?","a":"His management of all beings and His decree over the servants in what He wills of good and bad, benefit and harm; it includes the believer and disbeliever, the good and the bad."},{"q":"Who is granted Allaah's specific guardianship and support, and how is it achieved?","a":"His believing servants, obedient party and God-fearing allies; it is achieved only with true faith and taqwa in secret and in the open, and striving to come close to Him through the obligatory duties and desired aspects of the religion."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite for the specific guardianship of Allaah's allies?","a":"Yoonus 10:62-63: 'No doubt! Verily, the Auliya' of Allah... no fear shall come upon them nor shall they grieve.'"},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite for the general guardianship?","a":"An'aam 6:62: 'Then they are returned to Allah, their Maula...'"}]},{"chapter":28,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Awwal","arabic":"الأَوَّل","meaning":"The First"},{"translit":"Al-Aakhir","arabic":"الآخِر","meaning":"The Last"},{"translit":"Adh-Dhaahir","arabic":"الظَّاهِر","meaning":"The Uppermost"},{"translit":"Al-Baatin","arabic":"البَاطِن","meaning":"The Closest One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These four Names are found together in one place in the Noble Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is the First (nothing is before Him) and the Last (nothing is after Him), the Most High (nothing is above Him) and the Most Near (nothing is nearer than Him). And He is the All-Knower of everything.","ref":"Hadeed 57:3"},{"type":"p","text":"The best explanation that clarifies the meanings of the Beautiful Names is found in the Prophetic Sunnah in the Prophet ﷺ calling upon his Lord with these Names. This calling upon Allaah includes a clarification of the meanings of these Names and what they indicate."},{"type":"p","text":"Abu Hurairah said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to order that when one of us goes to sleep, he should say: 'O Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earths, and our Lord, and the Lord of everything, splitter of the seed-grain and date-stone, Revealer of the Tawrah, the Injil and the Qur'an. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every evil that You are holding by the forelock. You are the First, there is nothing before You, You are the Last, there is nothing after You, Adh-Dhaahir, there is nothing above you, and Al-Baatin, there is nothing below You. Relieve me of my debt, and enrich me from poverty'.\"","ref":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3400"},{"type":"p","text":"The Prophet ﷺ made clear in this comprehensive du'aa the meaning of each Name and negated what nullifies it. This is the highest level of clarification."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Awwal, Al-Aakhir, Adh-Dhaahir and Al-Baatin are found together in one place in the Qur'aan: Hadeed 57:3.","The best explanation of the meanings of the Beautiful Names is found in the Prophetic Sunnah, in the Prophet ﷺ calling upon his Lord with these Names.","Al-Awwal: there is nothing before Him; Al-Aakhir: there is nothing after Him.","Adh-Dhaahir: there is nothing above Him; Al-Baatin: there is nothing below Him (in the hadeeth), and nothing is nearer than Him (in the aayah's translation).","In the du'aa before sleeping, the Prophet ﷺ made clear the meaning of each Name and negated what nullifies it, which is the highest level of clarification."],"evidence":[{"text":"He is the First (nothing is before Him) and the Last (nothing is after Him), the Most High (nothing is above Him) and the Most Near (nothing is nearer than Him).","ref":"Hadeed 57:3"},{"text":"You are the First, there is nothing before You, You are the Last, there is nothing after You, Adh-Dhaahir, there is nothing above you, and Al-Baatin, there is nothing below You.","ref":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3400"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Awwal mean?","a":"The First: there is nothing before Him."},{"q":"What does Al-Aakhir mean?","a":"The Last: there is nothing after Him."},{"q":"What do Adh-Dhaahir and Al-Baatin mean?","a":"Adh-Dhaahir (The Uppermost): there is nothing above Him. Al-Baatin (The Closest One): there is nothing below Him / nothing is nearer than Him."},{"q":"In which aayah are these four Names found together?","a":"Hadeed 57:3."},{"q":"Where is the best explanation of these Names found, and when was the du'aa said?","a":"In the Prophetic Sunnah: the du'aa the Prophet ﷺ ordered to be said when going to sleep (narrated by Abu Hurairah, Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3400)."}]},{"chapter":29,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Hakeem","arabic":"الحَكِيم","meaning":"The All-Wise"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Hakeem The All-Wise is found in the Qur'aan nearly a hundred times. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And He is the Irresistible, above His slaves, and He is the All-Wise, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:18"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Almighty, All-Wise.","ref":"Baqarah 2:228"},{"type":"p","text":"This great Name affirms perfect rule for Allaah and perfect wisdom. As for perfect wisdom, then it is affirmation of wisdom for Allaah in His creation, command and legislation, where He places things in their rightful places and in their correct station. No one directs a question or voices criticism of His wisdom."},{"type":"p","text":"As for perfect rule, it is affirmation of rule for Allaah alone. He rules between His servants with what He wishes. He decrees for them what He wills. Nothing can repel His rule or change His decree."},{"type":"quote","text":"The decision is only for Allah.","ref":"An'aam 6:57"},{"type":"quote","text":"and He makes none to share in His Decision and His Rule.","ref":"Kahf 18:26"},{"type":"p","text":"No one can ask for reconsideration of Allaah's Rule like people do amongst themselves in their rulings."},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah judges, there is none to put back His Judgement and He is Swift at reckoning.","ref":"Ra'd 13:41"},{"type":"p","text":"His rule in His creation is applied with no one to repel or change it."},{"type":"p","text":"Affirming rule for Allaah comprises affirmation of all Allaah's Beautiful Names and Lofty Attributes because Allaah is not a Ruler except that He Hears, Sees, Knows, is All-Aware, Speaks, Directs affairs and so on from His Names and Attributes."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Hakeem is found in the Qur'aan nearly a hundred times.","This Name affirms two things for Allaah: perfect rule and perfect wisdom.","Perfect wisdom means Allaah places things in their rightful places and correct station in His creation, command and legislation, and no one directs a question or criticism at His wisdom.","Perfect rule means rule belongs to Allaah alone; nothing can repel His rule or change His decree, and no one can ask for reconsideration of it.","Affirming rule for Allaah comprises affirming all His Names and Attributes, because He is not a Ruler except that He Hears, Sees, Knows, Speaks and directs affairs."],"evidence":[{"text":"And He is the Irresistible, above His slaves, and He is the All-Wise, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:18"},{"text":"And Allah judges, there is none to put back His Judgement and He is Swift at reckoning.","ref":"Ra'd 13:41"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Hakeem mean?","a":"The All-Wise; the Name affirms for Allaah perfect rule and perfect wisdom."},{"q":"How often is Al-Hakeem found in the Qur'aan?","a":"Nearly a hundred times."},{"q":"What is meant by affirming perfect wisdom for Allaah?","a":"Affirming wisdom for Him in His creation, command and legislation, where He places things in their rightful places and correct station; no one directs a question or criticism at His wisdom."},{"q":"Why does affirming rule for Allaah comprise affirming all His Names and Attributes?","a":"Because Allaah is not a Ruler except that He Hears, Sees, Knows, is All-Aware, Speaks, Directs affairs and so on from His Names and Attributes."}]},{"chapter":30,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Ghanee","arabic":"الغَنِيّ","meaning":"The Rich free of all need"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name appears in 18 places in the Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And your Lord is Rich (Free of all wants), full of Mercy","ref":"An'aam 6:133"},{"type":"quote","text":"O mankind! it is you who stand in need of Allah, but Allah is Rich (Free of all wants and needs), Worthy of all praise.","ref":"Faatir 35:15"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah is Rich in His Self. He is completely and absolutely Free of need in every aspect and consideration due to His Perfection and Perfection of His Attributes which no deficiency from any angle can touch."},{"type":"p","text":"From the completeness of His Richness is that the obedience of the obedient does not benefit Him nor the disobedience of the disobedient harm Him. If all of the creation together on earth believed, it would not increase Allaah's Kingdom in anything. If they all disbelieved it would not decrease His Kingdom in anything."},{"type":"p","text":"Whoever knows his Lord with this mighty description will know his own self. Whoever knows his Lord is absolutely free of need, knows that he himself has absolute need and poverty. Whoever knows his Lord has complete power, knows that he himself has complete inability. Whoever knows his Lord has complete Might, knows that he himself has complete destitution. Whoever knows his Lord has complete knowledge and wisdom knows that he himself is ignorant. The fruit of knowing this information is that the servant knows his poverty in front of Allaah which is a means of happiness and success for him in this Life and the Next."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Ghanee appears in 18 places in the Qur'aan.","Allaah is Rich in His Self, completely and absolutely free of need in every aspect, due to His Perfection and the Perfection of His Attributes.","From the completeness of His Richness, the obedience of the obedient does not benefit Him and the disobedience of the disobedient does not harm Him.","If all the creation believed it would not increase His Kingdom in anything, and if they all disbelieved it would not decrease it in anything.","Whoever knows his Lord is absolutely free of need knows his own absolute need and poverty, and knowing this poverty before Allaah is a means of happiness and success in this Life and the Next."],"evidence":[{"text":"O mankind! it is you who stand in need of Allah, but Allah is Rich (Free of all wants and needs), Worthy of all praise.","ref":"Faatir 35:15"},{"text":"And your Lord is Rich (Free of all wants), full of Mercy","ref":"An'aam 6:133"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Ghanee mean?","a":"The Rich free of all need: Allaah is Rich in His Self, completely and absolutely free of need in every aspect and consideration."},{"q":"In how many places does Al-Ghanee appear in the Qur'aan?","a":"In 18 places."},{"q":"What is from the completeness of Allaah's Richness?","a":"That the obedience of the obedient does not benefit Him nor the disobedience of the disobedient harm Him; all creation believing would not increase His Kingdom, nor would all disbelieving decrease it."},{"q":"What is the fruit of knowing that Allaah is Al-Ghanee?","a":"The servant knows his own poverty in front of Allaah, which is a means of happiness and success for him in this Life and the Next."}]},{"chapter":31,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Kareem","arabic":"الكَرِيم","meaning":"The Generous"},{"translit":"Al-Akram","arabic":"الأَكْرَم","meaning":"The Most Generous"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Kareem is found in three places in the Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And whoever is grateful, truly, his gratitude is for (the good of) his ownself, and whoever is ungrateful, (he is ungrateful only for the loss of his ownself). Certainly! My Lord is Rich (Free of all wants), Bountiful.\"","ref":"Naml 27:40"},{"type":"quote","text":"O man! What has made you careless concerning your Lord, the Most Generous?","ref":"Infitaar 82:6"},{"type":"quote","text":"So Exalted be Allah, the True King, La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Lord of the Supreme Throne!","ref":"Mu'minoon 23:116"},{"type":"p","text":"For those who read the word 'al kareem' with a dammah it refers to an attribute of the Lord."},{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Akram is found in one place,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Read! And your Lord is the Most Generous.","ref":"Alaq 96:3"},{"type":"p","text":"It indicates the affirmation of generosity describing Allaah. The word 'Al-Karam' is all-encompassing to mean good virtues and praiseworthy descriptions - not only the meaning of 'giving'."},{"type":"p","text":"Giving is from the completion of its meaning. Due to this the people of knowledge have many sayings regarding the meaning of this Name:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Much good and giving."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Constantly doing good."},{"type":"p","text":"3. The One who has a mighty status and grand state."},{"type":"p","text":"4. One who is removed from having deficiencies and defects."},{"type":"p","text":"5. The One who is generous, the provider of blessings, the One who gives from His grace."},{"type":"p","text":"6. The One who gives not expecting anything in return."},{"type":"p","text":"7. The One who gives without a reason."},{"type":"p","text":"8. The One who gives the person who needs and the person who does not need."},{"type":"p","text":"9. The One who promises and fulfils it."},{"type":"p","text":"10. The One to whom every big and small need is raised to."},{"type":"p","text":"11. The One who does not abandon someone seeking nearness to Him nor One who leaves someone who calls upon Him."},{"type":"p","text":"12. The One who overlooks sins and forgives bad deeds."},{"type":"p","text":"There is more of what has been said about the meaning of this great Name. All of this is correct as this Name is from the Beautiful Names of Allaah that encompass multiple meanings not only one."},{"type":"p","text":"If a person considers everything that has been said about this Name, he will know that what is due to Allaah of this (from lofty meanings and honourable descriptions) cannot be counted and known."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Kareem is found in three places in the Qur'aan, and Al-Akram in one place (Alaq 96:3).","These Names affirm generosity as a description of Allaah.","The word 'Al-Karam' is all-encompassing, meaning good virtues and praiseworthy descriptions, not only 'giving'; giving is from the completion of its meaning.","The people of knowledge gave many meanings, such as much good and giving, constantly doing good, giving without expecting anything in return, fulfilling promises, and overlooking sins and forgiving bad deeds.","All these meanings are correct, as this Name encompasses multiple meanings, and what is due to Allaah of them cannot be counted."],"evidence":[{"text":"O man! What has made you careless concerning your Lord, the Most Generous?","ref":"Infitaar 82:6"},{"text":"Read! And your Lord is the Most Generous.","ref":"Alaq 96:3"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Kareem mean?","a":"The Generous; it affirms generosity for Allaah, and 'Al-Karam' encompasses good virtues and praiseworthy descriptions, not only giving."},{"q":"What does Al-Akram mean, and where is it found?","a":"The Most Generous; it is found in one place: \"Read! And your Lord is the Most Generous.\" [Alaq 96:3]."},{"q":"How many times is Al-Kareem found in the Qur'aan?","a":"In three places."},{"q":"Give some of the meanings the people of knowledge mentioned for Al-Kareem.","a":"Much good and giving; constantly doing good; the One with a mighty status; removed from deficiencies; giving without expecting return; giving without a reason; promising and fulfilling; the One to whom every need is raised; overlooking sins and forgiving bad deeds."},{"q":"Why are all the different sayings about Al-Kareem's meaning correct?","a":"Because this Name is from the Beautiful Names of Allaah that encompass multiple meanings, not only one."}]},{"chapter":32,"names":[{"translit":"As-Salaam","arabic":"السَّلَام","meaning":"The One Free from all Defects"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As-Salaam is found once in the Noble Qur'aan in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of this honourable Name is the One free from every defect and deficiency due to Him being perfect in His Self, His Attributes and His Actions. Allaah is As-Salaam The One Free from all defects, Al-Haqq The True One in every consideration. Salaam in His Self from every defect or deficiency that could be imagined: Salaam in His Attributes from every deficiency or defect, Salaam in His Actions from deficiency, defect, evil, oppression and doing things without wisdom. He is Salaam from having a partner or son. He is Salaam from having a match, equal, parallel or similar. Salaam from having a rival or associate."},{"type":"p","text":"As-Salaam is a Name including all the Attributes of Allaah. Each of Allaah's Attributes is Salaam, free from defect and deficiency. Ibnul Qayyim wrote about this matter in detail and at length with strong composed speech. Then he concluded by saying, \"Reflect upon how Allaah's Name As-Salaam comprises everything that He is removed from. How many people have memorized this Name and do not know what it entails of these hidden secrets and meanings.\""}],"keyPoints":["As-Salaam is found once in the Qur'aan, in Hashr 59:23.","It means the One free from every defect and deficiency, due to Him being perfect in His Self, His Attributes and His Actions.","He is Salaam in His Actions from deficiency, defect, evil, oppression and doing things without wisdom.","He is Salaam from having a partner or son, and from having a match, equal, parallel, similar, rival or associate.","As-Salaam includes all of Allaah's Attributes, since each of His Attributes is free from defect and deficiency."],"evidence":[{"text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security...","ref":"Hashr 59:23"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Salaam mean?","a":"The One free from every defect and deficiency, due to Him being perfect in His Self, His Attributes and His Actions."},{"q":"How many times is As-Salaam found in the Qur'aan, and where?","a":"Once, in Allaah's saying in Hashr 59:23."},{"q":"From what is Allaah Salaam in His Actions?","a":"From deficiency, defect, evil, oppression and doing things without wisdom."},{"q":"What did Ibnul Qayyim conclude about the Name As-Salaam?","a":"\"Reflect upon how Allaah's Name As-Salaam comprises everything that He is removed from. How many people have memorized this Name and do not know what it entails of these hidden secrets and meanings.\""}]},{"chapter":33,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Quddoos","arabic":"القُدُّوس","meaning":"The Pure and Perfect"},{"translit":"As-Subbooh","arabic":"السُّبُّوح","meaning":"The Supremely Glorious"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As for His Name Al-Quddoos The Pure and Perfect, it is found in the Qur'aan twice."},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"quote","text":"Whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is on the earth glorifies Allah, the King (of everything), the Holy, the Almighty, the All-Wise.","ref":"Jumu'ah 62:1"},{"type":"p","text":"As-Subbooh The Supremely Glorious is found in the Sunnah and that is what Muslim narrated in his Saheeh from 'Aa'ishah the Mother of the believers that the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ used to say in his rukoo and sujood:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Perfect, Blessed, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit.","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 487a"},{"type":"p","text":"In the hadeeth the Prophet ﷺ combined tasbeeh (glorifying - Subbooh) and taqdees (pure - Quddoos) as it is combined in Allaah's saying regarding the mention of the angels' taqdees of Allaah,"},{"type":"quote","text":"while we glorify You with praises and thanks (Exalted be You above all that they associate with You as partners) and sanctify You.\"","ref":"Baqarah 2:30"},{"type":"p","text":"It should be known here that tasbeeh and taqdees of Allaah is freeing Allaah from every evil and defect whilst affirming every praiseworthy perfect attribute in a manner suitable to His Majesty."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykhul Islaam ibn Taymiyyah said, \"The order of making tasbeeh of Allaah consists of freeing Him of every defect and evil and affirming everything praiseworthy which is praised. This consists of freeing Him from defects, praising Him, magnifying Him and singling Him out for worship.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Through this it is known that the people of innovation such as the Mu'attilah deny the Attributes and do not affirm them. They deny their reality and their meanings saying that they are glorifying Allaah and removing defects from Him. In reality it is more like criticising and denying, deviation and lies and not glorifying Allaah or removing defects from Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Rajab said about the meaning of Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"So glorify the Praises of your Lord","ref":"Nasr 110:3"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Glorify Him with what He praised Himself with. Therefore not every glorification (tasbeeh) is praiseworthy just as the glorification of the (deviant) Mu'tazilah who negate many of the Attributes for example.\""},{"type":"p","text":"He said, 'not every glorification is praiseworthy' which is extremely important speech. So glorifying Allaah by denying and disbelieving in His Attributes and not affirming them is an action that the doer is not praised for. Instead, he is severely blameworthy. With this he is not of those who glorify Allaah with His praises. He is of those who deny, negate and disbelieve. They are those whom Allaah has freed Himself from their speech and denied them by saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Glorified be your Lord, the Lord of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they attribute unto Him! And peace be on the Messengers! And all the praise and thanks be to Allah, Lord of the 'Alamin (mankind, jinns and all that exists).","ref":"Saafaat 37:180-182"},{"type":"p","text":"He glorified and freed Himself from what the opposers of the Prophets described Him with. He sent peace upon the Messengers for the peace and safety that they spoke about in negating deficiency and defect from being attributed to Him as Allaah's right."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Quddoos is found in the Qur'aan twice (Hashr 59:23 and Jumu'ah 62:1); As-Subbooh is found in the Sunnah, in the hadeeth of 'Aa'ishah in Saheeh Muslim.","The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his rukoo and sujood: \"Perfect, Blessed, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit\", combining tasbeeh (Subbooh) and taqdees (Quddoos).","Tasbeeh and taqdees of Allaah is freeing Him from every evil and defect whilst affirming every praiseworthy perfect attribute in a manner suitable to His Majesty.","The Mu'attilah who deny the Attributes claiming to glorify Allaah are in reality criticising, denying and deviating, not glorifying Him.","Ibn Rajab said not every glorification is praiseworthy, such as that of the Mu'tazilah who negate many of the Attributes."],"evidence":[{"text":"Whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is on the earth glorifies Allah, the King (of everything), the Holy, the Almighty, the All-Wise.","ref":"Jumu'ah 62:1"},{"text":"Perfect, Blessed, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit. (said by the Prophet ﷺ in his rukoo and sujood)","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 487a"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Quddoos mean, and how often is it found in the Qur'aan?","a":"The Pure and Perfect; it is found in the Qur'aan twice."},{"q":"What does As-Subbooh mean, and where is it found?","a":"The Supremely Glorious; it is found in the Sunnah, in the hadeeth of 'Aa'ishah in Saheeh Muslim that the Prophet ﷺ used to say in his rukoo and sujood: \"Perfect, Blessed, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit.\""},{"q":"What is tasbeeh and taqdees of Allaah?","a":"Freeing Allaah from every evil and defect whilst affirming every praiseworthy perfect attribute in a manner suitable to His Majesty."},{"q":"What did Ibn Rajab say about the meaning of \"So glorify the Praises of your Lord\"?","a":"\"Glorify Him with what He praised Himself with. Therefore not every glorification (tasbeeh) is praiseworthy just as the glorification of the (deviant) Mu'tazilah who negate many of the Attributes for example.\""}]},{"chapter":34,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Hameed","arabic":"الحَمِيد","meaning":"The Praiseworthy"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is repeatedly found in the Noble Qur'aan seventeen times. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"O mankind! It is you who stand in need of Allah, but Allah is Rich (Free of all wants and needs), Worthy of all praise.","ref":"Faatir 35:15"},{"type":"quote","text":"And they are guided (in this world) unto goodly speech (i.e. La ilaha ill-Allah, Alhamdu lillah, recitation of the Quran, etc.) and they are guided to the Path of Him (i.e. Allah's Religion of Islamic Monotheism), Who is Worthy of all praises.","ref":"Hajj 22:24"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Al-Hameed is the One who deserves all praises. Praised in His Self, His Names and His Attributes. Praise is the most expansive of the Attributes and the most comprehensive of what is to be praised and the greatest praise. All the Names of Allaah are praise. His Rulings are praise, His Justice is praise, His revenge over His enemies is praise. His Grace and Goodness to His allies is praise. Creation and command is established by His praise and the objective and the appearance of it is His praise. His praise is the spirit of everything. Everything is established with His praise. His praise runs through whatever exists and its effects appear as a witnessed command by mental and visual perception."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykhul Islaam Ibn Taymiyyah said, \"There are two types of praise: praise due to His good treatment to His servants and this is from gratefulness. Praise for what He Himself deserves from descriptions of His Perfection. This type of praise is only for one who is described as having perfect attributes.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah began His Book with praise. He began some of the Suwar of the Qur'aan with praise. He began His creation with praise and concluded it with praise. So He deserves praise firstly and lastly. For Him is apparent and hidden gratefulness. He is Al-Hameed Al-Majeed - The All-Praiseworthy, The Glorious."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Hameed is found in the Noble Qur'aan seventeen times.","Al-Hameed means the One who deserves all praises, praised in His Self, His Names and His Attributes.","All of Allaah's Names, Rulings, Justice, revenge over His enemies, and Grace to His allies are praise; His praise is the spirit of everything.","Ibn Taymiyyah said there are two types of praise: praise for His good treatment of His servants (from gratefulness), and praise for what He Himself deserves of descriptions of Perfection.","Allaah began His Book, some Suwar, and His creation with praise, and concluded creation with praise, so He deserves praise firstly and lastly."],"evidence":[{"text":"O mankind! It is you who stand in need of Allah, but Allah is Rich (Free of all wants and needs), Worthy of all praise.","ref":"Faatir 35:15"},{"text":"...and they are guided to the Path of Him (i.e. Allah's Religion of Islamic Monotheism), Who is Worthy of all praises.","ref":"Hajj 22:24"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Hameed mean?","a":"The Praiseworthy: the One who deserves all praises, praised in His Self, His Names and His Attributes."},{"q":"How many times is Al-Hameed found in the Qur'aan?","a":"Seventeen times."},{"q":"What are the two types of praise according to Shaykhul Islaam Ibn Taymiyyah?","a":"Praise due to His good treatment of His servants, which is from gratefulness; and praise for what He Himself deserves from descriptions of His Perfection, which is only for one described with perfect attributes."},{"q":"Why does Allaah deserve praise firstly and lastly?","a":"Because He began His Book with praise, began some Suwar with praise, and began His creation with praise and concluded it with praise."}]},{"chapter":35,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Majeed","arabic":"المَجِيد","meaning":"The One Perfect in Glory and Honour"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Majeed The One Perfect in Glory and Honour is a magnificent Name that appears in the Book of Allaah twice."},{"type":"quote","text":"The Mercy of Allah and His Blessings be on you, O the family [of Ibrahim (Abraham)]. Surely, He (Allah) is All-Praiseworthy, All-Glorious.\"","ref":"Hood 11:73"},{"type":"quote","text":"And He is Oft-Forgiving, full of love (towards the pious who are real true believers of Islamic Monotheism), Owner of the throne, the Glorious.","ref":"Burooj 85:14-15"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Majeed(u) is describing Allaah. It has been recited al-majeed(i) which describes Allaah's throne."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Majeed is one of Allaah's Beautiful Names indicating many descriptions and is not confined to only one meaning. Al-Majeed carries the meaning of 'vast with magnificent descriptions'. Having many noble descriptions. Al-Majeed refers back to numerous mighty vast descriptions. It refers back to His mighty kingdom and authority. It refers back to singling Him out with absolute perfection, honour and beauty of which the servants cannot comprehend anything."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah glorified Himself in His Book in many aayaat. Indeed the whole of the Noble Qur'aan is glory and honour for Allaah. There is not an aayah in the Qur'aan that does not mention anything of Allaah's Beautiful Names, Lofty Attributes and Wise Actions. Aayatul Kursee the greatest aayah in the Noble Qur'aan is one that includes these. It contains five of Allaah's Beautiful Names and over twenty of Allaah's Attributes. Sooratul Ikhlaas equals a third of the Qur'aan. It is 'sincerity' because it clarifies Allaah's Beautiful Names and Mighty Attributes. Sooratul Faatihah is the greatest Soorah in the Noble Qur'aan. Half of it is praise and glorifying Allaah. Muslim recorded in his Saheeh, Abu Hurayrah reported that he had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declare that Allah the Exalted had said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"I have divided the prayer into two halves between Me and My servant, and My servant will receive what he asks. When the servant says: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the universe, Allah the Most High says: My servant has praised Me. And when he (the servant) says: The Most Compassionate, the Merciful, Allah the Most High says: My servant has lauded Me. And when he (the servant) says: Master of the Day of judgement, He remarks: My servant has glorified Me.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 395a"},{"type":"p","text":"When a person praying sits for the tashahhud he praises and glorifies Allaah and he ends it by saying إنك حميد مجيد Indeed You are All-Praiseworthy, Perfect in glory and honour."},{"type":"p","text":"So the beginning of the prayer is praise and glorification and the end of the prayer is praise and glorification. Indeed all of it establishes praise and glorification for The All-Praiseworthy, the One Perfect in Glory and Honour Who deserves praise and glorification."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Majeed appears in the Book of Allaah twice (Hood 11:73 and Burooj 85:15).","Al-Majeed is not confined to one meaning; it carries the meaning of 'vast with magnificent descriptions', having many noble descriptions.","It refers back to His mighty kingdom and authority, and to singling Him out with absolute perfection, honour and beauty which the servants cannot comprehend.","The whole Qur'aan is glory and honour for Allaah; Aayatul Kursee, the greatest aayah, contains five of His Names and over twenty of His Attributes.","The prayer begins with praise and glorification (Al-Faatihah) and ends with it in the tashahhud: 'Indeed You are All-Praiseworthy, Perfect in glory and honour'."],"evidence":[{"text":"Surely, He (Allah) is All-Praiseworthy, All-Glorious.","ref":"Hood 11:73"},{"text":"\"...And when he (the servant) says: Master of the Day of judgement, He remarks: My servant has glorified Me.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 395a"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Majeed mean?","a":"The One Perfect in Glory and Honour; it carries the meaning of 'vast with magnificent descriptions', having many noble descriptions."},{"q":"How many times does Al-Majeed appear in the Qur'aan?","a":"Twice."},{"q":"How many Names and Attributes does Aayatul Kursee contain, according to the author?","a":"Five of Allaah's Beautiful Names and over twenty of His Attributes."},{"q":"What does Allaah say when the servant says \"Master of the Day of judgement\" in the prayer?","a":"\"My servant has glorified Me.\" (Saheeh Muslim)"},{"q":"With what words does the person praying end the tashahhud, showing the end of the prayer is praise and glorification?","a":"إنك حميد مجيد - Indeed You are All-Praiseworthy, Perfect in glory and honour."}]},{"chapter":36,"names":[{"translit":"Ash-Shakoor","arabic":"الشَّكُور","meaning":"The One Most ready to appreciate and reward abundantly"},{"translit":"Ash-Shaakir","arabic":"الشَّاكِر","meaning":"The Appreciative"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Ash-Shakoor The One Most ready to appreciate and reward abundantly is found in four places in the Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"That He may pay them their wages in full, and give them (even) more, out of His Grace. Verily! He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (good deeds and to recompense).","ref":"Faatir 35:30"},{"type":"quote","text":"And they will say: \"All the praises and thanks be to Allah, Who has removed from us (all) grief. Verily, our Lord is indeed Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (good deeds and to recompense).","ref":"Faatir 35:34"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (the deeds of those who are obedient to Him).","ref":"Shooraa 42:23"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Most Ready to appreciate and to reward, Most Forbearing","ref":"Taghaabun 64:17"},{"type":"p","text":"Ash-Shaakir The Appreciative occurs in two places,"},{"type":"quote","text":"then verily, Allah is All-Recogniser, All-Knower.","ref":"Baqarah 2:158"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Ever All-Appreciative (of good), All-Knowing.","ref":"Nisaa 4:147"},{"type":"p","text":"All these six places where the two Names occur are in the context of Allaah giving by rewarding the obedient people, giving and multiplying the rewards and increasing them in grace. This is what clarifies to us the meaning of these two Names."},{"type":"p","text":"Ash-Shaakir The Appreciative is:"},{"type":"p","text":"• The One who does not allow a good deed by a good doer to be lost instead He multiplies the reward without account."},{"type":"p","text":"• The One who accepts small good deeds and rewards them with many rewards, abundant giving and vast gifts."},{"type":"p","text":"• The One who multiplies the deeds of the sincere people without measure."},{"type":"p","text":"• He is appreciative of those who are grateful."},{"type":"p","text":"• He remembers those who remember Him."},{"type":"p","text":"• Whoever draws close to Him by a hand span, He draws close to him by an arm's length. Whoever comes close to Him by an arm's length He draws close to him by a fathom."},{"type":"p","text":"• Whoever comes with a good deed He increases it in goodness and He gives him from Himself a mighty reward."},{"type":"p","text":"In the previous aayaat Al-Ghafoor The Forgiving and Ash-Shakoor The One Most ready to appreciate and reward abundantly are combined. So He forgives all sins no matter how great. He does not make a sin too great to be forgiven. Ash-Shakoor The One most ready to appreciate every deed even if it be small, even if it is the weight of a seed. Due to this it is not allowed for a Muslim to despair of Allaah's forgiveness for sins no matter how great. Just as it is not allowed to look down upon any good deed no matter how small because indeed the Lord is Ghafoor Forgiving, Shakoor Appreciative."}],"keyPoints":["Ash-Shakoor is found in four places in the Qur'aan and Ash-Shaakir in two places.","All six places are in the context of Allaah rewarding the obedient, multiplying their rewards and increasing them in grace, which clarifies the meaning of these two Names.","Ash-Shaakir is the One who does not let a good deed be lost, accepts small good deeds and rewards them abundantly, and multiplies the deeds of the sincere without measure.","Whoever draws close to Him by a hand span, He draws close to him by an arm's length, and whoever comes close by an arm's length, He draws close by a fathom.","Al-Ghafoor and Ash-Shakoor are combined: He forgives all sins no matter how great and appreciates every deed even if small, so a Muslim must not despair of forgiveness nor look down on any good deed."],"evidence":[{"text":"That He may pay them their wages in full, and give them (even) more, out of His Grace. Verily! He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (good deeds and to recompense).","ref":"Faatir 35:30"},{"text":"And Allah is Ever All-Appreciative (of good), All-Knowing.","ref":"Nisaa 4:147"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ash-Shakoor mean, and how many times is it found in the Qur'aan?","a":"The One Most ready to appreciate and reward abundantly; it is found in four places."},{"q":"What does Ash-Shaakir mean, and how many times does it occur?","a":"The Appreciative; it occurs in two places (Baqarah 2:158 and Nisaa 4:147)."},{"q":"What is the common context of all six places where these two Names occur?","a":"Allaah giving by rewarding the obedient people, giving and multiplying the rewards and increasing them in grace."},{"q":"Which Name is combined with Ash-Shakoor in the aayaat, and what lesson does the author draw?","a":"Al-Ghafoor; so a Muslim must not despair of Allaah's forgiveness no matter how great the sin, nor look down upon any good deed no matter how small."}]},{"chapter":37,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Haleem","arabic":"الحَلِيم","meaning":"The Forbearing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Haleem The Forbearing occurs repeatedly in the Noble Qur'aan in many places."},{"type":"quote","text":"Truly, He is Ever Most Forbearing, Oft-Forgiving.","ref":"Faatir 35:41"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Ever All-Knowing, Most Forbearing.","ref":"Ahzaab 33:51"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Haleem means the One who does not hasten the punishment for His servants due to their sins and disobedience. He sees His servants when they disbelieve and disobey whilst He is Forbearing with them, delays, looks and postpones rather than hastens. He grants them blessings despite their disobedience, many sins and slips. He forbears in dealing with the disobedient with their disobedience, He gives them respite in order for them to repent. He does not hasten in punishing them so that they can turn back and repent to Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah informs us about His forbearance with the people of disobedience, sins and types of oppression that if He were to punish them for their sins one by one there would not remain an animal upon the surface of the earth."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And if Allah were to seize mankind for their wrong-doing, He would not leave on it (the earth) a single moving (living) creature, but He postpones them for an appointed term and when their term comes, neither can they delay nor can they advance it an hour (or a moment).","ref":"Nahl 16:61"},{"type":"quote","text":"And your Lord is Most Forgiving, Owner of Mercy. Were He to call them to account for what they have earned, then surely, He would have hastened their punishment. But they have their appointed time, beyond which they will find no escape.","ref":"Kahf 18:58"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite them committing shirk - associating partners with Allaah, showing annoyance, striving to go against, fighting His Religion and showing enmity towards His allies, Allaah shows forbearance with them. He gives them many types of good, grants them provision and grants them well-being. As in the Saheehayn from the hadeeth of Abee Moosaa al Ash'aree who said, The Prophet ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"None is more patient than Allah against harmful sayings. He hears from the people that they ascribe children to Him, yet He gives them health and (supplies them with) provision.\"","ref":"Saheeh Al-Bukhaaree 6099"},{"type":"p","text":"From His forbearance over the owners of the ditch,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, those who put into trial the believing men and believing women (by torturing them and burning them), and then do not turn in repentance, will have the torment of Hell, and they will have the punishment of the burning Fire.","ref":"Burooj 85:10"},{"type":"p","text":"Hasan al-Basree said, \"Look at this honour and generosity. They killed Allaah's allies and He calls them to repentance (tawbah) and forgiveness.\""}],"keyPoints":["Al-Haleem occurs repeatedly in the Noble Qur'aan in many places.","Al-Haleem means the One who does not hasten the punishment for His servants due to their sins and disobedience; He delays and postpones, giving them respite so they can repent.","He grants them blessings despite their disobedience, many sins and slips.","If Allaah were to punish people for their sins one by one, not an animal would remain upon the surface of the earth.","Even with those who commit shirk and show enmity to His allies, He gives them provision and well-being, and He called the owners of the ditch to repentance."],"evidence":[{"text":"And if Allah were to seize mankind for their wrong-doing, He would not leave on it (the earth) a single moving (living) creature, but He postpones them for an appointed term...","ref":"Nahl 16:61"},{"text":"\"None is more patient than Allah against harmful sayings. He hears from the people that they ascribe children to Him, yet He gives them health and (supplies them with) provision.\"","ref":"Saheeh Al-Bukhaaree 6099"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Haleem mean?","a":"The Forbearing: the One who does not hasten the punishment for His servants due to their sins and disobedience; He delays and postpones and gives them respite in order for them to repent."},{"q":"What would happen if Allaah punished people for their sins one by one?","a":"There would not remain an animal upon the surface of the earth (Nahl 16:61)."},{"q":"Which hadeeth does the author cite about Allaah's forbearance with those who ascribe children to Him?","a":"The hadeeth of Abu Moosaa al-Ash'aree: \"None is more patient than Allah against harmful sayings. He hears from the people that they ascribe children to Him, yet He gives them health and (supplies them with) provision.\""},{"q":"What did Hasan al-Basree say about the owners of the ditch?","a":"\"Look at this honour and generosity. They killed Allaah's allies and He calls them to repentance (tawbah) and forgiveness.\""}]},{"chapter":38,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Haqq","arabic":"الحَقّ","meaning":"The True One"},{"translit":"Al-Mubeen","arabic":"المُبِين","meaning":"The Clear and Manifest One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As for Allaah's Name Al-Haqq The True One, it is found in ten places in the Noble Qur'aan."},{"type":"quote","text":"Such is Allah, your Lord in truth. So after the truth, what else can there be, save error? How then are you turned away?","ref":"Yoonus 10:32"},{"type":"quote","text":"So Exalted be Allah, the True King, La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He), the Lord of the Supreme Throne!","ref":"Mu'minoon 23:116"},{"type":"p","text":"As for His Name Al-Mubeen The Clear and Manifest One, it is found in one place combined with the Name Al-Haqq The True One."},{"type":"quote","text":"On that Day Allah will pay them the recompense of their deeds in full, and they will know that Allah, He is the Manifest Truth.","ref":"Noor 24:25"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Mubeen means He is clear in His affair of Oneness and that He has no partner. The meaning of Al-Haqq is the One in whom there is no doubt or uncertainty - not in His Self, not in His Names and Attributes, not in His worship. He is the One that deserves to be worshipped in truth and nothing else has the right to be worshipped in truth besides Him."},{"type":"p","text":"He is The True One, His Names and Attributes are True, His Actions and speech are true. His religion and legislation is true, His news is all true, His promise is true and meeting Him is true."},{"type":"p","text":"The Prophet ﷺ used to begin his night salaah by confirming this meaning as in the hadeeth of Ibn 'Abbaas:"},{"type":"quote","text":"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ offered the night (Tahajjud) prayer, he used to say, \"O Allah! All the Praises are for You; You are the Light of the Heavens and the Earth. And all the Praises are for You; You are the Keeper of the Heavens and the Earth. All the Praises are for You; You are the Lord of the Heavens and the Earth and whatever is therein. You are the Truth, and Your Promise is the Truth, and Your Speech is the Truth, and meeting You is the Truth, and Paradise is the Truth and Hell (Fire) is the Truth and all the prophets are the Truth and the Hour is the Truth. O Allah! I surrender to You, and believe in You, and depend upon You, and repent to You, and in Your cause I fight and with Your orders I rule. So please forgive my past and future sins and those sins which I did in secret or in public. It is You Whom I worship, None has the right to be worshipped except You.\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhari 7499"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah gave various proofs, evidences, arguments and clarifications that He is the True Deity having no partners and that worshipping others besides Him is falsehood, deviancy, turning away and weakness."},{"type":"quote","text":"That is because Allah He is the Truth (the only True God of all that exists, Who has no partners or rivals with Him), and what they (the polytheists) invoke besides Him, it is Batil (falsehood). And verily, Allah He is the Most High, the Most Great.","ref":"Hajj 22:62"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Haqq is found in ten places in the Qur'aan; Al-Mubeen is found in one place, combined with Al-Haqq (Noor 24:25).","Al-Mubeen means He is clear in His affair of Oneness and that He has no partner.","Al-Haqq means the One in whom there is no doubt or uncertainty - not in His Self, His Names and Attributes, or His worship; He alone deserves to be worshipped in truth.","His Names, Attributes, Actions, speech, religion, legislation, news and promise are all true, and meeting Him is true.","The Prophet ﷺ began his night prayer affirming this meaning: \"You are the Truth, and Your Promise is the Truth, and Your Speech is the Truth...\""],"evidence":[{"text":"...and they will know that Allah, He is the Manifest Truth.","ref":"Noor 24:25"},{"text":"That is because Allah He is the Truth..., and what they (the polytheists) invoke besides Him, it is Batil (falsehood).","ref":"Hajj 22:62"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Haqq mean?","a":"The True One: the One in whom there is no doubt or uncertainty - not in His Self, His Names and Attributes, nor His worship; He is the One who deserves to be worshipped in truth."},{"q":"What does Al-Mubeen mean?","a":"The Clear and Manifest One: He is clear in His affair of Oneness and that He has no partner."},{"q":"How many times are Al-Haqq and Al-Mubeen found in the Qur'aan?","a":"Al-Haqq in ten places; Al-Mubeen in one place, combined with Al-Haqq in Noor 24:25."},{"q":"Which hadeeth does the author cite showing the Prophet ﷺ confirming this meaning?","a":"The hadeeth of Ibn 'Abbaas about the night (Tahajjud) prayer: \"...You are the Truth, and Your Promise is the Truth, and Your Speech is the Truth, and meeting You is the Truth...\" (Bukhari 7499)."}]},{"chapter":39,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Qadeer","arabic":"القَدِير","meaning":"The All-Powerful"},{"translit":"Al-Qaadir","arabic":"القَادِر","meaning":"The Fully Able"},{"translit":"Al-Muqtadir","arabic":"المُقْتَدِر","meaning":"The All-Capable"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"All of these Names are found in the Qur'aan with the most frequent being Al-Qadeer The All-Powerful, then Al-Qaadir The Fully Able and then Al-Muqtadir The All-Capable."},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Able to do all things.","ref":"Baqarah 2:284"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say: \"He has power to send torment on you from above or from under your feet, or to cover you with confusion in party strife, and make you to taste the violence of one another.\"","ref":"An'aam 6:65"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is Able to do everything.","ref":"Kahf 18:45"},{"type":"p","text":"All these Names indicate the affirmation of power as a description of Allaah and that Allaah is perfect in strength. By His power He brought into existence everything that exists. By His power He manages them, makes them and rules them. By His power He gives life and causes death. He resurrects the servants for recompense. He rewards the good doer for his good and He punishes the evil doer for his evil. Allaah if He wants something He says to it 'Be!' and it is. By His power He turns the hearts and directs them to what He wishes and wants. He guides whom He wills and He allows to go astray whom He wills. He makes the believer a believer and the disbeliever a disbeliever, the good doer good and the corrupt person corrupt. From the mighty foundations of faith is the belief in predestination (qadar). Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, We have created all things with Qadar (Divine Preordainments of all things before their creation, as written in the Book of Decrees Al-Lauh Al-Mahfuz).","ref":"Qamar 54:49"},{"type":"quote","text":"He has created everything, and has measured it exactly according to its due measurements.","ref":"Furqaan 25:2"},{"type":"p","text":"Whoever does not believe in predestination (qadar) does not believe in Allaah. Imaam Ahmad said qadar is Allaah's Power. Criticising qadar is criticising Allaah's power and denying His Attributes or part of them. It is negating faith in Him and His Oneness."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn 'Abbaas said, \"Predestination is the system of Tawheed (singling Allaah out alone for worship), whoever singles out Allaah alone for worship and believes in qadar has a trustworthy handhold which never breaks. Whoever singles out Allaah alone for worship but denies predestination (qadar), nullifies tawheed.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Believing in Allaah's power which these Names (Al-Qadeer, Al-Qaadir and Al-Muqtadir) indicate, has a mighty effect and blessed fruits which return to the servant in this world and the Next. How can it not when faith in it is a pivot of tawheed and its system. It is the basis and completion of faith. It is the foundation and support of the religion. It is one of the pillars of faith and a founding principle of perfection."}],"keyPoints":["All three Names are in the Qur'aan; the most frequent is Al-Qadeer, then Al-Qaadir, then Al-Muqtadir.","These Names affirm power as a description of Allaah and that He is perfect in strength.","By His power He brought everything into existence, manages it, gives life and death, resurrects, rewards and punishes, and turns the hearts, guiding whom He wills.","Belief in predestination (qadar) is from the mighty foundations of faith; Imaam Ahmad said qadar is Allaah's Power, so criticising qadar is criticising His power.","Ibn 'Abbaas said predestination is the system of Tawheed; whoever singles out Allaah but denies qadar nullifies tawheed."],"evidence":[{"text":"And Allah is Able to do all things.","ref":"Baqarah 2:284"},{"text":"Verily, We have created all things with Qadar.","ref":"Qamar 54:49"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do Al-Qadeer, Al-Qaadir and Al-Muqtadir mean?","a":"Al-Qadeer: The All-Powerful; Al-Qaadir: The Fully Able; Al-Muqtadir: The All-Capable. They affirm power as a description of Allaah and that He is perfect in strength."},{"q":"Which of these three Names is most frequent in the Qur'aan?","a":"Al-Qadeer, then Al-Qaadir, then Al-Muqtadir."},{"q":"What did Imaam Ahmad say about qadar?","a":"Qadar is Allaah's Power; criticising qadar is criticising Allaah's power and denying His Attributes or part of them."},{"q":"What did Ibn 'Abbaas say about predestination?","a":"\"Predestination is the system of Tawheed; whoever singles out Allaah alone for worship and believes in qadar has a trustworthy handhold which never breaks. Whoever singles out Allaah alone for worship but denies predestination nullifies tawheed.\""}]},{"chapter":40,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Wadood","arabic":"الوَدُود","meaning":"The Loving and the Beloved"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Wadood The Loving and the Beloved occurs in the Qur'aan twice,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"And ask forgiveness of your Lord and turn unto Him in repentance. Verily, my Lord is Most Merciful, Most Loving.\"","ref":"Hood 11:90"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, He it is Who begins (punishment) and repeats (punishment in the Hereafter) (or originates the creation of everything, and then repeats it on the Day of Resurrection). And He is Oft-Forgiving, full of love (towards the pious who are real true believers of Islamic Monotheism),","ref":"Burooj 85:13-14"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Wadood means the One who loves His Prophets, Messengers and their followers and they love Him. He is more beloved to them than anything else. Their hearts are filled with love for Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykh 'AbdurRahmaan bin Sa'dee said in a great research paper of his explaining the meaning and indications of this Name Al-Wadood, \"The One who is beloved to His creation by His beautiful descriptions, vast signs, hidden subtle kindness, His hidden and apparent blessings. He is Al-Wadood with the meaning of The Loving and with the meaning of the One who is Loved. He loves His allies and pure servants and they love Him. He is the One who is beloved to them and has put love in their hearts. So when they love Him, He loves them with another love as a reward for them for their love."},{"type":"p","text":"All favours return back to Allaah. He is the One who places all the means for them to love Him, to attract and draw their hearts to loving Him. He becomes beloved to them by mentioning what He has of beautiful, mighty, all-encompassing descriptions which will attract the sound upright hearts. Sound hearts and souls are drawn to loving perfection."},{"type":"p","text":"If a servant knows that His Lord is Loving and loves His allies, loves those who obey Him, loves the believers who have God consciousness (taqwa), loves the patient, loves those who put their trust in Him, loves those who seek repentance and those who purify themselves, loves the truthful and the good doers; He loves all those who are obedient and does not love the disbelieving oppressors, He does not love those who go to excesses, the deceptive, the self-deluding arrogant people. If a servant knows all this then it is upon him to obey His command and do what He loves and is pleased with such as sound speech and righteous deeds. He should come close to Allaah by fulfilling His command and avoiding His prohibitions. He should love what He loves of speech and actions, love His speech, love His Messenger ﷺ and his Sunnah and strive to follow it. Through this he will attain the love of Allaah."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say (O Muhammad to mankind): \"If you (really) love Allah then follow me (i.e. accept Islamic Monotheism, follow the Quran and the Sunnah), Allah will love you and forgive you of your sins.\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:31"},{"type":"p","text":"The Prophet ﷺ said in a du'aa,"},{"type":"quote","text":"'I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You, and for the action that will cause me to attain Your love...'","ref":"Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3490"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Wadood occurs in the Qur'aan twice (Hood 11:90 and Burooj 85:14).","Al-Wadood means the One who loves His Prophets, Messengers and their followers, and they love Him; He is more beloved to them than anything else.","Ibn Sa'dee said Al-Wadood carries both meanings: The Loving and the One who is Loved; when His servants love Him, He loves them with another love as a reward.","All favours return to Allaah: He places the means for them to love Him and becomes beloved by mentioning His beautiful, mighty descriptions.","Whoever knows that Allaah loves the obedient should do what He loves and follow His Messenger ﷺ and his Sunnah, and through this he attains Allaah's love."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"...Verily, my Lord is Most Merciful, Most Loving.\"","ref":"Hood 11:90"},{"text":"Say (O Muhammad to mankind): \"If you (really) love Allah then follow me, Allah will love you and forgive you of your sins.\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:31"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Wadood mean?","a":"The Loving and the Beloved: the One who loves His Prophets, Messengers and their followers and they love Him; He is more beloved to them than anything else."},{"q":"How many times does Al-Wadood occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"Twice."},{"q":"According to Shaykh Ibn Sa'dee, what happens when the servants love Allaah?","a":"He loves them with another love as a reward for them for their love."},{"q":"Which aayah does the author cite on how to attain the love of Allaah?","a":"Aali 'Imraan 3:31: \"If you (really) love Allah then follow me, Allah will love you and forgive you of your sins.\""},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ ask for in the du'aa quoted in this chapter?","a":"\"I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You, and for the action that will cause me to attain Your love...\""}]},{"chapter":41,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Barr","arabic":"البَرّ","meaning":"The Most Benign and Kind"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Barr The Most Benign and Kind is found in one place of the Noble Qur'aan,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Verily, We used to invoke Him (Alone and none else) before. Verily, He is Al-Barr (the Most Subtle, Kind, Courteous, and Generous), the Most Merciful.\"","ref":"Toor 52:28"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Barr means the One who comprehends the secrets of the creation through His kindness, bestowing and giving. He is the One who grants blessings, is generous in giving and is constant in good treatment. He is constantly described with kindness and generosity in the past and present. He is known by His bestowing and perfection. He grants favours upon the servants with ample blessings and various favours, giving one after the other. There is no measure to His beneficence, kindness and generosity. He possesses vast generosity, constant favours and abundant giving. It should be known here that Al-Barr The Most Kind loves the people of goodness. Their hearts come closer to Him due to what they do of goodness. He loves righteous actions so He rewards them with guidance, success and elevation in the worldly life and the Next. The origin of righteousness is doing plentiful good. There are aayaat that combine this characteristic. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"It is not Al-Birr (piety, righteousness, and each and every act of obedience to Allah, etc.) that you turn your faces towards east and (or) west (in prayers); but Al-Birr is (the quality of) the one who believes in Allah, the Last Day, the Angels, the Book, the Prophets and gives his wealth, in spite of love for it, to the kinsfolk, to the orphans, and to Al-Masakin (the poor), and to the wayfarer, and to those who ask, and to set slaves free, performs As-Salat (Iqamat-as-Salat), and gives the Zakat, and who fulfill their covenant when they make it, and who are As-Sabirin (the patient ones, etc.) in extreme poverty and ailment (disease) and at the time of fighting (during the battles). Such are the people of the truth and they are Al-Muttaqun.","ref":"Baqarah 2:177"},{"type":"quote","text":"By no means shall you attain Al-Birr (piety, righteousness, etc., it means here Allah's Reward, i.e. Paradise), unless you spend (in Allah's Cause) of that which you love; and whatever of good you spend, Allah knows it well.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:92"},{"type":"p","text":"Qataadah said, \"You will not achieve your Lord's Kindness until you spend of what you like and from what you desire of your wealth.\" Ibn Jareer At-Tabaree related this in his Tafseer."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah inspire us all to rectify ourselves and provide for us from His grace, kindness and generosity what we cannot imagine. Indeed He is All-Hearing, Responsive."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Barr is found in one place in the Noble Qur'aan (Toor 52:28).","Al-Barr means the One who comprehends the secrets of creation through His kindness, bestowing and giving; He grants blessings, is generous in giving and constant in good treatment.","There is no measure to His beneficence, kindness and generosity; He grants favours one after the other.","Al-Barr loves the people of goodness and righteous actions, and rewards them with guidance, success and elevation in this life and the Next.","The origin of righteousness (birr) is doing plentiful good; Qataadah said you will not achieve your Lord's Kindness until you spend of what you like of your wealth."],"evidence":[{"text":"Verily, He is Al-Barr (the Most Subtle, Kind, Courteous, and Generous), the Most Merciful.","ref":"Toor 52:28"},{"text":"By no means shall you attain Al-Birr..., unless you spend (in Allah's Cause) of that which you love.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:92"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Barr mean?","a":"The Most Benign and Kind: the One who comprehends the secrets of creation through His kindness, bestowing and giving; who grants blessings, is generous in giving and constant in good treatment."},{"q":"Where is Al-Barr found in the Qur'aan?","a":"In one place: Toor 52:28."},{"q":"What is the origin of righteousness according to the author?","a":"Doing plentiful good."},{"q":"What did Qataadah say about attaining Al-Birr?","a":"\"You will not achieve your Lord's Kindness until you spend of what you like and from what you desire of your wealth.\" (related by Ibn Jareer At-Tabaree in his Tafseer)"}]},{"chapter":42,"names":[{"translit":"Ar-Ra'oof","arabic":"الرَّؤُوف","meaning":"The Compassionate and Kind"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found in the Noble Qur'aan in ten aayaat."},{"type":"p","text":"The word الرأفة compassion according to Ibn Jareer 'is a higher meaning of mercy رحمة. It is general for all the creation in the world and for some of them in the Next Life.' 'Some' meaning: His believing allies and His God conscious servants. From the beneficial principles which the people of knowledge have laid down regarding the subject of understanding Allaah's Beautiful Names is that the endings of the Qur'aanic aayaat with Allaah's Beautiful Names indicate that the ruling mentioned in it is related to that Noble Name that ends the aayah. Reflecting upon that is from the greatest means of helping a servant to understand Allaah's Beautiful Names."},{"type":"p","text":"An example is in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"On the Day when every person will be confronted with all the good he has done, and all the evil he has done, he will wish that there were a great distance between him and his evil. And Allah warns you against Himself (His Punishment) and Allah is full of Kindness to the (His) slaves.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:30"},{"type":"p","text":"This means that despite Allaah's severe punishment and great exemplary punishment He is indeed Compassionate with His servants. It is from His Compassion with them that He makes His servants afraid and drives them away from deviancy and corruption, so that they will be safe from their consequences and that they will be saved from their punishments. He is Compassionate and Merciful and this eases the paths of His servants to achieve good and raises their levels. It is compassion and mercy from Him that the servants are warned about the paths that lead to disliked actions. Allaah says regarding this,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And those who came after them say: \"Our Lord! Forgive us and our brethren who have preceded us in Faith, and put not in our hearts any hatred against those who have believed. Our Lord! You are indeed full of kindness, Most Merciful.","ref":"Hashr 59:10"},{"type":"p","text":"This is from Allaah's mercy and compassion with His believing servants that He established a contract of faith, a religious link and a close tie of God-consciousness between them; He made the ones who came after love the ones who came before - calling to it with every goodness. What an excellent gift, how noble is the benefit that our Protector, The Compassionate, The Merciful has given as a favour."}],"keyPoints":["Ar-Ra'oof is found in the Noble Qur'aan in ten aayaat.","According to Ibn Jareer, compassion (ra'fah) is a higher meaning of mercy; it is general for all creation in this world and for some of them (His believing, God-conscious servants) in the Next Life.","A beneficial principle: when an aayah ends with one of Allaah's Names, the ruling mentioned in it is related to that Name.","In Aali 'Imraan 3:30, it is from His Compassion that He warns His servants and makes them afraid, so they are saved from deviancy and its punishments.","From His compassion with the believers is that He established a tie of faith between them, making later generations love those who came before (Hashr 59:10)."],"evidence":[{"text":"And Allah warns you against Himself (His Punishment) and Allah is full of Kindness to the (His) slaves.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:30"},{"text":"Our Lord! You are indeed full of kindness, Most Merciful.","ref":"Hashr 59:10"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ar-Ra'oof mean?","a":"The Compassionate and Kind; compassion (ra'fah), according to Ibn Jareer, is a higher meaning of mercy."},{"q":"In how many aayaat is Ar-Ra'oof found?","a":"In ten aayaat."},{"q":"What principle do the people of knowledge mention about aayaat ending with Allaah's Names?","a":"The ending of an aayah with one of Allaah's Names indicates that the ruling mentioned in it is related to that Name."},{"q":"How is Allaah's warning of His punishment in Aali 'Imraan 3:30 a sign of His compassion?","a":"From His Compassion He makes His servants afraid and drives them away from deviancy and corruption so that they are safe from their consequences and saved from their punishments."}]},{"chapter":43,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Haseeb","arabic":"الحَسِيب","meaning":"The Reckoner who suffices"},{"translit":"Al-Kaafee","arabic":"الكَافِي","meaning":"The Sufficient"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and Allah is All-Sufficient in taking account.","ref":"Nisaa 4:6"},{"type":"quote","text":"Is not Allah Sufficient for His slave? Yet they try to frighten you with those (whom they worship) besides Him! And whom Allah sends astray, for him there will be no guide.","ref":"Zumar 39:36"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Haseeb is the Sufficient, the One who is sufficient for all that is important for His servants of their religious and worldly affairs. He makes everything that they need easy for them and repels everything they dislike from them. From the meanings of Al-Haseeb is that He is the Protector over His servants in everything that they do. He takes account of them but they forget and He knows this. He distinguishes between righteous and corrupt deeds, good from bad and He knows what they deserve of punishment and reward and how much of each."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Kaafee The Sufficient. The One who suffices the creation by His Hand with everything they need. His Sufficiency is general and specific."},{"type":"p","text":"General Sufficiency – Allaah has sufficed all the creation and has brought them into existence, provided for them and prepared them for everything that they were created for. He prepared for the servants all the means that would enrich them, suffice them, feed them and give them drink."},{"type":"p","text":"Specific Sufficiency – This is the sufficiency for those who put their trust in Him. He undertakes to rectify the situation of His God-conscious servants,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And whosoever puts his trust in Allah, then He will suffice him.","ref":"Talaq 65:3"},{"type":"p","text":"This means He suffices him in all his religious and worldly affairs. When a servant puts his trust in his Lord, a true trust with his heart relying upon his Lord with a strong complete reliance to achieve a benefit for him and repel a harm; and he strengthens his trust and good thoughts about his Lord – he then achieves complete sufficiency. Allaah completes his affairs and makes his speech and action correct. He suffices his worry and removes his distress."},{"type":"p","text":"Some of the Salaf (Pious Predecessors) said, \"Allaah has made a reward similar to every action. He made the reward of putting trust in Him (tawakkul) His sufficiency for His servant; He said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And whosoever puts his trust in Allah, then He will suffice him.","ref":"Talaq 65:3"},{"type":"p","text":"He did not say, 'We will give him this and that of reward' as He has said with other good deeds. Instead He has made Himself sufficient and a Protector for His servants who put their trust in Him. If a servant puts his true trust in Allaah, the heavens, the earth and all in them almost give him a way out and suffice and help him due to that.\" Linking sufficiency to putting your trust in Allaah is linking the means to its causes. Allaah is sufficient for those who trust in Him and perfect their trust in Him. They sincerely turn to Him in their important matters and calamities. The more a servant has good thoughts about Allaah, great hopes in what is with Him and true trust upon Him then Allaah will not ever allow his wishes to be disappointed."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Haseeb is the One who is sufficient for all that is important for His servants of their religious and worldly affairs, making easy what they need and repelling what they dislike.","From the meanings of Al-Haseeb is that He is the Protector over His servants, taking account of their deeds and knowing what they deserve of reward and punishment.","Al-Kaafee is the One who suffices the creation with everything they need, and His Sufficiency is general and specific.","General sufficiency covers all creation: He brought them into existence, provided for them and prepared them for what they were created for.","Specific sufficiency is for those who put their trust in Him; the reward of tawakkul is Allaah's own sufficiency for His servant."],"evidence":[{"text":"and Allah is All-Sufficient in taking account.","ref":"Nisaa 4:6"},{"text":"Is not Allah Sufficient for His slave?","ref":"Zumar 39:36"},{"text":"And whosoever puts his trust in Allah, then He will suffice him.","ref":"Talaq 65:3"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Haseeb mean?","a":"The Sufficient, the One who is sufficient for all that is important for His servants of their religious and worldly affairs; also the Protector who takes account of their deeds."},{"q":"What does Al-Kaafee mean?","a":"The Sufficient, the One who suffices the creation by His Hand with everything they need."},{"q":"What are the two types of Allaah's sufficiency mentioned?","a":"General sufficiency for all the creation, and specific sufficiency for those who put their trust in Him."},{"q":"According to some of the Salaf, what is the reward of tawakkul?","a":"Allaah's sufficiency for His servant, as in 'And whosoever puts his trust in Allah, then He will suffice him' (Talaq 65:3)."}]},{"chapter":44,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Kafeel","arabic":"الكَفِيل","meaning":"The Witness"},{"translit":"Al-Wakeel","arabic":"الوَكِيل","meaning":"The Guardian/Disposer of Affairs"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and break not the oaths after you have confirmed them, and indeed you have appointed Allah your surety. Verily! Allah knows what you do.","ref":"Nahl 16:91"},{"type":"quote","text":"But it (only) increased them in Faith, and they said: \"Allah (Alone) is Sufficient for us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs (for us).\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:173"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Kafeel means the One responsible for the creation's affairs. The guarantor for their food and provisions. Whoever is truthful with Allaah in that and is pleased with Him as a guarantor, Allaah helps him to fulfil his duties and helps his affairs from where he would never imagine."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Wakeel means Al-Kaafee The Sufficient, Al-Kafeel The Witness. It is general and specific."},{"type":"p","text":"The General Guardian which is referred to in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and He is the Wakil (Trustee, Disposer of affairs, Guardian, etc.) over all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:102"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah is a Wakil (Disposer of affairs, Trustee, Guardian, etc.) over all things.","ref":"Hood 11:12"},{"type":"p","text":"Meaning the guardian over provision and food for all of the creation. The One who undertakes the management of the affairs of creation and directs them."},{"type":"p","text":"The Specific Guardian which is referred to in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and put your trust in Allah. And Allah is Ever All-Sufficient as a Disposer of affairs.","ref":"Nisaa 4:81"},{"type":"quote","text":"and they said: \"Allah (Alone) is Sufficient for us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs (for us).\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:173"},{"type":"p","text":"Meaning the best Sufficer for those who turn to Him and the Protector to those who seek refuge in Him. This is specific to His believing servants who put their trust in Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Putting your trust in Allaah alone is the foundation for all levels of the religion. Its status is that of the body to the head so just as the head cannot rest except upon the body, so too is the situation of faith, its levels and actions cannot rest except upon the trunk of putting your trust in Allaah (tawakkul)."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Kafeel means the One responsible for the creation's affairs, the guarantor for their food and provisions.","Whoever is truthful with Allaah and pleased with Him as a guarantor, Allaah helps him fulfil his duties and helps his affairs from where he would never imagine.","Al-Wakeel means Al-Kaafee (The Sufficient) and Al-Kafeel, and its meaning is general and specific.","The general meaning: He is the guardian over the provision of all creation, managing and directing their affairs.","The specific meaning: He is the best Sufficer and Protector for His believing servants who put their trust in Him.","Putting trust in Allaah alone (tawakkul) is the foundation for all levels of the religion, like the body upon which the head rests."],"evidence":[{"text":"and indeed you have appointed Allah your surety. Verily! Allah knows what you do.","ref":"Nahl 16:91"},{"text":"\"Allah (Alone) is Sufficient for us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs (for us).\"","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:173"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Kafeel mean?","a":"The One responsible for the creation's affairs; the guarantor for their food and provisions."},{"q":"What does Al-Wakeel mean?","a":"Al-Kaafee (The Sufficient) and Al-Kafeel; generally the One who manages the affairs of all creation, and specifically the best Sufficer and Protector for believers who trust in Him."},{"q":"Which aayah is cited for the specific meaning of Al-Wakeel?","a":"'and put your trust in Allah. And Allah is Ever All-Sufficient as a Disposer of affairs' (Nisaa 4:81) and 'Allah (Alone) is Sufficient for us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs' (Aali 'Imraan 3:173)."},{"q":"What example does the author give for the status of tawakkul in the religion?","a":"It is like the body to the head: just as the head cannot rest except upon the body, faith, its levels and actions cannot rest except upon tawakkul."}]},{"chapter":45,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Ghaalib","arabic":"الغَالِب","meaning":"The Predominant"},{"translit":"An-Naseer","arabic":"النَّصِير","meaning":"The Helper"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name of Allaah Al-Ghaalib The Predominant is found in one place in the Qur'aan. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And Allah has full power and control over His Affairs, but most of men know not.","ref":"Yoosuf 12:21"},{"type":"p","text":"The Name An-Naseer The Helper is found in four places,"},{"type":"quote","text":"then know that Allah is your Maula (Patron, Lord, Protector and Supporter, etc.), (what) an Excellent Maula, and (what) an Excellent Helper!","ref":"Anfaal 8:40"},{"type":"quote","text":"and Allah is Sufficient as a Helper.","ref":"Nisaa 4:45"},{"type":"quote","text":"and hold fast to Allah [i.e. have confidence in Allah, and depend upon Him in all your affairs] He is your Maula (Patron, Lord, etc.), what an Excellent Maula (Patron, Lord, etc.) and what an Excellent Helper!","ref":"Haj 22:78"},{"type":"quote","text":"But Sufficient is your Lord as a Guide and Helper.","ref":"Furqaan 25:31"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Ghaalib means the One who does as He wills, nothing overcomes Him and none can resist His Rule. No one possesses the ability to repel what He has decreed or prevent what He has concluded."},{"type":"p","text":"Qurtubee said, \"It is a must for every sane adult to know that Allaah is Al-Ghaalib The unrestrictedly Predominant. Whoever holds on to Him, He will be victorious even if everyone on earth has the same request. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah has decreed: \"Verily! It is I and My Messengers who shall be the victorious.\"","ref":"Mujaadilah 58:21"},{"type":"p","text":"Whoever turns away from Allaah and holds onto other than Him will be overcome, in the snares of shaytaan and overturned.\""},{"type":"p","text":"An-Naseer means the One who undertakes to help His servants. He guarantees help for His allies and defends them. Victory cannot come except from Him and cannot be realised except through Him giving it. The one who is victorious is the one that Allaah has aided and granted victory. So there is no helper for the servants except Him and no protector for them except Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And there is no victory except from Allah, the Almighty, the All-Wise.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:126"},{"type":"quote","text":"If Allah helps you, none can overcome you; and if He forsakes you, who is there after Him that can help you?","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:160"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah has mentioned in multiple places in the Noble Qur'aan His help for His prophets and allies with victory and support. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, We will indeed make victorious Our Messengers and those who believe (in the Oneness of Allah – Islamic Monotheism) in this world's life and on the Day when the witnesses will stand forth, (i.e. Day of Resurrection).","ref":"Ghaafir 40:51"},{"type":"p","text":"The speech is directed to the believers who establish the rights of faith, outwardly and inwardly, that they will be victorious and have a praiseworthy end in this Life and the Next."},{"type":"p","text":"Due to this, the believers who do not strive with their selves to actualise faith or come with the means of victory over the enemies will not achieve victory. Instead their enemies will overpower them due to their sins and shortcomings."},{"type":"p","text":"It is also necessary to sincerely turn to the One in whose Hand lies victory. Allaah is the Protector of those who turn to Him, He suffices those who seek His refuge. What a blessed Protector and what a blessed Helper."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Ghaalib is found in one place in the Qur'aan (Yoosuf 12:21), and An-Naseer is found in four places.","Al-Ghaalib means the One who does as He wills; nothing overcomes Him, none can resist His Rule, and none can repel what He has decreed.","Qurtubee said whoever holds on to Allaah will be victorious, and whoever turns away to other than Him will be overcome.","An-Naseer means the One who undertakes to help His servants, guaranteeing help for His allies and defending them; victory comes only from Him.","Allaah's promised victory is for the believers who establish the rights of faith outwardly and inwardly; those who fall short may be overpowered due to their sins."],"evidence":[{"text":"And Allah has full power and control over His Affairs, but most of men know not.","ref":"Yoosuf 12:21"},{"text":"And there is no victory except from Allah, the Almighty, the All-Wise.","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:126"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Ghaalib mean?","a":"The One who does as He wills; nothing overcomes Him and none can resist His Rule or repel what He has decreed."},{"q":"What does An-Naseer mean?","a":"The One who undertakes to help His servants, guarantees help for His allies and defends them; victory comes only from Him."},{"q":"How many times do Al-Ghaalib and An-Naseer occur in the Qur'aan according to the author?","a":"Al-Ghaalib in one place (Yoosuf 12:21) and An-Naseer in four places."},{"q":"Why do some believers not achieve victory over their enemies?","a":"Because they do not strive to actualise faith or come with the means of victory, so their enemies overpower them due to their sins and shortcomings."}]},{"chapter":46,"names":[{"translit":"Al-'Azeez","arabic":"العَزِيز","meaning":"The Almighty"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-'Azeez The Almighty occurs in the Noble Qur'aan almost a hundred times."},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Al-'Azeez is the One who possesses all the meanings of Might as Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"for all power and honour belong to Allah.","ref":"Yoonus 10:65"},{"type":"p","text":"This means the One who possesses Might with all of its meanings. It encompasses three meanings all of which are established for Allaah in terms of perfection and completeness."},{"type":"p","text":"The First meaning – Might and Strength. It is His mighty description which the creation (even if it is great) is not described with."},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong.","ref":"Dhaariyaat 51:58"},{"type":"p","text":"The Second meaning – Might of Refraining. Allaah is Rich in Himself and is not in need of anyone. The servants cannot harm or benefit Him. Allaah is the One who benefits and harms; He gives and withholds. He is free from anyone overcoming Him, from anyone having power over Him and from everything that is not befitting to His Majesty and Honour from deficiencies and defects. He is free from everything that negates His Perfection and from taking partners and associates."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Glorified be your Lord, the Lord of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they attribute unto Him! And peace be on the Messengers! And all the praise and thanks be to Allah, Lord of the 'Alamin (mankind, jinns and all that exists).","ref":"Saafaat 37:180-182"},{"type":"p","text":"The Third meaning – Might of Subduing and Overcoming. All of the creation are under His invincibility, humbled to His Might and under His Will. The forelocks of all of creation are in His Hand. No one moves or does anything without His Might, Power and Permission. What Allaah willed happened and what He did not will did not happen and there is no might nor power except by Allaah."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-'Azeez occurs in the Noble Qur'aan almost a hundred times.","Al-'Azeez is the One who possesses all the meanings of Might, and it encompasses three meanings.","First: Might and Strength, a description with which the creation, however great, is not described.","Second: Might of Refraining – Allaah is Rich in Himself, not in need of anyone, and the servants cannot harm or benefit Him; He is free from every deficiency and from partners.","Third: Might of Subduing and Overcoming – all creation is humbled to His Might and under His Will, and none moves except by His Permission."],"evidence":[{"text":"for all power and honour belong to Allah.","ref":"Yoonus 10:65"},{"text":"Glorified be your Lord, the Lord of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they attribute unto Him!","ref":"Saafaat 37:180"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-'Azeez mean?","a":"The One who possesses all the meanings of Might."},{"q":"How often does the Name Al-'Azeez occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"Almost a hundred times."},{"q":"What are the three meanings of Might established for Allaah?","a":"Might and Strength; Might of Refraining; and Might of Subduing and Overcoming."},{"q":"Which aayah is cited for the First meaning (Might and Strength)?","a":"'Verily, Allah is the All-Provider, Owner of Power, the Most Strong' (Dhaariyaat 51:58)."}]},{"chapter":47,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Jabbaar","arabic":"الجَبَّار","meaning":"The Exalted and Almighty Compeller"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is mentioned once in the Noble Qur'aan combined with the Name Al-'Azeez The Almighty in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Jabbaar has three meanings:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. It has the meaning of Al-Qahhaar The Invincible Subduer. Allaah is the Subduer of everything. Everything submits to Him, everything humbles themselves to Him. The upper and lower world with all that is in it of amazing creation humbly submits their movements and their staying still and what comes and goes to their Owner and Controller. They do not have any control nor any rule over anything, instead the command is all for Allaah – the legislated, predestined and rule of recompense is all for Allaah. There is no judge except for Him, no Lord other than Him and no deity worthy of worship besides Him."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Al-Jabbaar refers to subtle kindness, mercy and compassion. Allaah is the One who heals the defeated, enriches the poor, makes things easy for the one in hardship and grants success to the sick and afflicted to have patience. He makes it easy for them and replaces their hardship for the greatest reward. He grants special compassion to the hearts of those who humble themselves to His greatness and honour and to those hearts who love Him. They humble themselves to His Perfection, hoping for His grace and favours out of what He has bestowed upon their hearts of love, different types of recognition, divine success, guidance and direction. A person making du'aa saying 'Allaahummajburnee' is asking for this 'jabr' compassion which in reality is the rectification of the servant, repelling all types of disliked matters and evils from him."},{"type":"p","text":"The Prophet ﷺ used to say between the two prostrations (sajdah) in salaah:"},{"type":"quote","text":"'O Allah! Pardon me, have mercy on me, help me, guide me, and grant me sustenance.'","ref":"Jaami' at-Tirmidhee 284 and Sunan Ibn Maajah 898"},{"type":"p","text":"3. From the meanings of Al-Jabbaar is Al-'Alee The High and Exalted over everything. The One who encompasses all meanings of highness: highness of Himself, highness of status and highness of invincibility."},{"type":"p","text":"Power and Might (Al-Jabaroot) is for Allaah alone. Whoever from the creation brings about Allaah's anger, deserves His threat. Allaah has warned those who do this of a severe punishment, He will seal his heart and enter him into Hell Fire on the Day of Resurrection. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Thus does Allah seal up the heart of every arrogant, tyrant.","ref":"Ghaafir 40:35"},{"type":"p","text":"Ahmad and Tirmidhee related from Aboo Hurayrah who said that the Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Some of the Fire (in the shape of a long neck) will come out of the Fire on the Day of Judgment. It will have two eyes which can see, two ears which can hear, and a tongue which can speak. It will say: 'I have been left in charge of three: Every obstinate oppressor, everyone who called upon a deity besides Allah, and the image makers.'\"","ref":"Jaami' at-Tirmidhee 2574"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Jabbaar is mentioned once in the Qur'aan, combined with Al-'Azeez, in Hashr 59:23.","First meaning: Al-Qahhaar, the Invincible Subduer to whom everything submits and humbles itself.","Second meaning: subtle kindness, mercy and compassion – He heals the defeated, enriches the poor and eases hardship; saying 'Allaahummajburnee' asks for this jabr.","Third meaning: Al-'Alee, the High and Exalted over everything – in Himself, in status and in invincibility.","Power and Might (Al-Jabaroot) is for Allaah alone; the arrogant tyrant among the creation is threatened with a sealed heart and the Fire."],"evidence":[{"text":"the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"text":"'O Allah! Pardon me, have mercy on me, help me, guide me, and grant me sustenance.'","ref":"Jaami' at-Tirmidhee 284 and Sunan Ibn Maajah 898"}],"recall":[{"q":"What are the three meanings of Al-Jabbaar?","a":"1) Al-Qahhaar, the Invincible Subduer; 2) subtle kindness, mercy and compassion; 3) Al-'Alee, the High and Exalted over everything."},{"q":"Where is the Name Al-Jabbaar mentioned in the Qur'aan?","a":"Once, combined with Al-'Azeez, in Hashr 59:23."},{"q":"What is a person asking for when saying 'Allaahummajburnee'?","a":"The 'jabr' compassion, which in reality is the rectification of the servant and repelling all disliked matters and evils from him."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say between the two prostrations?","a":"'O Allah! Pardon me, have mercy on me, help me, guide me, and grant me sustenance.'"},{"q":"Which three will the neck of Fire say it has been left in charge of?","a":"Every obstinate oppressor, everyone who called upon a deity besides Allah, and the image makers."}]},{"chapter":48,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Qareeb","arabic":"القَرِيب","meaning":"The One Who is Near"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Qareeb The One who is Near is found in the Noble Qur'aan in three places. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And when My slaves ask you (O Muhammad) concerning Me, then (answer them), I am indeed near (to them by My Knowledge). I respond to the invocations of the supplicant when he calls on Me (without any mediator or intercessor). So let them obey Me and believe in Me, so that they may be led aright.","ref":"Baqarah 2:186"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say: \"If (even) I go astray, I shall stray only to my own loss. But if I remain guided, it is because of the Inspiration of my Lord to me. Truly, He is All-Hearer, Ever Near (to all things).\"","ref":"Saba 34:50"},{"type":"quote","text":"And to Thamud (people, We sent) their brother Salih (Saleh). He said: \"O my people! Worship Allah, you have no other Ilah (God) but Him. He brought you forth from the earth and settled you therein, then ask forgiveness of Him and turn to Him in repentance. Certainly, my Lord is Near (to all by His Knowledge), Responsive.\"","ref":"Hood 11:61"},{"type":"p","text":"The closeness of Allaah that is referred to in these aayaat is a special closeness to the worshippers, those who love Allaah, call upon Him and Allaah responds to them. It is a closeness the reality of which is not known but the effects of which are known by Allaah's Kindness to them, His granting success to them and His care of them. From its effects is that Allaah answers those who call upon Him and He grants firmness to the worshippers. Many ahaadeeth that are authentically related in the Sunnah refer to Allaah's closeness to His believing servants and God-conscious allies. He hears their du'aa, answers their calls, gives them their requests. In the two Saheehs it is reported by Aboo Moosaa al-Ash'aree who said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"We were with Allah's Apostle ﷺ on a journey when the people began to pronounce Allaahu Akbar in a loud voice. Thereupon Allah's Messenger ﷺ said: O people, show mercy to yourselves for you are not calling One who is deaf nor absent. Verily, you are calling One who is All-Hearing (and) Near to you and is with you.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 2704a"},{"type":"p","text":"Aboo Hurayrah reported Allah's Apostle ﷺ as saying that Allaah, the Exalted and Glorious, said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"When My servant draws close to Me by a palm span, I draw close to him by a cubit and when he draws close to Me by a cubit, I draw close to him by two arm spans, and when he comes to me walking, I go in a hurry towards him.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 2675e"}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Qareeb is found in the Noble Qur'aan in three places (Baqarah 2:186, Saba 34:50, Hood 11:61).","The closeness referred to in these aayaat is a special closeness to the worshippers who love Allaah and call upon Him, and He responds to them.","Its reality is not known, but its effects are known: His Kindness, granting success, care, answering du'aa and granting firmness.","Authentic ahaadeeth describe Allaah's closeness to His believing servants: He hears their du'aa, answers their calls and gives them their requests."],"evidence":[{"text":"And when My slaves ask you (O Muhammad) concerning Me, then (answer them), I am indeed near (to them by My Knowledge). I respond to the invocations of the supplicant when he calls on Me.","ref":"Baqarah 2:186"},{"text":"\"...you are not calling One who is deaf nor absent. Verily, you are calling One who is All-Hearing (and) Near to you and is with you.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 2704a"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Qareeb mean, and what kind of closeness do the aayaat refer to?","a":"The One who is Near; a special closeness to the worshippers who love Allaah and call upon Him, and He responds to them."},{"q":"In how many places is Al-Qareeb found in the Qur'aan?","a":"Three places."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say when the people pronounced Allaahu Akbar loudly on a journey?","a":"'O people, show mercy to yourselves for you are not calling One who is deaf nor absent. Verily, you are calling One who is All-Hearing (and) Near to you and is with you.'"},{"q":"Is the reality of this closeness known?","a":"No, its reality is not known, but its effects are known: Allaah's kindness, granting success, care, answering those who call upon Him and granting firmness."}]},{"chapter":49,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Mujeeb","arabic":"المُجِيب","meaning":"The Responsive"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Mujeeb The Responsive is found in one place in the Noble Qur'aan. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And to Thamud (people, We sent) their brother Salih (Saleh). He said: \"O my people! Worship Allah, you have no other Ilah (God) but Him. He brought you forth from the earth and settled you therein, then ask forgiveness of Him and turn to Him in repentance. Certainly, my Lord is Near (to all by His Knowledge), Responsive.\"","ref":"Hood 11:61"},{"type":"p","text":"His Name Al-Mujeeb The Responsive refers to Allaah hearing the supplication of the one who supplicates, answering the request of those who ask and not disappointing a believer when he calls upon Him. He does not reject a plea of a Muslim and He likes that a servant asks Him for all his religious and worldly affairs."},{"type":"p","text":"Many ahaadeeth occur in the Prophetic Sunnah encouraging du'aa and they clarify that Allaah is shy and generous. He is the most generous so he will not turn away someone who calls upon Him or disappoint the one who seeks His help or prevent someone who asks of Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Aboo Daawood, Tirmidhee and others relate from Salmaan al-Faarisee that the Prophet ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Indeed, Allaah is The One Possessing Honourable Shame (Hayyiy) and The Generous (Kareem). When a man raises his hands to Him, He feels too shy to return them to him empty and rejected.\"","ref":"Similar wording in Sunan Aboo Daawood 1488 and Jaami' at-Tirmidhee 3556"},{"type":"p","text":"In the hadeeth describing the Divine Descent Aboo Hurayrah narrated that Allaah's Messenger ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Our Lord, the Blessed, the Superior, comes down every night to the nearest Heaven to us when the last third of the night remains, saying: 'Is there anyone to invoke Me, so that I may respond to his invocation? Is there anyone to ask Me, so that I may grant him his request? Is there anyone seeking My forgiveness, so that I may forgive him?'\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhari 1145"},{"type":"p","text":"From the effects of the Name Al-Mujeeb upon the faith of a servant is that it strengthens his certainty in Allaah, it increases his hope, it encourages him to turn to Allaah more and hope for what He has (to offer). It also removes despair of Allaah's Mercy or hopelessness regarding His benevolence."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Mujeeb is found in one place in the Noble Qur'aan (Hood 11:61).","Al-Mujeeb refers to Allaah hearing the supplication of the supplicant, answering the request of those who ask and not disappointing a believer who calls upon Him.","He does not reject a Muslim's plea and likes that a servant asks Him for all his religious and worldly affairs.","The Sunnah clarifies that Allaah is shy and generous, too shy to return raised hands empty.","Its effects on the servant: stronger certainty, more hope, turning to Allaah more, and removal of despair of His Mercy."],"evidence":[{"text":"Certainly, my Lord is Near (to all by His Knowledge), Responsive.","ref":"Hood 11:61"},{"text":"\"When a man raises his hands to Him, He feels too shy to return them to him empty and rejected.\"","ref":"Sunan Aboo Daawood 1488 and Jaami' at-Tirmidhee 3556"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Mujeeb mean?","a":"The Responsive: Allaah hears the supplication of the one who supplicates, answers the request of those who ask and does not disappoint a believer who calls upon Him."},{"q":"In which aayah is the Name Al-Mujeeb found?","a":"Hood 11:61 – 'Certainly, my Lord is Near (to all by His Knowledge), Responsive.' It is found in one place only."},{"q":"What does Allaah say when He descends in the last third of the night?","a":"'Is there anyone to invoke Me, so that I may respond to his invocation? Is there anyone to ask Me, so that I may grant him his request? Is there anyone seeking My forgiveness, so that I may forgive him?'"},{"q":"What are the effects of this Name upon the servant's faith?","a":"It strengthens his certainty in Allaah, increases his hope, encourages him to turn to Allaah more, and removes despair of Allaah's Mercy."}]},{"chapter":50,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Qaahir","arabic":"القَاهِر","meaning":"The Invincible Subduer"},{"translit":"Al-Qahhaar","arabic":"القَهَّار","meaning":"The Overwhelming Subduer"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Qahhaar The Overwhelming Subduer is found in six places in the Qur'aan."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Qaahir The Invincible Subduer occurs in two places in the Qur'aan both in Sooratul An'aam,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And He is the Irresistible, above His slaves, and He is the All-Wise, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:18"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is the Irresistible, Supreme over His slaves and He sends guardians (angels guarding and writing all of one's good and bad deeds) over you.","ref":"An'aam 6:61"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Qahhaar is the emphatic form of Al-Qaahir. They both mean the One who Subdues all of creation and the One to whom all of creation are humbled."},{"type":"p","text":"The elements and components of the upper and lower worlds draw close to His Power and Will. Nothing happens or stays still without His permission. What He willed, happened and what He did not will did not happen. All of the creation are in need of Allaah and are helpless. They do not possess benefit or harm, good or evil for themselves."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah being the Subduer means that He has perfect life, might and power. Allaah's Name Al-Qahhaar occurs in all the places combined with the Name Allaah al-Waahid The One."},{"type":"p","text":"This counts as a proof of Allaah's Oneness and evidence that He is singled out for worship and it is an invalidation of shirk (polytheism and taking partners)."},{"type":"p","text":"One example of this is Allaah saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"Who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth?\" Say: \"(It is) Allah.\" Say: \"Have you then taken (for worship) Auliya' (protectors, etc.) other than Him, such as have no power either for benefit or for harm to themselves?\" Say: \"Is the blind equal to the one who sees? Or darkness equal to light? Or do they assign to Allah partners who created the like of His creation, so that the creation (which they made and His creation) seemed alike to them.\" Say: \"Allah is the Creator of all things, He is the One, the Irresistible.\"","ref":"Ra'd 13:16"},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Sa'dee in his tafseer of this aayah explains the meaning of the evidence that Allaah's Name Al-Qaahir invalidates shirk, \"Uniqueness and Subduing do not exist except for Allaah alone. In the creation every created being dominates over another and then over that there is a subduer subduing him higher than him until it reaches The One, The Invincible Subduer. Subduing and uniqueness go together and are specific only to Allaah alone. So it is clear with intellectual dominant proofs that what is called upon besides Allaah does not possess anything from the creation and therefore worshipping it is falsehood.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Establishing this makes clear the inseparability between tawheed and faith by Allaah's Name Al-Qahhaar. Whoever holds to the establishment that singles out Allaah alone with Invincibility will single Him out alone for worship and he will know the corruption of shirk. So how can someone consider objects that are made from the earth equal to the Lord of the Lords?! How can someone make creation that is subdued equal to Allaah, The One, The Invincible Subduer?! Allaah is high above what they associate with Him and He is Free from what they say."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Qahhaar is found in six places in the Qur'aan, and Al-Qaahir in two places, both in Sooratul An'aam.","Al-Qahhaar is the emphatic form of Al-Qaahir; both mean the One who subdues all of creation and to whom all creation are humbled.","All creation is in need of Allaah and helpless, not possessing benefit or harm for themselves; nothing happens without His permission.","Allaah being the Subduer means He has perfect life, might and power.","Al-Qahhaar always occurs combined with Al-Waahid (The One), which is a proof of His Oneness in worship and an invalidation of shirk."],"evidence":[{"text":"And He is the Irresistible, above His slaves, and He is the All-Wise, Well-Acquainted with all things.","ref":"An'aam 6:18"},{"text":"Say: \"Allah is the Creator of all things, He is the One, the Irresistible.\"","ref":"Ra'd 13:16"}],"recall":[{"q":"What do Al-Qaahir and Al-Qahhaar mean, and how are they related?","a":"Al-Qahhaar is the emphatic form of Al-Qaahir; both mean the One who subdues all of creation and to whom all of creation are humbled."},{"q":"How many times do Al-Qahhaar and Al-Qaahir occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"Al-Qahhaar in six places; Al-Qaahir in two places, both in Sooratul An'aam (6:18 and 6:61)."},{"q":"With which Name is Al-Qahhaar always combined, and what does this indicate?","a":"With Al-Waahid (The One); it is a proof of Allaah's Oneness, that He alone is to be worshipped, and an invalidation of shirk."},{"q":"How did Ibn Sa'dee explain that the Name Al-Qaahir invalidates shirk?","a":"Uniqueness and subduing exist only for Allaah; every created being is subdued by one higher until it reaches The One, The Invincible Subduer, so what is called upon besides Allaah possesses nothing and worshipping it is falsehood."}]},{"chapter":51,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Waarith","arabic":"الوَارِث","meaning":"The Inheritor"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name occurs in the plural form in the Qur'aan in three places."},{"type":"quote","text":"And certainly We! We it is Who give life, and cause death, and We are the Inheritors.","ref":"Hijr 15:23"},{"type":"quote","text":"And (remember) Zakariya (Zachariah), when he cried to his Lord: \"O My Lord! Leave me not single (childless), though You are the Best of the inheritors.\"","ref":"Anbiyaa' 21:89"},{"type":"quote","text":"And how many a town (population) have We destroyed, which were thankless for its means of livelihood (disobeyed Allah, and His Messengers, by doing evil deeds and crimes)! And those are their dwellings, which have not been inhabited after them except a little. And verily! We have been the inheritors.","ref":"Qasas 28:58"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Waarith The Inheritor means the One who is everlasting after the creation has perished. Everyone besides Allaah will come to an end and disappear whilst Allaah is Al-Hayy The Ever-Living that never dies. The Everlasting that does not end. To Him is the return and the end. To Him is the final outcome and the final destination. The owners and what they owned will perish and Allaah will inherit the whole of creation as He is the Ever-Lasting and they will come to an end and He is the One who continues and they will disappear."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And certainly We! We it is Who give life, and cause death, and We are the Inheritors.","ref":"Hijr 15:23"},{"type":"p","text":"This means We will inherit the earth and what is on it by causing everyone to pass away so that no living creature is left, only Allaah when that time comes. So everyone will perish and pass away and Allaah alone will remain, The Everlasting who does not die. This is a warning to those who are distracted by the worldly life and occupied from what Allaah created them for and brought them into existence to actualize. The world and what is in it from the beginning of it to the end will be removed from its people and they will be removed from it. Allaah will inherit the earth and whoever is on it and He will return them to Him in order to reward or punish them for their actions."},{"type":"p","text":"In the last khutbah that 'Umar ibn 'Abdul 'Azeez gave, he praised and thanked Allaah then said, \"As for what follows. You were not created in jest. You will not be left neglected. You have a place of return and Allaah will descend to judge and separate between you. The one who is excluded from Allaah's mercy has failed and lost. Paradise, the width of the heavens and the earth will be forbidden for him."},{"type":"p","text":"Do you not know that a person will not be safe tomorrow except the one who takes warning from today and fears it, selling what will disappear for what will remain, a small amount for a large amount, fear for safety."},{"type":"p","text":"Do you not see that you are from the loins of those who have been destroyed and there will be after you the rest of mankind until you all will be returned to the best of inheritors?!"},{"type":"p","text":"Then you will follow, coming and going every day to Allaah. He has fulfilled his vow and his term will have ended until you will be covered in a crevice in the earth, in the depths of it, that is not paved or smooth. You have been separated from your loved ones and have come close to the soil. You will face the reckoning and pass it with your deeds, free from what you have left, in need of what you have put forward."},{"type":"p","text":"Fear Allaah O slaves of Allaah before the ending of His covenants and the sending of death upon you.\" Then he placed the edge of his upper garment over his face and wept and those around him also wept."}],"keyPoints":["This Name occurs in the plural form in the Qur'aan in three places (Hijr 15:23, Anbiyaa' 21:89, Qasas 28:58).","Al-Waarith means the One who is everlasting after the creation has perished; everyone besides Allaah will come to an end.","The owners and what they owned will perish and Allaah will inherit the whole of creation, then return them to Him to reward or punish them.","The Name is a warning to those distracted by the worldly life from what Allaah created them for.","'Umar ibn 'Abdul 'Azeez in his last khutbah reminded the people that they will all be returned to the best of inheritors."],"evidence":[{"text":"And certainly We! We it is Who give life, and cause death, and We are the Inheritors.","ref":"Hijr 15:23"},{"text":"\"O My Lord! Leave me not single (childless), though You are the Best of the inheritors.\"","ref":"Anbiyaa' 21:89"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Waarith mean?","a":"The Inheritor: the One who is everlasting after the creation has perished, who inherits the whole of creation."},{"q":"In what form and how many times does this Name occur in the Qur'aan?","a":"In the plural form, in three places."},{"q":"What warning does the meaning of Hijr 15:23 carry?","a":"It is a warning to those distracted by the worldly life and occupied from what Allaah created them for, since everything will perish and Allaah alone will remain."},{"q":"Whose last khutbah does the author quote in this chapter?","a":"'Umar ibn 'Abdul 'Azeez, who began, 'You were not created in jest. You will not be left neglected.'"}]},{"chapter":52,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Mutakabbir","arabic":"المُتَكَبِّر","meaning":"The Rightfully Proud"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found once in the Qur'aan. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Mutakabbir The Rightfully Proud is a Name which indicates Allaah's description of having pride and majesty. The letter 'taa' in Al-Mutakabbir is not one of giving and excess, rather it is of uniqueness and specialness. Magnificence is a description of Allaah which is suitable only to Him."},{"type":"p","text":"Qataadah said, \"He is the One who is rightfully proud over every evil.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Maqaatil said, \"The rightfully proud is far greater above every evil.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Aboo Ishaaq as-Subay'ee said, \"The One who is above and does not oppress His servants.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Maymoon bin Mehraan said, \"Above evil and bad deeds – only good comes from Him.\""},{"type":"p","text":"In conclusion, this Name indicates that Allaah is above the characteristics of the creation and that He is exalted and far above having likeness to them or that they are like Him. Allaah is raised above every defect and fault. He is the Rightfully Proud from evil, bad, oppression and every defect. This entails the affirmation of perfection for Him in His Names, Attributes and Actions."},{"type":"p","text":"As for the created servant, his station is that of worship, servitude, humility, humbleness, bowing and prostrating to Al-Kabeer, The Great, Al-'Adheem The Mighty possessing Might. Perhaps in this is a secret of the secrets behind remembering Allaah with takbeer saying 'Allaahu akbar' Allaah is the Most Great when bowing for rukoo' and sujood and mentioning His Greatness and Might during the bowing and prostration."},{"type":"p","text":"As for a servant being arrogant, especially about the purpose for which he was brought into existence and created to fulfil – worshipping Allaah alone and singling Him out for humility, humbleness and submissiveness – then Allaah will punish him with the greatest punishment and disgrace him in this world and the Next."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah mentioned in many places in his Mighty Book examples of arrogant people and nations. He made clear what punishments they were given in the world and what has been prepared for them in the Next Life of exemplary punishment. This is to clarify the path of the wrong-doers and in mentioning their state it will be a lesson and an admonition for those who take advice."},{"type":"p","text":"We ask Allaah to humble us before His Honour and that He protects us from the way of the arrogant people. He alone is the One to grant us what we ask and to help."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Mutakabbir is found once in the Qur'aan, in Hashr 59:23.","It indicates Allaah's description of having pride and majesty; the 'taa' in it is of uniqueness and specialness, not of giving and excess.","The Salaf explained it as being rightfully proud above every evil, above oppressing His servants, with only good coming from Him.","The Name indicates Allaah is above the characteristics of the creation and every defect, entailing perfection in His Names, Attributes and Actions.","The servant's station is humility and servitude; the arrogant servant is punished with the greatest punishment and disgraced in this world and the Next."],"evidence":[{"text":"the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Mutakabbir mean?","a":"The Rightfully Proud: a Name indicating Allaah's description of having pride and majesty, being above the characteristics of the creation and every defect, evil and oppression."},{"q":"What is the significance of the letter 'taa' in Al-Mutakabbir?","a":"It is not one of giving and excess, rather it is of uniqueness and specialness."},{"q":"How did Maymoon bin Mehraan explain Al-Mutakabbir?","a":"\"Above evil and bad deeds – only good comes from Him.\""},{"q":"What secret does the author suggest lies behind saying 'Allaahu akbar' when bowing and prostrating?","a":"That the servant's station is worship, humility and prostration to Al-Kabeer, Al-'Adheem, mentioning His Greatness and Might."}]},{"chapter":53,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Mu'min","arabic":"المُؤْمِن","meaning":"The Giver of Security"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Mu'min The Giver of Security is found in one aayah where Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"He is Allah than Whom there is La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He) the King, the Holy, the One Free from all defects, the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures, the Almighty, the Compeller, the Supreme. Glory be to Allah! (High is He) above all that they associate as partners with Him.","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Mu'min indicates magnificent meanings and lofty affairs. From the meanings of His Name Al-Mu'min is His witnessing tawheed for Himself (singling Allaah out alone for worship). It is the greatest witness, from the Greatest Witness for the greatest of things to witness."},{"type":"p","text":"Mujaahid said, \"Al-Mu'min The Giver of Security. The One who singles Himself out by the statement"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah bears witness that La ilaha illa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He)","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:18"},{"type":"p","text":"Another meaning of Al-Mu'min is the One who attests His Messengers and Prophets with proofs and clarifications that what they said and conveyed from Him is the truth without any doubting it, correct without any dispute."},{"type":"p","text":"This is the meaning of Qataadah's saying, \"Al-Mu'min: He believes in His saying that He is True.\""},{"type":"p","text":"From its meanings is His attesting to the witnesses for Him of tawheed (singling Allaah out alone for worship) and witness for them that what they said is true and correct."},{"type":"p","text":"From this meaning is what at-Tirmidhee and Ibn Maajah recorded from Al-Agharr Abu Muslim who narrated that he bears witness from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah, that they bear witness that the Prophet ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Whoever says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, (La ilaha illallah, wa Allahu akbar)' His Lord affirms his statement and says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Me, and I am the Greatest,' and when he says: 'There is none worthy of worship except for Allah, Alone, (La ilaha illallah, wahdahu)' Allah says: 'There is none worthy of worship except for Me and I am Alone.' And when he says: 'There is none worthy of worship except for Allah, Alone, without partner, (La ilaha illallah, wahdahu la sharika lahu)' Allah says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Me, Alone, I have no partner.' And when he says: 'There is none worthy of worship except for Allah, to Him belongs all that exists, and to Him is the praise, (La ilaha illallah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu)' Allah says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Me, to Me belongs all that exists, and to Me is the praise.' And when he says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Allah, and there is no might or power except by Allah, (La ilaha illallah, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah)' Allah says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Me, and there is no might or power except by Me.'\" And he used to say: \"Whoever says it in his illness, then dies, the Fire shall not consume him.\"","ref":"Tirmidhee 3430; Ibn Maajah 3794; Silsilah Saheehah 1390"},{"type":"p","text":"From its meanings is that Allaah grants security to His believing servants and God-fearing allies from His punishment and penalty. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"It is those who believe (in the Oneness of Allah and worship none but Him Alone) and confuse not their belief with Zulm (wrong i.e. by worshipping others besides Allah), for them (only) there is security and they are the guided.","ref":"An'aam 6:82"},{"type":"p","text":"From its meanings is His granting security to those who are fearful by giving them safety which is opposite to fear. As Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"(He) Who has fed them against hunger, and has made them safe from fear.","ref":"Quraish 106:4"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the meaning of Ibn 'Abbaas' speech, \"Al-Mu'min means that He grants security to His creation that He will not oppress them.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Every fearful person who is sincere in turning to Allaah will find Allaah granting him safety from fear. The safety and security of a slave and of a country is in Allaah's Hand."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Mu'min is found in one aayah, Hashr 59:23.","From its meanings is His witnessing tawheed for Himself, the greatest witness for the greatest of things (Aali 'Imraan 3:18).","It also means He attests His Messengers and Prophets with proofs that what they conveyed is the truth, and He attests to those who witness His tawheed.","It means He grants security to His believing servants from His punishment, and grants safety to the fearful who sincerely turn to Him.","Ibn 'Abbaas said Al-Mu'min means He grants security to His creation that He will not oppress them."],"evidence":[{"text":"the Giver of security, the Watcher over His creatures","ref":"Hashr 59:23"},{"text":"(He) Who has fed them against hunger, and has made them safe from fear.","ref":"Quraish 106:4"}],"recall":[{"q":"What are the meanings of Al-Mu'min mentioned by the author?","a":"His witnessing tawheed for Himself; attesting His Messengers with proofs; attesting to those who witness His tawheed; granting security to the believers from His punishment; and granting safety to the fearful."},{"q":"How did Ibn 'Abbaas explain Al-Mu'min?","a":"\"Al-Mu'min means that He grants security to His creation that He will not oppress them.\""},{"q":"What does Allaah say when a servant says 'La ilaha illallah, wa Allahu akbar'?","a":"His Lord affirms his statement and says: 'There is none worthy of worship except Me, and I am the Greatest.'"},{"q":"Which aayah is cited for Allaah granting security to the fearful?","a":"'(He) Who has fed them against hunger, and has made them safe from fear' (Quraish 106:4)."}]},{"chapter":54,"names":[{"translit":"As-Saadiq","arabic":"الصَّادِق","meaning":"The Truthful"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name As-Saadiq The Truthful is found in one aayah of Allaah's Book and it is His saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And unto those who are Jews, We forbade every (animal) with undivided hoof, and We forbade them the fat of the ox and the sheep except what adheres to their backs or their entrails, or is mixed up with a bone. Thus We recompensed them for their rebellion [committing crimes like murdering the Prophets, eating of Riba (usury), etc.]. And verily, We are Truthful.","ref":"An'aam 6:146"},{"type":"p","text":"This means the Truthful in His promise and His threat and in everything that He informs us about. He fulfilled what He promised His servants of victory and establishment on the earth."},{"type":"quote","text":"Then We fulfilled to them the promise, and We saved them and those whom We willed.","ref":"Anbiyaa' 21:9"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah has promised those among you who believe, and do righteous good deeds, that He will certainly grant them succession to (the present rulers) in the earth, as He granted it to those before them, and that He will grant them the authority to practise their religion, that which He has chosen for them (i.e. Islam). And He will surely give them in exchange a safe security after their fear (provided) they (believers) worship Me and do not associate anything (in worship) with Me. But whoever disbelieved after this, they are the Fasiqun (rebellious, disobedient to Allah).","ref":"Noor 24:55"},{"type":"p","text":"He fulfilled what He promised His servants of a great victory and entrance into blessed gardens. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And they will say: \"All the praises and thanks be to Allah Who has fulfilled His Promise to us and has made us inherit (this) land. We can dwell in Paradise where we will; how excellent a reward for the (pious good) workers!\"","ref":"Zumar 39:74"},{"type":"p","text":"He is the Truthful One who does not break His promise. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah's Promise is the Truth, and whose words can be truer than those of Allah? (Of course, none).","ref":"Nisaa 4:122"},{"type":"p","text":"From the effects of belief in this Name is that a good-doer does not fear being given too little or overburdened by oppression. He neither fears losing the weight of a speck of dust because Allaah has promised – and He is The Truthful – to give those who do good deeds their rewards. Even if it be the weight of a speck of dust He will reward it and not let it go to waste. Indeed He multiplies it for whomever He wills and He gives a tremendous reward from Himself."},{"type":"p","text":"As for the evil doer, He recompenses his evil deed with the like of it and He removes it from him after repentance, regret, seeking forgiveness, good deeds and calamities. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"They are those from whom We shall accept the best of their deeds and overlook their evil deeds. (They shall be) among the dwellers of Paradise, a promise of truth, which they have been promised.","ref":"Ahqaaf 46:16"}],"keyPoints":["The Name As-Saadiq is found in one aayah of Allaah's Book, An'aam 6:146.","It means the Truthful in His promise and His threat and in everything He informs us about.","He fulfilled what He promised His servants of victory and establishment on the earth, and of entrance into blessed gardens.","From the effects of belief in this Name: the good-doer does not fear oppression or losing even the weight of a speck of dust of reward.","The evil doer is recompensed with the like of his evil deed, and it is removed from him after repentance, regret, seeking forgiveness, good deeds and calamities."],"evidence":[{"text":"Thus We recompensed them for their rebellion. And verily, We are Truthful.","ref":"An'aam 6:146"},{"text":"Allah's Promise is the Truth, and whose words can be truer than those of Allah? (Of course, none).","ref":"Nisaa 4:122"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Saadiq mean?","a":"The Truthful in His promise and His threat and in everything that He informs us about."},{"q":"In which aayah is the Name As-Saadiq found?","a":"An'aam 6:146, ending 'And verily, We are Truthful.'"},{"q":"What is an effect of belief in this Name for the good-doer?","a":"He does not fear being given too little or oppressed, nor losing even the weight of a speck of dust, because the Truthful has promised to reward good deeds."},{"q":"Through what is an evil deed removed from the evil doer?","a":"Through repentance, regret, seeking forgiveness, good deeds and calamities."}]},{"chapter":55,"names":[{"translit":"An-Noor","arabic":"النُّور","meaning":"The Light"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found in the Noble Qur'aan in Allaah's statement,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth. The parable of His Light is as (if there were) a niche and within it a lamp, the lamp is in glass, the glass as it were a brilliant star, lit from a blessed tree, an olive, neither of the east (i.e. neither it gets sun-rays only in the morning) nor of the west (i.e. nor it gets sun-rays only in the afternoon, but it is exposed to the sun all day long), whose oil would almost glow forth (of itself), though no fire touched it. Light upon Light! Allah guides to His Light whom He wills. And Allah sets forth parables for mankind, and Allah is All-Knower of everything.","ref":"Noor 24:35"},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykh 'AbdurRahmaan bin Sa'dee spoke comprehensively regarding the meaning and explanation of this Name. \"An-Noor (Light) is of two types regarding Allaah's Attribute:"},{"type":"p","text":"Physical Light – Noor Hissee. It is what He is described with of magnificent light. If the veil were lifted from His Face, the splendour of His Face and the light of His majesty would burn everything of the creation in sight."},{"type":"p","text":"This light cannot be explained except by way of this Prophetic example which was given to explain its great meaning. None of creation will be able to bear the light of Allaah's Face if it appeared to them. However, the Lord will give people in the Hereafter a perfect life and will help them with this. They will be able to see the Mighty Lord. All of the lights in the high heavens are from His light. Indeed the light of the gardens of pleasure (paradise) whose width is of the heavens and the earth – and its vastness is only known to Allaah – is from His light."},{"type":"p","text":"So the light of the throne, the footstool and of paradise is from His light rather than from the light of the sun, moon or stars."},{"type":"p","text":"Abstract Light – Noor Ma'nawee. This light is the light of the hearts of His Prophets, pure people, allies and angels."},{"type":"p","text":"It is from the lights of knowing Him and loving Him. Knowledge of Allaah in the hearts of His believing allies is light according to how much they know His majestic descriptions and how much they believed in His beautiful attributes. Every one of His descriptions has an effect upon their hearts. Knowing Allaah the Mawlaa The Protector is the greatest knowledge there is and having knowledge of Him is the most mighty of sciences. All beneficial knowledge is light in the hearts. So how about this knowledge which is the best science, exalted foundation and base of it...\""},{"type":"p","text":"In conclusion, as An-Noor The Light is from Allaah's Names and Attributes, His religion is light, His Messengers are light, His speech is light, His honourable abode for His servants is light which radiates and shines. Light kindles in the hearts of His believing servants and runs upon their tongues, it appears on their faces. Allaah will complete this light upon them on the Day of Resurrection as He said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Their Light will run forward before them and with (their Records – Books of deeds) in their right hands they will say: \"Our Lord! Keep perfect our Light for us [and do not put it off till we cross over the Sirat (a slippery bridge over the Hell) safely] and grant us forgiveness. Verily, You are Able to do all things.\"","ref":"Tahreem 66:8"}],"keyPoints":["The Name An-Noor is found in Allaah's statement, 'Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth' (Noor 24:35).","Ibn Sa'dee explained that Light, as Allaah's Attribute, is of two types: Physical Light (Noor Hissee) and Abstract Light (Noor Ma'nawee).","Physical Light: if the veil were lifted from His Face, its splendour would burn everything of the creation in sight; the light of the throne, footstool and paradise is from His light.","Abstract Light is the light in the hearts of His Prophets, allies and angels from knowing and loving Him; knowledge of Allaah is the greatest knowledge.","His religion, Messengers, speech and abode are light, and He will complete the believers' light on the Day of Resurrection."],"evidence":[{"text":"Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth... Light upon Light! Allah guides to His Light whom He wills.","ref":"Noor 24:35"},{"text":"\"Our Lord! Keep perfect our Light for us and grant us forgiveness. Verily, You are Able to do all things.\"","ref":"Tahreem 66:8"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does An-Noor mean, and in which aayah is it found?","a":"The Light; found in 'Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth...' (Noor 24:35)."},{"q":"What are the two types of Light regarding Allaah's Attribute according to Ibn Sa'dee?","a":"Physical Light (Noor Hissee) and Abstract Light (Noor Ma'nawee)."},{"q":"What would happen if the veil were lifted from Allaah's Face?","a":"The splendour of His Face and the light of His majesty would burn everything of the creation in sight."},{"q":"What is Abstract Light (Noor Ma'nawee)?","a":"The light of the hearts of His Prophets, pure people, allies and angels, from the lights of knowing Him and loving Him."}]},{"chapter":56,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Muhsin","arabic":"المُحْسِن","meaning":"The One whose actions are all perfect and good"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name does not occur in the Qur'aan as a noun, however the verb form of it does occur in Allaah's saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and do good as Allah has been good to you,","ref":"Qasas 28:77"},{"type":"quote","text":"He was indeed good to me, when He took me out of the prison, and brought you (all here) out of the bedouin-life,","ref":"Yoosuf 12:100"},{"type":"p","text":"The Sunnah confirms this Name for Allaah. One example is the Prophet's ﷺ saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"If you judge then be just, if you kill – do it well, for indeed Allaah is Muhsin (Perfect) and loves those who do good.\"","ref":"At-Tabaraanee, Awsat 5735 and Aboo Na'eem with a good chain; Silsilah Saheehah 1/761"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Allaah's Name Al-Muhsin returns back to virtue, blessings, generosity, honour, giving and bestowing. Ihsaan (perfection) is a permanent description of Allaah. Nothing that exists is without His perfection for the blinking of an eye by Him supplying, kindly bestowing and helping. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Who made everything He has created good, and He began the creation of man from clay.","ref":"Sajdah 32:7"},{"type":"quote","text":"and He shaped you and made good your shapes, and to Him is the final Return.","ref":"Taghaabun 64:3"},{"type":"p","text":"The greatest perfection is success for this religion, the hearts turning to obedience to the Lord of the worlds, being firm upon the truth and guidance until death. Until he crowns that with the greatest honour and noblest perfection: entrance into the gardens on the Day of Resurrection in addition to seeing Allaah – Al-Kareem The Generous, Ar-Rahmaan The All-Merciful, Al-Muhsin The Perfect, Al-Mannaan The Generous. We ask Allaah from His mighty grace and abundant perfection."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah loves His servants to draw close to Him according to the meanings of His Names. He is ar-Rahmaan, The All-Merciful, He loves those who are merciful. He is Al-Kareem The Generous, He loves those who are generous. He is Al-Muhsin The One whose actions are all perfect and good, He loves those who do good. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"and do good. Truly, Allah loves Al-Muhsinun (the good-doers).","ref":"Baqarah 2:195"},{"type":"p","text":"Examples of doing good include: doing good to Allaah's servants; treating parents well; keeping the ties of kinship; fulfilling rights; helping those in need; averting harm from the people; striving to bring good to them."},{"type":"p","text":"There are many more ways of doing good to Allaah's servants. In many verses Allaah has promised those doers of good a great reward brought forward in this life and the next. Allaah gathered together these two rewards for the doers of good in His saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"So Allah gave them the reward of this world, and the excellent reward of the Hereafter. And Allah loves Al-Muhsinun (the good-doers).","ref":"Aali 'Imraan 3:148"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah make us of them through His kindness and generosity."}],"keyPoints":["The Name Al-Muhsin does not occur in the Qur'aan as a noun, but its verb form does (Qasas 28:77, Yoosuf 12:100); the Sunnah confirms the Name.","Its meaning returns back to virtue, blessings, generosity, honour, giving and bestowing.","Ihsaan (perfection) is a permanent description of Allaah; nothing that exists is without His perfection for the blinking of an eye.","The greatest perfection is success in this religion and firmness upon the truth until death, crowned with entrance into the gardens and seeing Allaah.","Allaah loves His servants to draw close to Him according to the meanings of His Names: He is Al-Muhsin and loves those who do good."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"...for indeed Allaah is Muhsin (Perfect) and loves those who do good.\"","ref":"At-Tabaraanee, Awsat 5735; Silsilah Saheehah 1/761"},{"text":"and do good. Truly, Allah loves Al-Muhsinun (the good-doers).","ref":"Baqarah 2:195"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Muhsin mean?","a":"The One whose actions are all perfect and good; its meaning returns back to virtue, blessings, generosity, honour, giving and bestowing."},{"q":"Does Al-Muhsin occur in the Qur'aan as a noun?","a":"No; only its verb form occurs (e.g. Qasas 28:77 and Yoosuf 12:100). The Sunnah confirms the Name."},{"q":"Which hadeeth confirms the Name Al-Muhsin?","a":"\"If you judge then be just, if you kill – do it well, for indeed Allaah is Muhsin and loves those who do good.\" (At-Tabaraanee; Silsilah Saheehah)"},{"q":"Give examples of doing good mentioned by the author.","a":"Treating parents well, keeping ties of kinship, fulfilling rights, helping those in need, averting harm from people and striving to bring good to them."},{"q":"What is the greatest perfection according to the author?","a":"Success for this religion, hearts turning to obedience, firmness upon truth until death, crowned with entering the gardens and seeing Allaah."}]},{"chapter":57,"names":[{"translit":"Ad-Dayyaan","arabic":"الدَّيَّان","meaning":"The Supreme Judge"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ad-Dayyaan is a confirmed Name of Allaah in the sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ."},{"type":"p","text":"Jaabir bin 'Abdullaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"I purchased a camel and rode it hard for a month until I reached Syria. 'Abdullah ibn Unays was there, and I sent word to him, saying, 'Jabir is at the door.' The messenger returned and said, 'Jabir ibn 'Abdullah?' 'Yes,' I replied. So 'Abdullah came out and embraced me. I said, 'A hadith reached me which I had not heard before and I feared that one of us might die.'\" He went on, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Allah will gather His slaves or people naked, uncircumcised, without anything.' We asked, 'What is meant by \"without anything\"?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'They will have nothing with them.' 'They will be called by a voice that is heard from afar (and I think that he said, 'as if it was from close at hand'), saying, \"I am the King, I am the Supreme Judge. None of the people of the Fire will enter the Fire while any of the people of the Garden are seeking him for an injustice he did to him. None of the people of the Garden will enter the Garden while any of the people of the Fire are seeking him for some injustice he did to him. Even for a slap.\"' I asked, 'How is this? We come to Allah naked and without any worldly goods?' He said, 'This applies to good actions and evil actions.'\"","ref":"Ahmad, Al-Musnad 3/495; Bukhaaree, Al-Adab al-Mufrad 970; Ibn Abee 'Aasim, As-Sunnah 514; Al-Haakim, Al-Mustadrak 2/437; and others"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Haakim added, \"The Messenger of Allaah ﷺ recited,"},{"type":"quote","text":"This Day shall every person be recompensed for what he earned. No injustice (shall be done to anybody).","ref":"Ghaafir 40:17"},{"type":"p","text":"Ad-Dayyaan The Supreme Judge means the One who rewards or punishes, the One to take Account. Allaah will gather together the first and the last people on the Day of Resurrection naked without clothes, barefooted without footwear, uncircumcised and standing without any worldly possessions. Then He will reward or punish them and bring them to account for what they have put forward in their worldly life of deeds – if they were good then it will be good and if they were bad then it will be bad."},{"type":"p","text":"If an intelligent person knows that the Lord is The Supreme Judge and that the Day of Resurrection is a day of recompense and account, and that he will meet Allaah on that Day without any doubt, and that on that Day he will find all of his deeds that he performed brought forth – the good deeds and the bad, the fine deeds and the evil ones. Indeed he will prepare to be taken to account for that day and ready his provisions."},{"type":"p","text":"The astute clever person is the one who passes judgement upon himself and takes himself to account whilst he has respite in this life to do so and has time to do good deeds. The weak person is the one who is heedless of it which comes from being in sin and error and following his desires until regret suddenly comes upon him. A poet spoke about this with the following words:"},{"type":"quote","text":"And by Allaah indeed oppression is despicable.\nThe evil doer is still in his plentiful oppression.\nTo the Judge on the Day of Judgement we pass away,\nAnd in front of Allah those who have grievances will gather.","ref":"A poet"},{"type":"p","text":"The rightly guided Khaleefah 'Umar bin Al-Khattaab said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Bring yourselves to account before you are brought to account. Weigh your deeds before they are weighed. It will be easier for your account tomorrow if you bring yourselves to account today. Beautify yourselves for the greatest exhibition – on that Day you will be brought for judgement and nothing will be hidden from amongst you.\"","ref":"Ibn Abee ad-Dunyaa, Muhaasibatun Nafs no. 2"}],"keyPoints":["Ad-Dayyaan is a confirmed Name of Allaah in the sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ, in the hadeeth of Jaabir from 'Abdullah ibn Unays: \"I am the King, I am the Supreme Judge.\"","Ad-Dayyaan means the One who rewards or punishes, the One to take Account.","Allaah will gather the first and the last people on the Day of Resurrection naked, barefooted, uncircumcised and without any worldly possessions, then reward or punish them for their deeds.","Whoever knows that the Lord is The Supreme Judge and that the Day of Resurrection is a day of recompense and account will prepare for that Day and ready his provisions.","The astute person takes himself to account whilst he has respite in this life, while the weak person is heedless until regret suddenly comes upon him."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"I am the King, I am the Supreme Judge. None of the people of the Fire will enter the Fire while any of the people of the Garden are seeking him for an injustice he did to him...\"","ref":"Ahmad, Al-Musnad 3/495; Bukhaaree, Al-Adab al-Mufrad 970"},{"text":"This Day shall every person be recompensed for what he earned. No injustice (shall be done to anybody).","ref":"Ghaafir 40:17"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ad-Dayyaan mean?","a":"The Supreme Judge: the One who rewards or punishes, the One to take Account."},{"q":"Where is the Name Ad-Dayyaan confirmed?","a":"In the sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ, in the hadeeth Jaabir bin 'Abdullaah travelled a month to Syria to hear from 'Abdullah ibn Unays: \"I am the King, I am the Supreme Judge.\""},{"q":"Which aayah did the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ recite, according to Al-Haakim's addition?","a":"\"This Day shall every person be recompensed for what he earned. No injustice (shall be done to anybody).\" [Ghaafir 40:17]"},{"q":"Who is the astute clever person according to the chapter?","a":"The one who passes judgement upon himself and takes himself to account whilst he has respite in this life and has time to do good deeds."},{"q":"What did 'Umar bin Al-Khattaab say about taking oneself to account?","a":"\"Bring yourselves to account before you are brought to account. Weigh your deeds before they are weighed...\""}]},{"chapter":58,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Muqaddim","arabic":"المُقَدِّم","meaning":"The One who gives precedence"},{"translit":"Al-Mu'akhkhir","arabic":"المُؤَخِّر","meaning":"The One who puts back"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These two Names are found in authentic ahaadeeth from the Prophet ﷺ. An example of which is that Abu Musa narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to invoke Allaah with the following invocation:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"O Lord forgive me my faults, my ignorance, my immoderation in all my affairs. You are more knowing about them than myself. O Allaah, grant me forgiveness for my faults the ones that I committed deliberately, unintentionally or out of jest and all that I did. O Allaah, grant me forgiveness for what I put forward or sent back, what I committed secretly or in the open. You are the One who gives precedence and the One who puts back and You are able to do all things.\" Agreed upon (found in Saheeh Al-Bukhaaree and Saheeh Muslim)","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhaaree 6398; Saheeh Muslim"},{"type":"p","text":"These two Names are from those that are paired opposites. One Name cannot be used alone for Allaah without the other as perfection comes when the two Names are together. Giving precedence and putting back are two descriptions of Allaah indicating Allaah's perfect Ability, execution of His Will and His complete Wisdom."},{"type":"p","text":"They are from His Attributes of Action as giving precedence and putting back are connected to the creation in self, action and description. This giving precedence and putting back is universal such as the giving precedence to some of creation over others or putting back some of creation over others. It is also like giving precedence to the cause and overall effect; and the conditions over their agreements among other examples. Another example of giving precedence and putting back is in creation and predestination."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples of giving precedence and putting back in terms of legislation is where the Prophets are better than the creation. Some Prophets are better than others. Some of his servants are better than others. He gave precedence to them in knowledge, faith, action, manners and in all descriptions and He also put them back with some of those. All of this is according to His wisdom. He puts forward whoever He wills of His creation to His mercy by His success and grace and He puts back whoever He wills of that by His justice."},{"type":"p","text":"These two names occur in the context of seeking forgiveness for all sins put forward and put back, secret and open, mistakenly done or intended. From this it is known that sins put back a servant and destroys him. Allaah forgiving and pardoning His servant gives him precedence and raises him. Command is all for Allaah in His hand. He debases and raises, He gives honour and humiliates, He gives and prevents whomever Allaah has written to have honour, status and precedence and no one can prevent him from that. Whoever Allaah has written to be humiliated, debased and put back, no one can help him escape from that."},{"type":"p","text":"From the fruits of believing in this Name is having motivation to give precedence to what Allaah gave precedence to and to put back what Allaah put back. The Prophet ﷺ had strong motivation in seeking to give precedence to what Allaah gave precedence to and to start with what He started with. Due to this he started with (Mount) Safaa in the Sa'ee. He ﷺ said, 'We begin with what Allaah began with'. He ﷺ started with the face, the two hands and then the head in ritual ablution (wudhoo). He did not change this even once."},{"type":"p","text":"This is so in all the affairs of the religion. It is obligatory to give precedence to whoever Allaah gave precedence to and to put back those that He put back. Also to love those He loved and hate those He hated. This is the most trustworthy handhold of faith."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Muqaddim and Al-Mu'akhkhir are found in authentic ahaadeeth, such as the Prophet's ﷺ invocation: \"You are the One who gives precedence and the One who puts back.\"","They are paired opposite Names: one cannot be used alone for Allaah without the other, as perfection comes when the two are together.","Giving precedence and putting back indicate Allaah's perfect Ability, execution of His Will and His complete Wisdom, and are from His Attributes of Action.","Giving precedence and putting back is both universal (in creation and predestination) and legislative (e.g. the Prophets being better than the creation and some Prophets better than others).","Sins put back a servant and destroy him, while Allaah's forgiveness and pardon give him precedence and raise him.","A fruit of believing in these Names is giving precedence to what Allaah gave precedence to and putting back what He put back, as the Prophet ﷺ began with Safaa and followed the order of wudhoo."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"...O Allaah, grant me forgiveness for what I put forward or sent back, what I committed secretly or in the open. You are the One who gives precedence and the One who puts back and You are able to do all things.\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhaaree 6398; Saheeh Muslim"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Muqaddim mean?","a":"The One who gives precedence."},{"q":"What does Al-Mu'akhkhir mean?","a":"The One who puts back."},{"q":"Why can't one of these two Names be used alone for Allaah?","a":"Because they are paired opposites, and perfection comes when the two Names are together."},{"q":"In which hadeeth do these two Names occur?","a":"In the Prophet's ﷺ invocation for forgiveness narrated by Abu Musa: \"...You are the One who gives precedence and the One who puts back and You are able to do all things\" (Agreed upon)."},{"q":"Give an example from the chapter of the Prophet ﷺ giving precedence to what Allaah gave precedence to.","a":"He started with Safaa in the Sa'ee, saying 'We begin with what Allaah began with', and he started with the face, the two hands and then the head in wudhoo, never changing this."}]},{"chapter":59,"names":[{"translit":"At-Tayyib","arabic":"الطَّيِّب","meaning":"The Pure One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found in a hadeeth by Aboo Hurayrah. Allah's Messenger ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"O people, Allah is Good and He therefore, accepts only that which is good. And Allah commanded the believers as He commanded the Messengers by saying: \"O Messengers, eat of the good things, and do good deeds; verily I am aware of what you do\" [Mu'minoon 23:51]. And He said: \"O those who believe, eat of the good things that We gave you\" [Baqarah 2:172]. He then made a mention of a person who travels widely, his hair disheveled and covered with dust. He lifts his hand towards the sky (and thus makes the supplication): \"O Lord, O Lord,\" whereas his diet is unlawful, his drink is unlawful, and his clothes are unlawful and his nourishment is unlawful. How can his supplication then be accepted?\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 1015"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning is that Allaah is pure and far removed from every imperfection and defect. The origin of At-Tayyib is purity and safety from evil. Allaah was always and is still perfect in His Self, His Attributes, His Actions and His Speech originating from His perfection."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah is complete so He did actions suiting His perfection. From here Allaah's Beautiful Names and lofty Attributes indicate what He does and says and what He does not do or say. Allaah is complete so He did actions suiting His perfection and majesty. He does not do or say anything that opposes that. He is Pure, His actions are pure, His Attributes are the purest matter. His Names are the purest Names. His Name is At-Tayyib the Pure. Nothing originates from Him except goodness. Nothing ascends to Him except goodness. Nothing draws near to Him except goodness. His speech is pure and to Him ascends good speech. His actions are pure and good and good actions are raised up to Him. All goodness is for Him and ascribed to Him, originating from Him and ending with Him. The Prophet ﷺ said in the (previous) hadeeth, \"Indeed Allaah is Pure and does not accept but the pure.\" This indicates that Allaah does not accept actions or speech if they are not described as being pure and good."},{"type":"p","text":"This is general for every action or speech. A believing person does not act except that it is righteous. He does not speak except that it is good. He only earns good and he only spends from good. Goodness describes actions, speech and beliefs. These are divided into good and bad as Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"Not equal are Al-Khabith (all that is evil and bad as regards things, deeds, beliefs, persons, foods, etc.) and At-Taiyib (all that is good as regards things, deeds, beliefs, persons, foods, etc.), even though the abundance of Al-Khabith (evil) may please you.\"","ref":"Maa'idah 5:100"},{"type":"p","text":"The pure religion, all of it, is a pure religion in beliefs, rulings and manners. Its beliefs are that which return back to faith in Allaah, His angels, His books, His Messengers, the Last Day and predestination, the good and the bad of it. These are the correct beliefs which make the heart tranquil and make the souls pure. These make the one who believes in them and stick to them reach the lofty objective and best good. Its manners are the best rulings and the best of manners. Through them lies the rectification of the religion, the worldly life and the Next Life; without them all rectification is missing."},{"type":"p","text":"When a believer is pure in this world in his beliefs, actions and speech, Allaah blesses him in the everlasting abode by entering him into the abode of the pure and good which only admits good. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And those who kept their duty to their Lord will be led to Paradise in groups, till, when they reach it, and its gates will be opened (before their arrival for their reception) and its keepers will say: Salamun 'Alaikum (peace be upon you)! You have done well, so enter here to abide therein.\"","ref":"Zumar 39:73"},{"type":"p","text":"The letter 'faa' 'so' in Arabic comes after طِبْتُم 'you have done well' which implies that the reason for entering paradise was due to them being pure. Due to them being good and pure it will be said to them 'enter paradise'."},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah make us of those servants who are good and pure, those to whom it will be said on the Day of Resurrection,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Enter Paradise, no fear shall be on you, nor shall you grieve.\"","ref":"A'raaf 7:49"}],"keyPoints":["At-Tayyib is found in the hadeeth of Aboo Hurayrah: \"O people, Allah is Good and He therefore, accepts only that which is good.\"","At-Tayyib means that Allaah is pure and far removed from every imperfection and defect; the origin of the word is purity and safety from evil.","Allaah is pure in His Self, Attributes, Actions and Speech; nothing originates from Him, ascends to Him or draws near to Him except goodness.","Allaah does not accept actions or speech unless they are pure and good, so the believer only acts righteously, speaks good, earns good and spends from good.","The pure religion is pure in beliefs, rulings and manners, and the one pure in this world is entered into Paradise, the abode of the pure, as indicated by \"You have done well, so enter here\" (Zumar 39:73)."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"O people, Allah is Good and He therefore, accepts only that which is good...\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 1015"},{"text":"Not equal are Al-Khabith and At-Taiyib, even though the abundance of Al-Khabith (evil) may please you.","ref":"Maa'idah 5:100"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does At-Tayyib mean?","a":"The Pure One: Allaah is pure and far removed from every imperfection and defect; the origin of At-Tayyib is purity and safety from evil."},{"q":"In which hadeeth is the Name At-Tayyib found?","a":"The hadeeth of Aboo Hurayrah: \"O people, Allah is Good and He therefore, accepts only that which is good...\" (Saheeh Muslim 1015)."},{"q":"What does the hadeeth \"Allaah is Pure and does not accept but the pure\" indicate?","a":"That Allaah does not accept actions or speech if they are not described as being pure and good."},{"q":"What does the author derive from the letter 'faa' after 'you have done well' in Zumar 39:73?","a":"That the reason for entering Paradise was due to them being pure; due to them being good and pure it will be said to them 'enter Paradise'."}]},{"chapter":60,"names":[{"translit":"Ash-Shaafee","arabic":"الشَّافِي","meaning":"The One who Cures"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ash-Shaafee The One who Cures is from the Names found authentically in the Prophetic Sunnah. It is authentically recorded in the two Saheehs from 'Aa'ishah who said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"The Prophet ﷺ used to treat some of his wives by passing his right hand over the place of ailment and used to say, \"O Allah, Lord of the people! Remove the harm and heal the patient, for You are The Healer. There is no cure except Your cure; healing that will leave behind no ailment.\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhaaree 5743"},{"type":"p","text":"The meaning of Ash-Shaafee is the One from whom comes the cure - curing the chests from doubt, uncertainties, envy, jealousy and other than those from the diseases of the heart. Curing the body from illnesses and defects and no one else is able to do this. There is no cure except His cure and no one can cure except Him. As Ibraaheem al-Khaleel said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And when I am ill, it is He who cures me.","ref":"Shu'araa 26:80"},{"type":"p","text":"This means He alone is the One to cure, without partners. Due to this it is a must upon every adult to have firm belief that there is no one to cure except Allaah."},{"type":"p","text":"Due to this, from the best ways to Allaah in seeking a cure from illnesses and diseases is seeking nearness tawassul by singling Him out alone for Lordship and that the cure is in His Hand alone. There is no cure for anyone except by His permission. The command is His command, the creation is His creation. Everything is by His direction. What He willed happened and what He did not will, did not happen and there is no might nor strength except from Him."},{"type":"p","text":"This, the servant's belief and faith that The Shaafee The One to cure is Allaah alone and that the cure is in His Hand, does not prevent him from seeking beneficial means of therapy, treatment or taking beneficial medicines. There are many ahaadeeth from the Prophet ﷺ regarding treatment with the mention of beneficial good medicines and that does not negate reliance (tawakkul) upon Allaah or the belief that the cure is in His Hand."},{"type":"p","text":"Bukhaaree relates in his Saheeh from Aboo Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"There is no disease that Allah has created, except that He also has created its treatment.\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhaaree 5678"},{"type":"p","text":"In the Musnad (of Imaam Ahmad) Usaamah bin Shareek said, the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Allaah did not send down a sickness except that He sent down its cure, whether a person knows it or not or is ignorant of it or not.\"","ref":"Ahmad 4/278; Aboo Daawood 3855; Ibn Hibbaan 486; Al-Haakim 1/121 and others with an authentic chain"},{"type":"p","text":"I ask Allaah the Mighty, the Lord of the people, the remover of harm, the One who cures without whom there is no cure except His, to cure our sick and the Muslims who are sick."}],"keyPoints":["Ash-Shaafee is found authentically in the Sunnah, in the Prophet's ﷺ supplication: \"Remove the harm and heal the patient, for You are The Healer.\"","Ash-Shaafee is the One from whom comes the cure: curing the chests from doubts, envy and the diseases of the heart, and curing the body from illnesses and defects.","There is no cure except His cure and no one can cure except Him, as Ibraaheem said: \"And when I am ill, it is He who cures me.\"","From the best ways of seeking a cure is seeking nearness (tawassul) to Allaah by singling Him out for Lordship and affirming that the cure is in His Hand alone.","Believing that the cure is only from Allaah does not prevent seeking beneficial treatment and medicines, and that does not negate reliance (tawakkul) upon Allaah."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"O Allah, Lord of the people! Remove the harm and heal the patient, for You are The Healer. There is no cure except Your cure...\"","ref":"Saheeh al-Bukhaaree 5743"},{"text":"And when I am ill, it is He who cures me.","ref":"Shu'araa 26:80"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ash-Shaafee mean?","a":"The One who Cures: the One from whom comes the cure, curing the chests from doubts and diseases of the heart and the body from illnesses and defects; no one else is able to do this."},{"q":"Which aayah of Ibraaheem does the author cite?","a":"\"And when I am ill, it is He who cures me.\" [Shu'araa 26:80]"},{"q":"Does believing Allaah alone cures prevent taking medicine?","a":"No. It does not prevent seeking beneficial therapy, treatment or medicines, and that does not negate reliance (tawakkul) upon Allaah."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say about disease and its treatment (Bukhaaree, from Aboo Hurayrah)?","a":"\"There is no disease that Allah has created, except that He also has created its treatment.\""}]},{"chapter":61,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Jameel","arabic":"الجَمِيل","meaning":"The Beautiful"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Jameel The Beautiful is a Name that is established in the sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ. Muslim reports it in his saheeh from 'Abdullaah bin Mas'ood that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"He who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride shall not enter Paradise. A man said: Verily a person loves to have nice clothes and shoes. He ﷺ remarked: Verily, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Pride is disdaining the truth (out of self-conceit) and contempt for the people.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 91"},{"type":"p","text":"This noble Name indicates the establishment of beauty for Allaah in His Names, Attributes, His Self and His Actions. Ibnul Qayyim said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"His beauty is of four levels: beauty of Self, beauty of Attributes, beauty of Actions and beauty of Names. All of His Names are beautiful and perfect, all His Attributes are perfect, all of His Actions are from wisdom, are of benefit and are just and merciful. As for the beauty of Self and what it means, then it is an issue that no one perceives other than Him. No one apart from Him knows. The creation only knows what has been explained to the noblest of His servants. For indeed this beauty is protected from others, veiled with the raiment of the cloak and waist wrapper as His Messenger ﷺ said in what is related from him, \"Magnificence is my cloak and greatness is my lower garment.\" So what do you think about beauty that is guarded by attributes of perfection and veiled with descriptions of greatness and majesty? From this meaning some of the meanings of beauty of His Self is understood. A servant advances in knowing the Actions to knowing the Attributes and from knowing the Attributes to knowing the Self. If he witnesses something of the beauty of the Actions he takes it as a proof of the beauty of the Attributes then he takes the beauty of the Attributes as a proof of the beauty of His Self...\"","ref":"Ibn Al-Qayyim, Al-Fawaa'id p. 322 (the hadeeth within it: Musnad Ahmad 2/376, narrated by Aboo Hurayrah)"},{"type":"p","text":"This and the completion of blessings upon the people of paradise is the greatest blessing of them seeing their God, their Lord and beautiful Majestic Protector."},{"type":"p","text":"Indeed it is the greatest of what they are given, the noblest of what they obtain, the apple of their eyes, the delight of the souls, the pleasure of their hearts, the light on their faces and the greatest honour. In Saheeh Muslim Suhayb narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"When those deserving Paradise enter Paradise, the Blessed and the Exalted will ask: 'Do you wish Me to give you anything more?' They will say: 'Have You not brightened our faces? Have You not made us enter Paradise and saved us from the Fire?' He (the narrator) said: He (God) will lift the veil, and of things given to them nothing would be dearer to them than the sight of their Lord, the Mighty and the Glorious.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 181"},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah! We ask You for the delight of seeing Your Noble Face, we yearn to meet You without harm or trials that lead one astray."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Jameel is established in the sunnah in the hadeeth of 'Abdullaah bin Mas'ood: \"Verily, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty.\"","The Name indicates the establishment of beauty for Allaah in His Names, Attributes, His Self and His Actions.","Ibnul Qayyim said His beauty is of four levels: beauty of Self, of Attributes, of Actions and of Names; the beauty of His Self is something no one perceives other than Him.","A servant advances from knowing the beauty of the Actions to the Attributes, and from the Attributes to the Self, taking each as proof of the next.","The greatest blessing for the people of Paradise is seeing their Lord, as in the hadeeth of Suhayb in Saheeh Muslim."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"Verily, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Pride is disdaining the truth (out of self-conceit) and contempt for the people.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 91"},{"text":"\"...He will lift the veil, and of things given to them nothing would be dearer to them than the sight of their Lord, the Mighty and the Glorious.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 181"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Jameel mean and what does it indicate?","a":"The Beautiful; it indicates the establishment of beauty for Allaah in His Names, Attributes, His Self and His Actions."},{"q":"Which hadeeth establishes the Name Al-Jameel?","a":"The hadeeth of 'Abdullaah bin Mas'ood in Saheeh Muslim: \"Verily, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty...\""},{"q":"What are the four levels of Allaah's beauty according to Ibnul Qayyim?","a":"Beauty of Self, beauty of Attributes, beauty of Actions and beauty of Names."},{"q":"What is the greatest blessing given to the people of Paradise?","a":"Seeing their Lord; nothing given to them would be dearer to them than the sight of their Lord (hadeeth of Suhayb, Saheeh Muslim)."}]},{"chapter":62,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Qaabid","arabic":"القَابِض","meaning":"The Withholder"},{"translit":"Al-Baasit","arabic":"البَاسِط","meaning":"The Granter of extensive provision"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These two Names are found in the Prophetic sunnah. In the Sunan and in the Musnad of Imaam Ahmad Anas bin Maalik said, when prices were high in al-Madeenah at the time of Allaah's Messenger ﷺ the people said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"'O Allaah's Messenger! Prices have become high so fix them for us'. Allaah's Messenger ﷺ replied, 'Allaah is the One who fixes prices, Who withholds, gives lavishly and provides. And I hope that when I meet Allaah, the Most High, none of you will have any claim on me for an injustice regarding blood or property.'","ref":"Sunan Abi Dawood no. 3451; at-Tirmidhee no. 1314; Ibn Maajah no. 2200; Musnad Ahmad 3/156 and others with a sound chain"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Baasit The Granter of extensive provision means the One who extends His provision to whomever He wishes of His servants."},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Qaabid means the One who restricts or withholds His provisions from whomever He wishes out of what Allaah sees as being of benefit to the servants."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And if Allah were to enlarge the provision for His slaves, they would surely rebel in the earth, but He sends down by measure as He wills.","ref":"Shooraa 42:27"},{"type":"p","text":"'Al-Qabd' is restricting provision and 'al-bast' is expanding and increasing it. Both of them are in Allaah's Hand so He is Al-Qaabid and Al-Baasit, the One who debases and raises, the One who gives and withholds, the One who gives honour and humiliates, He has no partner."},{"type":"p","text":"Extending and withholding provision is attributed to Allaah in many of the texts found in the Book and Sunnah. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Allah increases the provision for whom He wills, and straitens (it for whom He wills), and they rejoice in the life of the world, whereas the life of this world as compared with the Hereafter is but a brief passing enjoyment.","ref":"Ra'd 13:26"},{"type":"quote","text":"Truly, your Lord enlarges the provision for whom He wills and straitens (for whom He wills). Verily, He is Ever All-Knower, All-Seer of His slaves.","ref":"Israa 17:30"},{"type":"p","text":"These texts and others like them prove that extending and withholding provision is all in Allaah's Hand. He can manage it and dispose of it. He extends provision to whomever He wills regarding his wealth, health, age, knowledge and life. He also withholds provision as He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware."},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah increase us in Your blessings, mercy, grace and provision!"}],"keyPoints":["Al-Qaabid and Al-Baasit are found in the Prophetic sunnah, in the hadeeth of Anas: \"Allaah is the One who fixes prices, Who withholds, gives lavishly and provides.\"","Al-Baasit means the One who extends His provision to whomever He wishes of His servants.","Al-Qaabid means the One who restricts or withholds His provisions from whomever He wishes out of what Allaah sees as being of benefit to the servants.","'Al-Qabd' is restricting provision and 'al-bast' is expanding and increasing it; both are in Allaah's Hand alone, He has no partner.","Allaah extends provision to whomever He wills in wealth, health, age, knowledge and life, and withholds it as He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware."],"evidence":[{"text":"'Allaah is the One who fixes prices, Who withholds, gives lavishly and provides.'","ref":"Sunan Abi Dawood no. 3451; at-Tirmidhee no. 1314; Musnad Ahmad 3/156"},{"text":"And if Allah were to enlarge the provision for His slaves, they would surely rebel in the earth, but He sends down by measure as He wills.","ref":"Shooraa 42:27"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Qaabid mean?","a":"The Withholder: the One who restricts or withholds His provisions from whomever He wishes out of what Allaah sees as being of benefit to the servants."},{"q":"What does Al-Baasit mean?","a":"The Granter of extensive provision: the One who extends His provision to whomever He wishes of His servants."},{"q":"On what occasion did the Prophet ﷺ say 'Allaah is the One who fixes prices, Who withholds, gives lavishly and provides'?","a":"When prices were high in al-Madeenah and the people asked him to fix prices for them (narrated by Anas bin Maalik)."},{"q":"Which aayah explains why Allaah does not enlarge provision for all His slaves?","a":"\"And if Allah were to enlarge the provision for His slaves, they would surely rebel in the earth, but He sends down by measure as He wills.\" [Shooraa 42:27]"}]},{"chapter":63,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Mannaan","arabic":"المَنَّان","meaning":"The Ever-Bestowing"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is confirmed in the Sunnah of the noble Prophet ﷺ. Imaam Ahmad and others recorded from Anas bin Maalik that the Prophet ﷺ heard a man saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"'O Allah! I ask You by virtue of the fact that all praise is due to You; none has the right to be worshiped but You alone, and You have no partner or associate, the Bestower, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, the Possessor of majesty and honour.' He ﷺ said: 'He has asked Allah by His Greatest Name which, if He is asked thereby He gives and if He is called upon thereby He answers.'","ref":"Ibn Maajah 3858"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Mannaan is the One who gives abundantly, mighty in giving, expansive in doing good. The One who lavishly showers His servants with gifts, He bestows blessings upon them out of His Grace and Generosity. There is no one else who is Al-Mannaan The Ever-Bestowing in an absolute sense except Allaah alone. Allaah begins by giving before He is asked. He shows graciousness to His servants and there is no graciousness from them upon Him, Allaah is far above and greater than that. This is something witnessed for all of creation, those who are good and those who are bad that Allaah abundantly showers His blessings upon them, gives them plentifully with generous Hands, beautiful actions, expansive mercy, goodness and subtle mercy. He answers the requests of those who are destitute, He relieves the calamities from those who are distressed, He saves those who are troubled. He repels trials and tests after the steps have been taken and He averts them after they have befallen. His subtle mercy in this reaches beyond hopes."},{"type":"p","text":"An example of His mighty graciousness is His specific guidance for His chosen people and His servants to the path of the abode of peace, His defence of them in the best way, His protection for them from falling into sins, Him making belief beloved to them and adorning it in their hearts, Him making disbelief, corruption and disobedience hateful to them and making them from those who are guided. These are just some of the types of Allaah's grace and favours. Allaah says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And if you would count the graces of Allah, never could you be able to count them.","ref":"Nahl 16:18"},{"type":"p","text":"He also says,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And whatever of blessings and good things you have, it is from Allah.","ref":"Nahl 16:53"},{"type":"p","text":"Whoever wants to look at the foundations of benevolence then let him take a quick look in the garden of the Noble Qur'aan and let him contemplate what Allaah has enumerated in it of great blessings, noble gifts and abundant acts of kindness. Whoever knows His Lord by this mighty Name (Al-Mannaan), that He alone is the One to bestow and give and that He is the Owner of gifts and blessings then it is obligatory upon him to praise His Lord for his blessings and that he thanks Him for His grace and benevolence."},{"type":"quote","text":"He says: \"My Lord! Grant me the power and ability that I may be grateful for Your Favour which You have bestowed upon me and upon my parents, and that I may do righteous good deeds, such as please You, and make my off-spring good. Truly, I have turned to You in repentance, and truly, I am one of the Muslims (submitting to Your Will).\"","ref":"Ahqaaf 46:15"},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah to You are all praises for that, many pure, blessed praises. O Allaah to You are all praises up until You are pleased, and to You O Lord are all praises when You are pleased."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Mannaan is confirmed in the Sunnah, in the hadeeth of Anas where a man called upon Allaah as \"the Bestower\" and the Prophet ﷺ said he had asked Allaah by His Greatest Name.","Al-Mannaan is the One who gives abundantly, mighty in giving, expansive in doing good, who lavishly showers His servants with gifts out of His Grace and Generosity.","No one else is Al-Mannaan in an absolute sense except Allaah; He begins by giving before He is asked, and there is no graciousness from the servants upon Him.","An example of His mighty graciousness is His specific guidance of His chosen servants, protecting them from sins and making belief beloved to them.","Whoever knows His Lord by this Name must praise Him for His blessings and thank Him for His grace and benevolence."],"evidence":[{"text":"'...the Bestower, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, the Possessor of majesty and honour.' He ﷺ said: 'He has asked Allah by His Greatest Name...'","ref":"Ibn Maajah 3858"},{"text":"And if you would count the graces of Allah, never could you be able to count them.","ref":"Nahl 16:18"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Mannaan mean?","a":"The Ever-Bestowing: the One who gives abundantly, mighty in giving, expansive in doing good, who lavishly showers His servants with gifts out of His Grace and Generosity."},{"q":"In which hadeeth is Al-Mannaan confirmed?","a":"The hadeeth of Anas bin Maalik in which the Prophet ﷺ heard a man call on Allaah as 'the Bestower, the Originator of the heavens and the earth...' and said he had asked Allaah by His Greatest Name (Ibn Maajah 3858)."},{"q":"Give an example the author mentions of Allaah's mighty graciousness.","a":"His specific guidance for His chosen servants to the path of the abode of peace, His protection of them from sins, making belief beloved to them and making disbelief, corruption and disobedience hateful to them."},{"q":"What is obligatory upon whoever knows His Lord by the Name Al-Mannaan?","a":"To praise His Lord for His blessings and thank Him for His grace and benevolence."}]},{"chapter":64,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Hayyiy","arabic":"الحَيِيّ","meaning":"The One possessing honourable shame"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Shyness is mentioned in the Qur'aan as a verb attributed to Allaah. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Verily, Allah is not ashamed to set forth a parable even of a mosquito or so much more when it is bigger (or less when it is smaller) than it.","ref":"Baqarah 2:26"},{"type":"p","text":"The Name Al-Hayyiy The One possessing honourable shame is mentioned in two hadeeth:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Ya'alaa bin Umayyah narrated that,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man washing in a public place without a lower garment. So he mounted the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah and said: Allah is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy) and The Concealer (Sitteer), He loves modesty and concealment. So when any of you washes, he should conceal himself.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4012; An-Nisaa'ee 406"},{"type":"p","text":"2. Salmaan al-Faarisee said, that the Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Indeed your Lord is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy), The Generous (Kareem), He is shy when His servant raises his hands towards Him to return them empty.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 1488; Ibn Maajah 3865"},{"type":"p","text":"This Noble Name affirms shyness and honourable shame is an Attribute of Allaah that is befitting to His Majesty and Perfection. Allaah in all of His Attributes is not like any of His creation and none from His creation comes near to being like Allaah as Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"There is nothing like unto Him, and He is the All-Hearer, the All-Seer.","ref":"Shooraa 42:11"},{"type":"quote","text":"Do you know of any who is similar to Him? (of course none is similar or coequal or comparable to Him, and He has none as partner with Him).","ref":"Maryam 19:65"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's honourable shame is a description suited to Him and is not like the shyness of creation."},{"type":"p","text":"Speaking about this Attribute is the same as all of the Lord's Attributes. We affirm knowledge for Allaah which is not like our knowledge, He has sight which is not like our sight, He has hearing which is not like our hearing and His Will is not like our will. So the same with His honourable shame which is not like our shame or shyness. Therefore everything that Allaah affirms for Himself or His Messenger ﷺ affirms for Him, is true without any doubt. Allaah is Al-Hayyiy The One possessing honourable shame, He loves modesty and those who are modest. There are many texts that give the order to have modesty and to encourage it and promote it. It is counted as a branch of faith and the texts clarify its great benefits and blessed effects and that it is all goodness."},{"type":"p","text":"The greatest modesty and what is most obligatory upon us is to have shyness of Allaah. 'Abdullaah bin Mas'ood said, The Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Have modesty and shyness for Allaah as is His due.\" [He said:] We said: \"O Prophet of Allaah! We have shyness, and all praise is due to Allah.\" He said: \"Not that, but having modesty and shyness for Allah which He is due is to protect the head and what it contains and to protect the insides and what it includes, and to remember death and trials, and whoever intends the Hereafter, he leaves the adornments of the world. So whoever does that, then he has indeed fulfilled modesty and shyness, meaning that which Allaah is due.\"","ref":"Tirmidhee 2458; Ahmad 1/387; Saheeh at-Targheeb wat-Tarheeb 3337"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah grant us shyness of Him. Allaah grant us success to actualise fear of Him when we are alone and in public, secretly and openly."}],"keyPoints":["Shyness is mentioned in the Qur'aan as a verb attributed to Allaah: \"Verily, Allah is not ashamed to set forth a parable even of a mosquito...\" (Baqarah 2:26).","The Name Al-Hayyiy is mentioned in two hadeeth: that of Ya'alaa bin Umayyah and that of Salmaan al-Faarisee.","The Name affirms shyness and honourable shame as an Attribute of Allaah befitting His Majesty and Perfection, not like the shyness of creation.","Allaah is shy when His servant raises his hands towards Him to return them empty.","Allaah loves modesty and those who are modest; the greatest and most obligatory modesty is to have shyness of Allaah as is His due."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"Allah is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy) and The Concealer (Sitteer), He loves modesty and concealment.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4012; An-Nisaa'ee 406"},{"text":"\"Indeed your Lord is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy), The Generous (Kareem), He is shy when His servant raises his hands towards Him to return them empty.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 1488; Ibn Maajah 3865"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Hayyiy mean?","a":"The One possessing honourable shame; the Name affirms shyness and honourable shame as an Attribute of Allaah befitting His Majesty and Perfection."},{"q":"In which two hadeeth is Al-Hayyiy mentioned?","a":"The hadeeth of Ya'alaa bin Umayyah about the man washing in public, and the hadeeth of Salmaan al-Faarisee: \"Indeed your Lord is Hayyiy, Kareem, He is shy when His servant raises his hands towards Him to return them empty.\""},{"q":"Is Allaah's honourable shame like the shyness of creation?","a":"No. It is a description suited to Him, just as His knowledge, sight, hearing and Will are not like ours (\"There is nothing like unto Him\" Shooraa 42:11)."},{"q":"According to the hadeeth of Ibn Mas'ood, what is having shyness for Allaah as is His due?","a":"To protect the head and what it contains, protect the insides and what they include, remember death and trials, and whoever intends the Hereafter leaves the adornments of the world."}]},{"chapter":65,"names":[{"translit":"As-Sitteer","arabic":"السِّتِّير","meaning":"The Concealer of sins"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found in the previous hadeeth of Ya'alaa bin Umayyah who narrated that,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man washing in a public place without a lower garment. So he mounted the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah and said: Allah is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy) and The Concealer (Sitteer), He loves modesty and concealment. So when any of you washes, he should conceal himself.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4012; An-Nisaa'ee 406"},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn Abee Haatim narrated in his tafseer and Al-Bayhaqi in 'As-Sunan al-Kubraa' from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbaas who said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Two men asked him about seeking permission in the three times of privacy which Allaah ordered in the Qur'aan. So Ibn 'Abbaas said, \"Indeed Allaah is the Concealer of sins, He loves concealment. People did not have curtains on their doors nor alcoves in their houses. It was possible that a man would be caught by his servant, son or orphan in his room while he was with his wife. So Allaah ordered them to seek permission (to enter) in those times of privacy that Allaah named. Then afterwards curtains came. Allaah increased them in wealth so they put up curtains and had alcoves. People then saw that as enough instead of seeking the permission that was ordered.\"","ref":"Ibn Abee Haatim, Tafseer; Al-Bayhaqi, As-Sunan al-Kubraa (the times of privacy referred to are in Noor 24:58)"},{"type":"p","text":"Its chain was authenticated by Ibn Katheer in his Tafseer."},{"type":"p","text":"As-Sitteer means the One who conceals His servants frequently. He does not embarrass them openly. He wants His servants to conceal themselves from that which would embarrass them, disgrace them and dishonour. This is a bounty, mercy, forbearance and generosity from Allaah. A servant may fall into something of sins and disobedience, even though he is in dire need of his Lord. With this the Lord despite being perfectly free of need from any of His creation and from their obedience and worship, He honours His servant, conceals his faults and is shy from uncovering him, dishonouring him and making the punishment of him permissible."},{"type":"p","text":"He leads him to the means of concealment and grants him success to regret and repent. He pardons and forgives him. This is from His mercy and subtleness towards His creation. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And He it is Who accepts repentance from His slaves, and forgives sins, and He knows what you do.","ref":"Shooraa 42:25"},{"type":"p","text":"For this reason Allaah dislikes from His servants that they spread it and advertise when they fall into disobedience. He calls them to repent from it to Allaah between them and Him. Allaah conceals and covers him, not to let any person know. The most hated person is the one who spends the night as a sinner with Allaah concealing him then in the morning he removes the concealment that Allaah afforded him."},{"type":"p","text":"In the two Saheehs from Abee Hurayrah who said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"I heard Allah's Messenger ﷺ saying, \"All the sins of my followers will be forgiven except those who commit a sin openly or disclose their sins to the people. An example of such disclosure is that a person commits a sin at night and though Allah screens it from the public, then he comes in the morning, and says, 'O so-and-so, I did such-and-such (evil) deed yesterday,' though he spent his night screened by his Lord (none knowing about his sin) and in the morning he removes Allah's screen from himself.\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 6069; Saheeh Muslim 2990"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the meaning comes from where 'sitr' concealment of Allaah's servants is not removing their screen or looking for their private faults. In the two Saheehs, Ibn 'Umar said that the Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allaah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 2442; Saheeh Muslim 2580"},{"type":"p","text":"O Allaah! Cover our defects and faults, forgive us our sins and slips and let our deeds and lives be sealed with good deeds."}],"keyPoints":["As-Sitteer is found in the hadeeth of Ya'alaa bin Umayyah: \"Allah is ... The Concealer (Sitteer), He loves modesty and concealment.\"","As-Sitteer means the One who conceals His servants frequently and does not embarrass them openly.","Despite being free of need of His creation, Allaah conceals His sinning servant's faults, is shy from exposing him, and leads him to regret, repent and be forgiven.","Allaah dislikes that His servants advertise their sins; the most hated person is the one Allaah concealed at night who then exposes himself in the morning.","From the meaning of 'sitr' is concealing the faults of Allaah's servants and not looking for their private faults: \"Whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allaah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.\""],"evidence":[{"text":"\"Allah is The One possessing honourable shame (Hayyiy) and The Concealer (Sitteer), He loves modesty and concealment.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4012; An-Nisaa'ee 406"},{"text":"\"All the sins of my followers will be forgiven except those who commit a sin openly or disclose their sins to the people...\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 6069; Saheeh Muslim 2990"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Sitteer mean?","a":"The Concealer of sins: the One who conceals His servants frequently and does not embarrass them openly."},{"q":"Which Companion described Allaah as 'the Concealer of sins, He loves concealment' when asked about the three times of privacy?","a":"Ibn 'Abbaas (narrated by Ibn Abee Haatim and Al-Bayhaqi; its chain authenticated by Ibn Katheer)."},{"q":"Who is the most hated person regarding concealment, according to the chapter?","a":"The one who spends the night as a sinner with Allaah concealing him, then in the morning removes the concealment that Allaah afforded him."},{"q":"What reward is promised for concealing the faults of a Muslim?","a":"\"Allaah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection\" (Bukhaaree and Muslim, from Ibn 'Umar)."}]},{"chapter":66,"names":[{"translit":"As-Sayyid","arabic":"السَّيِّد","meaning":"The Lord and Master"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name As-Sayyid The Lord and Master is found in a hadeeth from the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ which is recorded by Aboo Daawood with a good chain. 'Abdullaah bin ash-Shikheer said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"I went with a deputation of Banoo 'Aamir to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we said: You are our lord (sayyid). To this he replied: The lord is Allah, the Blessed and Exalted. Then we said: And the one of us most endowed with excellence and superiority. To this he replied: Say what you have to say, or part of what you have to say, and do not let the devil make you his agents.\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4806"},{"type":"p","text":"It comes from Ibn 'Abbaas that he said regarding the saying of Allaah,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Allaah is As-Samad The Self-Sufficient Master (Whom all creatures need, He neither eats nor drinks).","ref":"Ikhlaas 112:2"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Indeed He is the Master who is perfect in His Mastership.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The intention of the Prophet ﷺ when he said 'Allaah is the Lord and Master' is that Mastership is in truth only for Allaah. He alone is the One to actualize mastership, ownership, creation, disposing of affairs with the creation displaying humbleness and humility. He is the Lord and Master who disposes and directs the affairs in this universe without an equal. He is the Lord and Master without partner to whom obedience, humility and humbleness is directed. So as He is the Lord and Master without equal who directs creation without a helper, it is He also who is the Lord and Master, the One who deserves to be worshipped without partner. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say: \"Shall I seek a lord other than Allah, while He is the Lord of all things?","ref":"An'aam 6:164"},{"type":"p","text":"Ibn 'Abbaas said about the meaning of 'I seek a Lord' that it means 'God to be worshipped, Lord and Master.'"},{"type":"p","text":"The saying 'while He is the Lord of all things' in the above aayah is explained by Ibn Jareer at-Tabaree as meaning 'He is the Lord and Master of everything besides Him. He is the disposer of affairs and the One that brings benefit.'"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the strongest proof and the clearest evidence of the falsehood of shirk polytheism and taking partners. So whoever takes a Lord and Master other than Allaah, whether it is from the people of the graves or of the living, and he believes that he can bring benefit or repel harm; or he relies upon him for a need, or asks him to remove his worry, calamity or something like that, then he has committed shirk with Allaah the Mighty. Many nations have been put to trial with this belief so much so that some of them have been given this nickname of 'grave worshippers'. They believe in them, they turn to them, they are humble before them and with this they have negated their oneness of Allaah (tawheed) and have been polluted with what opposes and breaks it. Reflect upon the previous hadeeth of how the chosen Prophet ﷺ protected and saved tawheed and blocked the paths to shirk."},{"type":"p","text":"So when they said to him 'you are our master' He said, 'As-Sayyid The Lord and Master is Allaah'. Then he said to them 'and do not let the devil make you his agents' even though they only spoke the truth. For he ﷺ is the 'sayyid' head of the children of Aadam, the best of Allaah's servants and the leader of the pious. However, when Allaah perfected his ﷺ level of worship he disliked people praising him for it. He directed and advised the Ummah to leave this in order to protect the status of singling Allaah out alone for worship (tawheed) from what could enter, corrupt and weaken it with polytheism (shirk) and what leads to it which could direct the heart to a type of connection to the creation, humbling and lowering themselves to them which is not allowed or permissible to do except to Allaah, Al-Waahid The One, Al-Qahhaar The Invincible Subduer."}],"keyPoints":["As-Sayyid is found in a hadeeth recorded by Aboo Daawood with a good chain, in which the Prophet ﷺ said: \"The lord (sayyid) is Allah, the Blessed and Exalted.\"","Ibn 'Abbaas explained As-Samad (Ikhlaas 112:2) as: \"Indeed He is the Master who is perfect in His Mastership.\"","Mastership in truth is only for Allaah: He alone actualizes mastership, ownership, creation and disposing of affairs, and He alone deserves to be worshipped without partner.","Whoever takes a Lord and Master other than Allaah, from the dead or the living, believing he can bring benefit or repel harm, or relying on him for a need, has committed shirk.","Although the Prophet ﷺ is the 'sayyid' of the children of Aadam, he disliked being praised this way in order to protect tawheed and block the paths to shirk."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"...we said: You are our lord (sayyid). To this he replied: The lord is Allah, the Blessed and Exalted...\"","ref":"Aboo Daawood 4806"},{"text":"Say: \"Shall I seek a lord other than Allah, while He is the Lord of all things?","ref":"An'aam 6:164"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does As-Sayyid mean?","a":"The Lord and Master; Mastership in truth is only for Allaah, who alone actualizes mastership, ownership, creation and disposing of affairs."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ reply when the deputation of Banoo 'Aamir said 'You are our lord (sayyid)'?","a":"\"The lord is Allah, the Blessed and Exalted\", and later: \"Say what you have to say, or part of what you have to say, and do not let the devil make you his agents.\""},{"q":"How did Ibn 'Abbaas explain As-Samad?","a":"\"Indeed He is the Master who is perfect in His Mastership.\""},{"q":"Why did the Prophet ﷺ dislike being called 'sayyid' even though it was true?","a":"To protect tawheed from what could corrupt and weaken it with shirk, and to block the paths leading the heart to humble itself to the creation."}]},{"chapter":67,"names":[{"translit":"Ar-Rafeeq","arabic":"الرَّفِيق","meaning":"The Gentle"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Name Ar-Rafeeq The Gentle, is from the beautiful Names of Allaah that is found in the authentic Sunnah. Imaam Bukhaaree recorded in his Saheeh from 'Urwah who narrated from 'Aaishah that she said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"A group of Jews asked permission to visit the Prophet (and when they were admitted) they said, \"As-Saamu 'Alaika (Death be upon you).\" I said (to them), \"But death and the curse of Allah be upon you!\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O 'Aaisha! Allah is kind and lenient and likes that one should be kind and lenient in all matters.\" I said, \"Haven't you heard what they said?\" He said, \"I said (to them), 'Wa 'Alaikum (and upon you).'\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 6927"},{"type":"p","text":"In the hadeeth is a clear mention of Allaah's Name Ar-Rafeeq The Gentle and a description that He has gentleness. Allaah being described as having gentleness is from the highest form of it, the most perfect form and that it is befitting His Majesty and perfection."},{"type":"p","text":"Gentleness means mildness and ease and deliberateness in affairs; it is granting respite. The opposite of gentleness is violence and harshness."},{"type":"p","text":"Ar-Rafeeq The Gentle is taken from gentleness which is deliberateness in affairs and doing things in stages. Allaah is gentle in His Predestination, His ordainments and His Actions. He is gentle in His commands, rulings, religion and legislation."},{"type":"p","text":"From Allaah's gentleness in His actions is that He created all of the creation stage by stage, step by step due to His wisdom and gentleness despite being able to create everything at one time through a word 'be'."},{"type":"p","text":"From Allaah's gentleness with His servants is His gentleness with them in His rulings, commands and prohibitions. He does not burden His servant with more than he can bear. He makes His commands according to ability and He takes away many commands from him due to difficulty as a concession for them out of mercy and gentleness for him."},{"type":"p","text":"He does not hold His servants responsible in one go. He grants them stages from state to state until the souls accept it and the character moulds to it ending in submission."},{"type":"p","text":"From Allaah's gentleness is His granting respite to the one who commits bad deeds and falls into sins. He does not punish him so he can turn to His Lord, repent from his sin and return to guidance."},{"type":"p","text":"From Allaah's gentleness is that all of His religion is gentleness, ease and mercy. He ordered His servants with gentleness. Gentleness gives what harshness cannot. Gentleness is not part of something of the affairs except that it beautifies it. Whoever has been prevented from gentleness has been prevented from good. Due to this every Muslim should be gentle in all his affairs and situation, away from haste, rashness, carelessness and impetuosity. Haste is from shaytaan the devil and it only results in the person being unsuccessful and losing. It is enough that gentleness is nobility and grace and that it is beloved to Ar-Rahmaan The Most Merciful. Allaah is Ar-Rafeeq The Gentle and He loves gentleness."},{"type":"p","text":"We should adorn ourselves with gentleness in all of our affairs and Allaah alone without partner is the One to grant success."}],"keyPoints":["Ar-Rafeeq is found in the authentic Sunnah, in the hadeeth of 'Aaishah in Saheeh Bukhaaree: \"Allah is kind and lenient and likes that one should be kind and lenient in all matters.\"","Gentleness means mildness, ease and deliberateness in affairs and granting respite; its opposite is violence and harshness.","Ar-Rafeeq is taken from gentleness, which is deliberateness in affairs and doing things in stages; Allaah is gentle in His Predestination, Actions, commands, rulings and legislation.","From His gentleness: He created the creation stage by stage though able to create all at once with 'be', He does not burden servants beyond their ability, legislates in stages, and grants sinners respite to repent.","Every Muslim should be gentle in all his affairs, away from haste, which is from shaytaan; Allaah is Ar-Rafeeq and He loves gentleness."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"O 'Aaisha! Allah is kind and lenient and likes that one should be kind and lenient in all matters.\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 6927"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Ar-Rafeeq mean?","a":"The Gentle; it is taken from gentleness, which is deliberateness in affairs and doing things in stages."},{"q":"On what occasion did the Prophet ﷺ say 'Allah is kind and lenient and likes that one should be kind and lenient in all matters'?","a":"When a group of Jews greeted him with 'As-Saamu 'Alaika (Death be upon you)' and 'Aaishah replied harshly; he had only said 'Wa 'Alaikum'."},{"q":"What is the opposite of gentleness according to the book?","a":"Violence and harshness."},{"q":"Give an example of Allaah's gentleness in His actions mentioned by the author.","a":"He created all of the creation stage by stage, step by step, due to His wisdom and gentleness, despite being able to create everything at one time through the word 'be'."}]},{"chapter":68,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Witr","arabic":"الوِتْر","meaning":"The Singular One"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Al-Witr is a Name that is authentically reported in the Sunnah. In the two Saheehs, Aboo Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Allaah has ninety-nine names and whoever memorizes them, understands them and acts upon them will enter Paradise and He is Witr One, He likes oneness\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree no. 6410"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Witr means the singular One who has no partner or helper. It is a Name that indicates Allaah's singularity, His uniqueness of perfect attributes and descriptions of Majesty. He does not have a partner nor equal in anything. There are many texts in the Noble Qur'aan that negate Allaah having a rival, equal, anything like Him or anything comparable to Him which is proof of that and the clearest account."},{"type":"p","text":"Belief that Allaah is Singular contains a negation of partners from every angle: in His Self, His Attributes and His Actions. It is from belief to single Him out alone for might, perfection, glory, greatness and honour."},{"type":"p","text":"In it is also a belief of His oneness in creating beings, bringing creatures into existence and creating creation. He disposes of the affairs as He Wills. He has no rival, nothing like Him, no helper and no equal."},{"type":"p","text":"This belief that He is Singular and alone should make us humble and lower us in humility. It should make us love, hope, trust and turn to Him along with other types of worship."},{"type":"p","text":"Abul 'Abbaas al-Qurtubee said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Witr The Singular One means Tawheed singling Allaah out alone for worship. It means that Allaah is One in His Self, His perfection and His actions. He loves tawheed - meaning He is singled out and believed in alone and He is separate from His creation. So it gathers the beginning of the hadeeth and its end, its apparent and hidden.\"","ref":"Al-Qurtubee, Al-Mufhim 7/18"},{"type":"p","text":"The beginning of the hadeeth is information of Allaah's Oneness and singling Him out with honour, perfection, creation, disposing of affairs and directing. The end is an encouragement for singling Allaah out alone (tawheed) by clarifying His love for the people of tawheed who practice it and preserve it."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah makes clear in the Noble Qur'aan that those who take intercessors are polytheists (mushriks). They do not possess any good or benefit for those who worship them. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"And they worship besides Allah things that hurt them not, nor profit them, and they say: \"These are our intercessors with Allah.\" Say: \"Do you inform Allah of that which He knows not in the heavens and on the earth?\" Glorified and Exalted be He above all that which they associate as partners with Him!","ref":"Yoonus 10:18"},{"type":"p","text":"So the one who takes intercessors is a polytheist (mushrik). His intercession will not be of benefit to him neither will his intercession be accepted. The one who takes the Lord alone as his deity object of worship, love, hope and fear is the one who draws close to Him alone. He seeks His pleasure and avoids His anger. He is a believer, a muwahhid who singles Allaah out alone. He will have a praiseworthy end, happiness and success in this world and the Next."},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah grant us success to actualise this and make us of the people of the blessed gardens by His grace and generosity."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Witr is authentically reported in the Sunnah: \"...and He is Witr One, He likes oneness\" (Bukhaaree and Muslim, from Aboo Hurayrah).","Al-Witr means the singular One who has no partner or helper; it indicates Allaah's singularity and His uniqueness of perfect attributes and descriptions of Majesty.","Belief that Allaah is Singular negates partners from every angle: in His Self, His Attributes and His Actions, including His oneness in creating and disposing of affairs.","Al-Qurtubee said Witr means Tawheed: Allaah is One in His Self, His perfection and His actions, and He loves tawheed and its people.","Those who take intercessors are polytheists, while the muwahhid who takes Allaah alone as his object of worship, love, hope and fear will have happiness and success in this world and the Next."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"Allaah has ninety-nine names and whoever memorizes them, understands them and acts upon them will enter Paradise and He is Witr One, He likes oneness\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree no. 6410"},{"text":"And they worship besides Allah things that hurt them not, nor profit them, and they say: \"These are our intercessors with Allah.\"","ref":"Yoonus 10:18"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Witr mean?","a":"The Singular One: the singular One who has no partner or helper; the Name indicates Allaah's singularity and His uniqueness of perfect attributes and descriptions of Majesty."},{"q":"In which hadeeth is Al-Witr mentioned?","a":"The hadeeth of Aboo Hurayrah in the two Saheehs: \"Allaah has ninety-nine names... and He is Witr One, He likes oneness.\""},{"q":"How did Abul 'Abbaas al-Qurtubee explain Witr?","a":"It means Tawheed: Allaah is One in His Self, His perfection and His actions, and He loves tawheed."},{"q":"What effect should belief that Allaah is Singular have on us?","a":"It should make us humble and lower us in humility, and make us love, hope, trust and turn to Him along with other types of worship."}]},{"chapter":69,"names":[{"translit":"Al-Mu'tee","arabic":"المُعْطِي","meaning":"The Giver"},{"translit":"Al-Jawaad","arabic":"الجَوَاد","meaning":"The Most Generous"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Mu'tee The Giver, is authentically reported in Saheeh Bukhaaree from a hadeeth by Mu'aawiyah who said that the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"If Allah wants to do good for somebody, he makes him comprehend the Religion (i.e. Islam), and Allah is the Giver and I am Al-Qaasim (i.e. the distributor), and this (Muslim) nation will remain victorious over their opponents, till Allaah's Order comes and they will still be victorious\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 3116"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Name Al-Jawaad The Most Generous is mentioned in a Qudsee Hadeeth by Aboo Dharr who said that the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Allaah says, O My servants, all of you are astray except those that I have guided… That is because I am the Most Generous, The Glorious, I do what I want. I give by My speech and I punish by My speech, whenever I want something I only say: \"Be\" and it is.\"","ref":"Tirmidhee 2495; Ibn Maajah 4257"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Mu'tee The Giver means the One alone who gives in reality. Nothing can prevent Him giving and nothing can give when He prevents. His giving is by speech and His preventing is by speech. If He wishes something He only has to say 'Be' and it is. Everything that a servant has of blessings is from His grace and giving. His giving extends over all His servants – believers and disbelievers, righteous and disobedient. This is in this life, as for the Day of Resurrection He will specifically give to His allies and believers. Allaah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Say (O Muhammad): \"Who has forbidden the adoration with clothes given by Allah, which He has produced for his slaves, and At-Taiyibat [all kinds of Halal (lawful) things] of food?\" Say: \"They are, in the life of this world, for those who believe, (and) exclusively for them (believers) on the Day of Resurrection (the disbelievers will not share them).\" Thus We explain the Ayat (Islamic laws) in detail for people who have knowledge.","ref":"A'raaf 7:32"},{"type":"p","text":"Al-Jawaad The Most Generous means plentiful giving. The One whose generosity covers all created beings. He fills them from His grace, generosity and varied blessings. Nothing created is free from His good treatment for the blinking of an eye."},{"type":"p","text":"Ibnul Qayyim said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Allaah loves for His servants to have hope in Him, to have expectations and to ask Him of His grace. This is because He is the King, the Truth and the Most Generous. He is more generous than what He was asked for and is more expansive than the one who gives. There is nothing more beloved to The Generous than His servants having hope and expectation in Him and for them asking Him. In a hadeeth it states that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, he who does not ask Allah, He becomes angry with him.\"\"","ref":"Ibnul Qayyim, Madaarij as-Saalikeen 1/211-212 (the hadeeth: Tirmidhee 3373; Bukhaaree in Al-Adab al-Mufrad 658)"},{"type":"p","text":"We hope The Most Generous Al-Jawaad Al-Kareem grants us all the means that lead to gaining His generosity and bounty and that He protects us from the means that lead to His anger, punishment and just revenge. Generosity is His generosity and giving is His giving. The command is His before and after. He has no partner."}],"keyPoints":["Al-Mu'tee is authentically reported in Saheeh Bukhaaree in the hadeeth of Mu'aawiyah: \"Allah is the Giver and I am Al-Qaasim (the distributor).\"","Al-Jawaad is mentioned in the Qudsee hadeeth of Aboo Dharr: \"That is because I am the Most Generous, The Glorious, I do what I want.\"","Al-Mu'tee means the One alone who gives in reality; nothing can prevent His giving and nothing can give when He prevents, and His giving and preventing are by speech.","His giving in this life extends over all His servants, believers and disbelievers, but on the Day of Resurrection He will specifically give to His allies and believers.","Al-Jawaad means plentiful giving, the One whose generosity covers all created beings; nothing created is free from His good treatment for the blinking of an eye.","Ibnul Qayyim said nothing is more beloved to The Generous than His servants having hope in Him and asking Him; whoever does not ask Allaah, He becomes angry with him."],"evidence":[{"text":"\"...and Allah is the Giver and I am Al-Qaasim (i.e. the distributor)...\"","ref":"Saheeh Bukhaaree 3116"},{"text":"\"...That is because I am the Most Generous, The Glorious, I do what I want. I give by My speech and I punish by My speech...\"","ref":"Tirmidhee 2495; Ibn Maajah 4257"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Al-Mu'tee mean?","a":"The Giver: the One alone who gives in reality; nothing can prevent Him giving and nothing can give when He prevents."},{"q":"What does Al-Jawaad mean?","a":"The Most Generous: plentiful giving, the One whose generosity covers all created beings; nothing created is free from His good treatment for the blinking of an eye."},{"q":"In which hadeeth is Al-Mu'tee reported?","a":"The hadeeth of Mu'aawiyah in Saheeh Bukhaaree: \"If Allah wants to do good for somebody, he makes him comprehend the Religion... and Allah is the Giver and I am Al-Qaasim.\""},{"q":"How does Allaah's giving differ between this life and the Day of Resurrection?","a":"In this life His giving extends over believers and disbelievers, righteous and disobedient; on the Day of Resurrection He will specifically give to His allies and believers (A'raaf 7:32)."},{"q":"According to Ibnul Qayyim, what is most beloved to The Generous?","a":"His servants having hope and expectation in Him and asking Him."}]},{"chapter":70,"names":[{"translit":"Dhul Jalaali wal Ikraam","arabic":"ذُو الجَلَالِ وَالإِكْرَام","meaning":"Possessing Majesty and Honour"}],"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This Name is found in Soorat Ar-Rahmaan in His saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"Blessed be the Name of your Lord (Allah), the Owner of Majesty and Honour","ref":"Rahmaan 55:78"},{"type":"p","text":"The virtues of making du'aa with this Name comes in the Prophetic Sunnah. In the Musnad it is reported from Rabee'ah bin 'Aamir that he said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Stick to Dhul jalaali wal ikraam.'\"","ref":"Musnad Ahmad 4/177; Silsilah as-Saheehah 1536"},{"type":"p","text":"This means say it, stick to it and say it often in speech and in your supplications."},{"type":"p","text":"In Saheeh Muslim Thawbaan said the Messenger of Allaah ﷺ used to say I seek Allaah's forgiveness three times after finishing his prayers and he would say,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"O Allah! You are peace, and peace comes from You; Blessed are You, O Possessor of Glory and Honour.\"","ref":"Saheeh Muslim 591"},{"type":"p","text":"Dhul Jalaali wal Ikraam is among the compound Names and is counted by a group of scholars as being from Allaah's beautiful Names."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykhul Islaam ibn Taymiyyah said,"},{"type":"quote","text":"\"Likewise, Allaah's Names that come together such as:\nأرحم الراحمين The Most Merciful of those who have mercy\nخير الغافرين The Best of those who forgive\nرب العالمين Lord of the worlds\nمالك يوم الدين Owner of the Day of Resurrection\nأحسن الخالقين Best of creators\nجامع الناس ليوم لا ريب فيه Gatherer of the people on the day there is no doubt\nمقلب القلوب Turner of the hearts\nand so on from what is authentically reported from the Book and Sunnah have been established that a person can make du'aa with them by the consensus of the Muslims.\"","ref":"Majmoo' al-Fataawaa of Ibn Taymiyyah 22/485"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah's Names Dhul Jalaali wal Ikraam gathers together two descriptions: dhul Jalaali possessing Majesty which includes exaltation; and ikraam honour which includes praise and love."},{"type":"p","text":"Shaykhul Islaam Ibn Taymiyyah said, \"As Allaah is deserving of Majesty and Honour, He must be described in Himself as such. As when it is said, 'al Ilaah' 'The God who deserves to be worshipped'. He is deserving in Himself of that, meaning to be exalted and honoured.\""},{"type":"p","text":"He goes on to say, \"Servants cannot attain the praise He deserves and He is as He has praised Himself. Likewise He deserves to be exalted and honoured and He exalts Himself and honours Himself. The servants cannot attain this exaltation and honouring of Him. Majesty is from the category of exaltation and honouring is from the category of love and praise. This is like His saying,"},{"type":"quote","text":"His is the dominion, and to Him belong all the praises and thanks","ref":"Taghaabun 64:1"},{"type":"p","text":"He has might and the Kingdom, He has honour and praise.\""},{"type":"p","text":"All praises are for Allaah, many pure and blessed praises for what He has facilitated and given. I cannot attain the praise He deserves."},{"type":"quote","text":"My Lord! Inspire and bestow upon me the power and ability that I may be grateful for Your Favours which You have bestowed on me and on my parents, and that I may do righteous good deeds that will please You, and admit me by Your Mercy among Your righteous slaves.","ref":"Naml 27:19"},{"type":"p","text":"Allaah praise, honour and protect our Prophet Muhammad, his family and companions."},{"type":"p","text":"End of the Shaykh's Work"}],"keyPoints":["This Name is found in Soorat Ar-Rahmaan: \"Blessed be the Name of your Lord (Allah), the Owner of Majesty and Honour\" (55:78).","The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Stick to Dhul jalaali wal ikraam', meaning say it often in speech and supplications; he also said it after the prayer: \"Blessed are You, O Possessor of Glory and Honour.\"","Dhul Jalaali wal Ikraam is among the compound Names, counted by a group of scholars as being from Allaah's beautiful Names, and Ibn Taymiyyah said making du'aa with such authentically reported compound Names is by consensus.","The Name gathers two descriptions: dhul Jalaali, possessing Majesty, which includes exaltation; and ikraam, honour, which includes praise and love.","Allaah deserves in Himself to be exalted and honoured, and the servants cannot attain the exaltation, honouring and praise He deserves."],"evidence":[{"text":"Blessed be the Name of your Lord (Allah), the Owner of Majesty and Honour","ref":"Rahmaan 55:78"},{"text":"\"Stick to Dhul jalaali wal ikraam.\"","ref":"Musnad Ahmad 4/177; Silsilah as-Saheehah 1536"}],"recall":[{"q":"What does Dhul Jalaali wal Ikraam mean?","a":"Possessing Majesty and Honour: dhul Jalaali is possessing Majesty, which includes exaltation; ikraam is honour, which includes praise and love."},{"q":"Where in the Qur'aan is this Name found?","a":"In Soorat Ar-Rahmaan: \"Blessed be the Name of your Lord (Allah), the Owner of Majesty and Honour\" [Rahmaan 55:78]."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say about this Name according to Rabee'ah bin 'Aamir, and what does it mean?","a":"'Stick to Dhul jalaali wal ikraam' — meaning say it, stick to it and say it often in speech and in supplications."},{"q":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say after finishing his prayers, according to Thawbaan?","a":"He sought Allaah's forgiveness three times and said: \"O Allah! You are peace, and peace comes from You; Blessed are You, O Possessor of Glory and Honour.\" (Saheeh Muslim 591)"}]}]};
